('JHS','LS1-EN',1,1,1,'Lena was always afraid of the dark. From childhood, she felt shadows moving and whispering to her. But tonight was different. She wanted to be brave. Taking a deep breath, she switched off the lights and stood in the center of her room. Her heartbeat as she attempted to get rid of the fear building up on her. For a while, there was nothing. No sound. And then, after her eyes were adjusted, Lena saw the thin light of moonlight coming from the window. The shadows no longer frightened her. She laughed at herself thinking that possibly the dark didn''t have to be as dreadful as she''d imagined.','What was Lena afraid of?','Heights','Animals','The dark','The cold','C','The passage repeatedly states Lena''s fear of the dark since childhood',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-EN',1,1,2,'Lena was always afraid of the dark. From childhood, she felt shadows moving and whispering to her. But tonight was different. She wanted to be brave. Taking a deep breath, she switched off the lights and stood in the center of her room. Her heartbeat as she attempted to get rid of the fear building up on her. For a while, there was nothing. No sound. And then, after her eyes were adjusted, Lena saw the thin light of moonlight coming from the window. The shadows no longer frightened her. She laughed at herself thinking that possibly the dark didn''t have to be as dreadful as she''d imagined.','What did Lena do to confront her fear?','Went outside','Switched on more lights','Called a friend','Switched off the lights','D','Lena switched off the lights to face her fear of darkness',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-EN',1,1,3,'Lena was always afraid of the dark. From childhood, she felt shadows moving and whispering to her. But tonight was different. She wanted to be brave. Taking a deep breath, she switched off the lights and stood in the center of her room. Her heartbeat as she attempted to get rid of the fear building up on her. For a while, there was nothing. No sound. And then, after her eyes were adjusted, Lena saw the thin light of moonlight coming from the window. The shadows no longer frightened her. She laughed at herself thinking that possibly the dark didn''t have to be as dreadful as she''d imagined.','Where was Lena standing when she turned off the lights?','Kitchen','Outside','Center of her room','By the window','C','The text clearly states Lena stood in the center of her room.',NULL,0,1),
