('JHS','LS1-EN',1,1,21,'How to Stay Organized at Work\n\nStaying organized at work is essential for productivity and success. First, prioritize tasks by creating a to-do list. This simple yet effective method helps you focus on what needs to be done. Next, break large tasks into smaller, more manageable steps. This makes the job less overwhelming and allows you to track your progress. Additionally, maintaining a tidy workspace helps reduce distractions and improve focus. Lastly, set regular intervals to check your progress and adjust your priorities if necessary. By implementing these strategies, you can stay organized, reduce stress, and increase efficiency at work.','What is the main goal of staying organized at work?','To impress your boss','To increase stress','To boost productivity and success','To avoid talking to coworkers','C','The first sentence of the passage clearly states this goal.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-EN',1,1,22,'How to Stay Organized at Work\n\nStaying organized at work is essential for productivity and success. First, prioritize tasks by creating a to-do list. This simple yet effective method helps you focus on what needs to be done. Next, break large tasks into smaller, more manageable steps. This makes the job less overwhelming and allows you to track your progress. Additionally, maintaining a tidy workspace helps reduce distractions and improve focus. Lastly, set regular intervals to check your progress and adjust your priorities if necessary. By implementing these strategies, you can stay organized, reduce stress, and increase efficiency at work.','What tool is suggested to prioritize tasks?','Calendar','Stopwatch','To-do list','Alarm','C','A to-do list is recommended to organize and prioritize tasks.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-EN',1,1,23,'How to Stay Organized at Work\n\nStaying organized at work is essential for productivity and success. First, prioritize tasks by creating a to-do list. This simple yet effective method helps you focus on what needs to be done. Next, break large tasks into smaller, more manageable steps. This makes the job less overwhelming and allows you to track your progress. Additionally, maintaining a tidy workspace helps reduce distractions and improve focus. Lastly, set regular intervals to check your progress and adjust your priorities if necessary. By implementing these strategies, you can stay organized, reduce stress, and increase efficiency at work.','How can big tasks be made easier?','Ignoring them','Delegating everything','Breaking them into smaller steps','Postponing them','C','The passage mentions this helps reduce overwhelm.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-EN',1,1,24,'How to Stay Organized at Work\n\nStaying organized at work is essential for productivity and success. First, prioritize tasks by creating a to-do list. This simple yet effective method helps you focus on what needs to be done. Next, break large tasks into smaller, more manageable steps. This makes the job less overwhelming and allows you to track your progress. Additionally, maintaining a tidy workspace helps reduce distractions and improve focus. Lastly, set regular intervals to check your progress and adjust your priorities if necessary. By implementing these strategies, you can stay organized, reduce stress, and increase efficiency at work.','What should be kept tidy to reduce distractions?','The inbox','The kitchen','The workspace','The hallway','C','A tidy workspace is said to help with focus and reducing distractions.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-EN',1,1,25,'How to Stay Organized at Work\n\nStaying organized at work is essential for productivity and success. First, prioritize tasks by creating a to-do list. This simple yet effective method helps you focus on what needs to be done. Next, break large tasks into smaller, more manageable steps. This makes the job less overwhelming and allows you to track your progress. Additionally, maintaining a tidy workspace helps reduce distractions and improve focus. Lastly, set regular intervals to check your progress and adjust your priorities if necessary. By implementing these strategies, you can stay organized, reduce stress, and increase efficiency at work.','What should you do regularly with your priorities?','Ignore them','Hide them','Adjust them','Erase them','C','The text advises checking progress and adjusting priorities when needed to stay on track with your goals.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-EN',1,2,26,'The Importance of Renewable Energy Sources\n\nRenewable energy sources, such as solar, wind, and hydropower, are crucial for the future of our planet. As global demand for energy increases, traditional fossil fuels like coal, oil, and natural gas are becoming less sustainable due to their environmental impact. The use of renewable energy sources presents a solution to this issue, offering cleaner, more sustainable alternatives. Solar power, one of the most popular renewable energy sources, harnesses the energy of the sun to generate electricity. It produces no harmful emissions and can be used in a variety of settings, from residential homes to large-scale solar farms. Wind energy, similarly, uses the power of wind to drive turbines that produce electricity, while hydropower relies on water flow to generate energy. Transitioning to renewable energy has numerous benefits, including reducing greenhouse gas emissions, mitigating climate change, and creating jobs in the green energy sector. While the initial cost of renewable energy infrastructure can be high, the long-term environmental and economic benefits make it a viable option for the future. In conclusion, renewable energy sources are essential for sustainable growth and environmental preservation. By investing in and expanding the use of these sources, we can help ensure a cleaner, healthier future for generations to come.','In the essay "The Importance of Renewable Energy Resources," which of the following terms best represents a technical concept related to the generation of clean energy?','Climate change','Solar photovoltaic cells','Greenhouse gases','Fossil fuels','B','This question assesses the ability to identify a discipline-specific term ("solar photovoltaic cells") that is directly related to renewable energy in an expository text.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-EN',1,2,27,'The Importance of Renewable Energy Sources\n\nRenewable energy sources, such as solar, wind, and hydropower, are crucial for the future of our planet. As global demand for energy increases, traditional fossil fuels like coal, oil, and natural gas are becoming less sustainable due to their environmental impact. The use of renewable energy sources presents a solution to this issue, offering cleaner, more sustainable alternatives. Solar power, one of the most popular renewable energy sources, harnesses the energy of the sun to generate electricity. It produces no harmful emissions and can be used in a variety of settings, from residential homes to large-scale solar farms. Wind energy, similarly, uses the power of wind to drive turbines that produce electricity, while hydropower relies on water flow to generate energy. Transitioning to renewable energy has numerous benefits, including reducing greenhouse gas emissions, mitigating climate change, and creating jobs in the green energy sector. While the initial cost of renewable energy infrastructure can be high, the long-term environmental and economic benefits make it a viable option for the future. In conclusion, renewable energy sources are essential for sustainable growth and environmental preservation. By investing in and expanding the use of these sources, we can help ensure a cleaner, healthier future for generations to come.','Based on the essay, the term "sustainability" is often used. What is the correct meaning and context of "sustainability" in this essay?','The ability to continue producing energy from fossil fuels without environmental impact.','The long-term ability of renewable energy sources to meet energy demands without harming the environment.','The process of developing new, non-renewable energy resources for the future.','The short-term production of renewable energy sources to meet current needs only.','B','This question tests the understanding of discipline-specific terminology like "sustainability" in the context of renewable energy in an expository essay.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-EN',1,2,28,'Moderator: Welcome to today''s debate! The topic is whether school uniforms should be mandatory in schools. Let’s begin with the opening statements. Sarah, you have the floor. Sarah (Pro-School Uniforms): Thank you. I believe that school uniforms should be mandatory because they promote equality among students. When everyone wears the same outfit, there is less pressure to compete based on clothing, which can reduce bullying and distractions. Uniforms also help students focus more on their studies instead of worrying about fashion. Moderator: Thank you, Sarah. Alex, your opening statement? Alex (Against School Uniforms): I disagree with Sarah. While uniforms might reduce some pressure, they also take away students'' freedom to express themselves. Clothing is a way for students to show their personality and creativity. By forcing everyone to wear the same thing, schools are limiting individual expression. Plus, uniforms can be uncomfortable and expensive for some families. Moderator: Thank you, Alex. Sarah, would you like to respond? Sarah (Pro-School Uniforms): Yes, I understand that some students may feel that uniforms limit their freedom, but the point of school is to learn, not to focus on what you''re wearing. Uniforms can actually make mornings easier because students don''t have to decide what to wear. Additionally, schools should be places where everyone is treated equally, regardless of how much money their families have. Moderator: Alex, your response? Alex (Against School Uniforms): While I agree that equality is important, forcing students to wear uniforms doesn''t really solve the issue. Instead of focusing on clothes, we should teach students to appreciate differences and respect others'' choices. Also, if families can''t afford uniforms, that creates an extra burden on them. Schools should focus on making education better, not controlling what students wear. Moderator: Thank you both for your arguments. We’ll now open the floor to questions.','What is one reason Sarah supports school uniforms?','They allow students to express their individuality','They are more fashionable than casual clothes','They help reduce bullying and distractions','They encourage students to break school rules','C','Sarah argues that uniforms promote equality and reduce bullying and distractions by removing pressure to dress in certain ways.',NULL,0,1),
