('JHS','LS1-EN',2,1,25,'How to Stay Organized at Work\n\nStaying organized at work is essential for productivity and success. First, prioritize tasks by creating a to-do list. This simple yet effective method helps you focus on what needs to be done. Next, break large tasks into smaller, more manageable steps. This makes the job less overwhelming and allows you to track your progress. Additionally, maintaining a tidy workspace helps reduce distractions and improve focus. Lastly, set regular intervals to check your progress and adjust your priorities if necessary. By implementing these strategies, you can stay organized, reduce stress, and increase efficiency at work.','Which of these strategies contributes directly to stress reduction?','Avoiding communication','Staying organized','Taking longer breaks','Skipping tasks','B','The passage links organization to lower stress and better productivity.',NULL,0,1);
