('JHS','LS1-EN',3,1,21,'How to Stay Organized at Work\n\nStaying organized at work is essential for productivity and success. First, prioritize tasks by creating a to-do list. This simple yet effective method helps you focus on what needs to be done. Next, break large tasks into smaller, more manageable steps. This makes the job less overwhelming and allows you to track your progress. Additionally, maintaining a tidy workspace helps reduce distractions and improve focus. Lastly, set regular intervals to check your progress and adjust your priorities if necessary. By implementing these strategies, you can stay organized, reduce stress, and increase efficiency at work.','What is the underlying reason why breaking tasks into steps improves productivity?','It makes work disappear','It delays action','It prevents feeling overwhelmed and builds momentum','It reduces the number of tasks','C','Smaller steps make work easier to start and finish, which helps people stay on track.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-EN',3,1,22,'How to Stay Organized at Work\n\nStaying organized at work is essential for productivity and success. First, prioritize tasks by creating a to-do list. This simple yet effective method helps you focus on what needs to be done. Next, break large tasks into smaller, more manageable steps. This makes the job less overwhelming and allows you to track your progress. Additionally, maintaining a tidy workspace helps reduce distractions and improve focus. Lastly, set regular intervals to check your progress and adjust your priorities if necessary. By implementing these strategies, you can stay organized, reduce stress, and increase efficiency at work.','How could adjusting priorities improve overall work performance?','It helps avoid tasks','It keeps your work aligned with changing demands','It allows you to multitask more','It creates less communication','B','Changing plans or goals is part of staying flexible and efficient at work.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-EN',3,1,23,'How to Stay Organized at Work\n\nStaying organized at work is essential for productivity and success. First, prioritize tasks by creating a to-do list. This simple yet effective method helps you focus on what needs to be done. Next, break large tasks into smaller, more manageable steps. This makes the job less overwhelming and allows you to track your progress. Additionally, maintaining a tidy workspace helps reduce distractions and improve focus. Lastly, set regular intervals to check your progress and adjust your priorities if necessary. By implementing these strategies, you can stay organized, reduce stress, and increase efficiency at work.','What might happen if someone doesn’t follow any of the suggested strategies?','They might become more relaxed','Their performance may improve','They may become disorganized and stressed','They’ll finish tasks faster','C','Without good strategies, tasks pile up and cause confusion and stress.',NULL,0,1),
