to questions.','Based on the debate, which of the following is the most accurate supporting evidence for Sarah''s claim that school uniforms promote equality?','School uniforms are a form of creativity and self-expression for students.','Uniforms can make mornings easier by eliminating the need to decide what to wear.','School uniforms help students express their individuality through unique designs.','Some families find school uniforms to be a financial burden.','B','Sarah''s argument centers around the idea that school uniforms promote equality by reducing distractions related to clothing and helping students focus on their studies. In her response, she also mentions that uniforms make mornings easier because students don''t have to spend time deciding what to wear, which supports her point about the benefits of uniformity. This evidence is directly tied to her claim about how uniforms help students focus on learning rather than fashion.',NULL,0,0),
