nakatingin kay James, nanginginig) Hindi ko na kayang magpatuloy… (lumakad palayo, natutuklasan ang kanyang pagkabaliw sa loob ng kanyang isipan) James: (tinutok ang mga kamay sa kanyang ulo, nawawala ang pag-asa) Betty… hindi ko kayang mawalan ka! Hindi ko kayang tanggapin ito! (huwag mong gawing ganito!) (Si Betty ay hindi na sumagot, tanging ang kanyang mga mata ay tila wala nang buhay. Ang mga huling sandali ay ang tuluyang pagkabaliw na nagdadala sa kanya sa mas madilim na kalagayan.) Wakas. James: (tinutok ang mga kamay sa kanyang ulo, nawawala ang pag-asa) Betty… hindi ko kayang mawalan ka! Hindi ko kayang tanggapin ito! (huwag mong gawing ganito!)\n\n(Si Betty ay hindi na sumagot, tanging ang kanyang mga mata ay tila wala nang buhay. Ang mga huling sandali ay ang tuluyang pagkabaliw na nagdadala sa kanya sa mas madilim na kalagayan.)\n\nWakas.','Anong panlingguwistikong elemento ang gumamit sa dula upang maipakita ang tensyon at emosyon ng mga tauhan?','Di-alam na mga wika','Simbolismo at metapora','Paggamit ng makapangyarihang pahayag at padamdam','Pares ng tugmaang salita','C','Gumamit ang dula ng mga padamdam at matitinding emosyonal na linya tulad ng “Hindi ko kayang magtiwala pa!” at “Hindi ko na kayang magpatuloy!” na nagpapakita ng damdamin ng mga tauhan, na isang panlingguwistikong estratehiya sa kontemporaneong dula.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,9,'Dula: "Ang Pagluha ng Puso" ni: Loreto B. Demetillo, Jr. Tauhan: James – Kasintahan ni Betty, naguguluhan at galit Betty – Kasintahan ni James, naguguluhan at emosyonal\n\nTagpo: Isang maliit na sala sa bahay ni Betty. Si James ay dumating ng maaga upang sorpresahin si Betty, ngunit nakatagpo siya ng isang nakakagulat na eksena. Si Betty ay may kasama ibang lalaki sa sala.\n\n(Si James ay papasok sa pinto, nakita niyang si Betty ay nakaupo sa sofa kasama si Marco, isang matandang kaibigan ni Betty.)\n\nJames: (naguguluhan at galit) Betty… ano ito? Sino siya?!\n\nBetty: (nagulat, agad tumayo at nagsimula magpaliwanag) James, hindi ito ganun… Si Marco lang siya, kaibigan ko lang siya!\n\nJames: (tinuturo si Marco, galit na galit) Kaibigan?! Bakit siya nandito?! Bakit ko siya lang ngayon nakita?! Ano ito, Betty?! Ano ang nangyayari sa atin?!\n\nBetty: (nag-aalalang pilit na ipaliwanag) James, pakiusap, makinig ka! Hindi ko kayang itago ang nararamdaman ko. Si Marco… siya ang tumulong sa akin nung ako’y naguguluhan. Wala sa plano ko na maging ganito, James.\n\nJames: (naglalakad palapit, nanginginig ang kamay) Hindi ko kayang intindihin ito, Betty! Kung mahal mo ako, bakit mo ako tinatago? Bakit siya nandiyan? Kung gusto mo siya, sabihin mo na lang!\n\nBetty: (nagluluhang nakatayo, nanginginig) Hindi ko gusto siya, James! Pero… hindi ko na kayang magpanggap! Hindi ko na kayang itago! (sumabog ang luha)\n\nJames: (nahulog ang kanyang mga mata, nasasaktan) Betty… hindi ko kayang makita kang ganito. Hindi ko kayang magtiwala pa! Kung ganito ka, paano pa tayo?\n\nBetty: (nanghihina, nanginginig) Hindi ko na alam kung anong nangyayari sa akin, James… Hindi ko na kayang labanan ang lahat ng ito. Lahat ng sakit, lahat ng kalituhan. Hindi ko na kayang magpatuloy ng ganito!\n\n(Si Betty ay humakbang palayo kay James, tila nawawala na ang mga saloobin.)\n\nJames: (nagmamadaling lumapit) Betty, pakiusap… wag mong gawin ito. Pakiusap, mahal kita!\n\nBetty: (nakatingin kay James, nanginginig) Hindi ko na kayang magpatuloy… (lumakad palayo, natutuklasan ang kanyang pagkabaliw sa loob ng kanyang isipan) James: (tinutok ang mga kamay sa kanyang ulo, nawawala ang pag-asa) Betty… hindi ko kayang mawalan ka! Hindi ko kayang tanggapin ito! (huwag mong gawing ganito!) (Si Betty ay hindi na sumagot, tanging ang kanyang mga mata ay tila wala nang buhay. Ang mga huling sandali ay ang tuluyang pagkabaliw na nagdadala sa kanya sa mas madilim na kalagayan.) Wakas. James: (tinutok ang mga kamay sa kanyang ulo, nawawala ang pag-asa) Betty… hindi ko kayang mawalan ka! Hindi ko kayang tanggapin ito! (huwag mong gawing ganito!)\n\n(Si Betty ay hindi na sumagot, tanging ang kanyang mga mata ay tila wala nang buhay. Ang mga huling sandali ay ang tuluyang pagkabaliw na nagdadala sa kanya sa mas madilim na kalagayan.)\n\nWakas.','Paano naiiba ang dulang ito sa mga dula noong Panahon ng Katutubo sa aspetong kultural at tematikal?','Dahil Mas nakatuon ito sa pag-aalsa laban sa kolonyalismo sa bansa.','Mas makabayan ang tema nito at nakasentro sa panlipunang Kalayaan.','Tinatampok nito ang mas personal, emosyonal, at relasyunal na suliranin.','Nakatuon ito sa pagsasagawa ng ritwal at paniniwalang espiritwal.','C','. Ang mga dula noong Panahon ng Katutubo ay kadalasang panrelihiyon, panritwal, o pampamayanan ang tema. Samantalang ang kontemporaneong dula tulad nito ay mas nakasentro sa personal na emosyon, relasyon, at mental health— isang repleksyon ng modernong kultural na sensibilidad.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,10,'Ang early pregnancy o maagang pagbubuntis ay isang kondisyon kung saan ang isang babae, karaniwan ay isang kabataan, ay nagdadalang-tao sa edad na hindi pa ganap na handa sa pisikal at emosyonal na aspeto. Ito ay madalas na dulot ng kakulangan ng tamang kaalaman ukol sa kalusugan ng reproduktibo at hindi paggamit ng kontraseptibo. Ang mga kabataang nagiging buntis ng maaga ay kadalasang nahaharap sa mga komplikasyon sa kalusugan tulad ng preeclampsia, anemia, at premature birth. Bukod dito, ang kanilang buhay ay maaari ring magkaroon ng malaking epekto, tulad ng pagkakagambala sa edukasyon at paghahanapbuhay. Mahalaga ang papel ng mga magulang, guro, at pamahalaan upang magbigay ng tamang edukasyon at gabay sa mga kabataan ukol sa sekswalidad at responsibilidad sa pagiging magulang. Sa pamamagitan ng mga programang pang-edukasyon tulad ng Comprehensive Sexuality Education at pagpapalaganap ng kaalaman, maaaring mapigilan ang patuloy na pagtaas ng bilang ng ang kanilang buhay ay maaari ring magkaroon ng malaking epekto, tulad ng pagkakagambala sa edukasyon at paghahanapbuhay. Mahalaga ang papel ng mga magulang, guro, at pamahalaan upang magbigay ng tamang edukasyon at gabay sa mga kabataan ukol sa sekswalidad at responsibilidad sa pagiging magulang. Sa pamamagitan ng mga programang pang-edukasyon tulad ng Comprehensive Sexuality Education at pagpapalaganap ng kaalaman, maaaring mapigilan ang patuloy na pagtaas ng bilang ng mga batang nagiging ina.','Paano nakaambag ang paggamit ng mga espesipikong halimbawa (tulad ng “preeclampsia, anemia, at premature birth”) sa pagiging epektibo ng teksto?','Nagbigay ito ng emosyonal na lalim para makaantig sa mambabasa','Ipinakita nito ang konkretong epekto ng isyu para maging mas malinaw','Pinalawak nito ang pananaw ng may-akda sa moral na aspeto ng isyu','Ipinakita nito ang relihiyosong paninindigan ng Lipunan para sa mamamayan.','B','Sa isang tekstong ekspositori, mahalagang may konkretong halimbawa upang mas maging malinaw at kapanipaniwala ang impormasyon. Ang mga medikal na komplikasyon ay konkretong ebidensyang nagpapalakas sa layunin ng teksto na magbigay-impormasyon.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,11,'Ang early pregnancy o maagang pagbubuntis ay isang kondisyon kung saan ang isang babae, karaniwan ay isang kabataan, ay nagdadalang-tao sa edad na hindi pa ganap na handa sa pisikal at emosyonal na aspeto. Ito ay madalas na dulot ng kakulangan ng tamang kaalaman ukol sa kalusugan ng reproduktibo at hindi paggamit ng kontraseptibo. Ang mga kabataang nagiging buntis ng maaga ay kadalasang nahaharap sa mga komplikasyon sa kalusugan tulad ng preeclampsia, anemia, at premature birth. Bukod dito, ang kanilang buhay ay maaari ring magkaroon ng malaking epekto, tulad ng pagkakagambala sa edukasyon at paghahanapbuhay. Mahalaga ang papel ng mga magulang, guro, at pamahalaan upang magbigay ng tamang edukasyon at gabay sa mga kabataan ukol sa sekswalidad at responsibilidad sa pagiging magulang. Sa pamamagitan ng mga programang pang-edukasyon tulad ng Comprehensive Sexuality Education at pagpapalaganap ng kaalaman, maaaring mapigilan ang patuloy na pagtaas ng bilang ng ang kanilang buhay ay maaari ring magkaroon ng malaking epekto, tulad ng pagkakagambala sa edukasyon at paghahanapbuhay. Mahalaga ang papel ng mga magulang, guro, at pamahalaan upang magbigay ng tamang edukasyon at gabay sa mga kabataan ukol sa sekswalidad at responsibilidad sa pagiging magulang. Sa pamamagitan ng mga programang pang-edukasyon tulad ng Comprehensive Sexuality Education at pagpapalaganap ng kaalaman, maaaring mapigilan ang patuloy na pagtaas ng bilang ng mga batang nagiging ina.','Kung isasalin ang tekstong ito para sa kampanya ng lokal na pamahalaan sa mga komunidad, ano ang dapat baguhin sa estruktura upang mas maging epektibo ito para sa target audience?','Gumamit ng mas personal na karanasan o testimonya ng kabataan.','Palitan ang impormasyon ng mas maraming datos at estadistika.','Iwasan ang pagsama ng mga komplikasyon sa kalusugan.','Tanggalin ang bahagi ng solusyon at magbigay na lang ng babala.','A','Upang mas maging epektibo ang mensahe sa komunidad, lalo na sa kabataan, mainam na dagdagan ang tekstong ekspositori ng personal na naratibo o testimonya. Bagamat ekspositori ito, ang paghahalo ng informative at narrative elements ay mas makakatawag-pansin, lalo na kung layunin ay pagbabago ng asal.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,12,'Ang early pregnancy o maagang pagbubuntis ay isang kondisyon kung saan ang isang babae, karaniwan ay isang kabataan, ay nagdadalang-tao sa edad na hindi pa ganap na handa sa pisikal at emosyonal na aspeto. Ito ay madalas na dulot ng kakulangan ng tamang kaalaman ukol sa kalusugan ng reproduktibo at hindi paggamit ng kontraseptibo. Ang mga kabataang nagiging buntis ng maaga ay kadalasang nahaharap sa mga komplikasyon sa kalusugan tulad ng preeclampsia, anemia, at premature birth. Bukod dito, ang kanilang buhay ay maaari ring magkaroon ng malaking epekto, tulad ng pagkakagambala sa edukasyon at paghahanapbuhay. Mahalaga ang papel ng mga magulang, guro, at pamahalaan upang magbigay ng tamang edukasyon at gabay sa mga kabataan ukol sa sekswalidad at responsibilidad sa pagiging magulang. Sa pamamagitan ng mga programang pang-edukasyon tulad ng Comprehensive Sexuality Education at pagpapalaganap ng kaalaman, maaaring mapigilan ang patuloy na pagtaas ng bilang ng ang kanilang buhay ay maaari ring magkaroon ng malaking epekto, tulad ng pagkakagambala sa edukasyon at paghahanapbuhay. Mahalaga ang papel ng mga magulang, guro, at pamahalaan upang magbigay ng tamang edukasyon at gabay sa mga kabataan ukol sa sekswalidad at responsibilidad sa pagiging magulang. Sa pamamagitan ng mga programang pang-edukasyon tulad ng Comprehensive Sexuality Education at pagpapalaganap ng kaalaman, maaaring mapigilan ang patuloy na pagtaas ng bilang ng mga batang nagiging ina.','Ano ang mas malawak na implikasyon ng estrukturang ginamit sa tekstong ito sa pagbuo ng mga pampublikong polisiya ukol sa kalusugan ng kabataan?','Nagpapalakas ito ng argumento para sa legalisasyon ng aborsyon sa ating bansa.','Nagbibigay ito ng batayan sa pagpapatupad ng mga programang edukasyonal at agarang aksyon','Itinutulak nito ang ideya ng pagkakaroon ng parusa sa mga batang ina sa lipunan.','Nagtatanggal ito ng papel ng pamahalaan sa pagresolba sa isyu hinggil sa maagang pagbubuntis.','B','Dahil sa maayos na estrukturang nagpapaliwanag ng sanhi, epekto, at solusyon, ang tekstong ito ay nagiging gabay sa mga policy makers para gumawa ng proactive na hakbang tulad ng edukasyon sa sekswalidad, imbes na parusa o represibong aksyon.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,13,'Bilang ng Malnutrisyon bumulusok sa Pinas\n\nLumubo ang bilang ng mga batanag nagkakaroon ng malnutrisyon ayon sa datos na Department of Health (DOH) natinatayang 3 milyong bata mula Enero hangang Marso nitong taon.\n\nMarami sa mga batang ito ang hindi nakakakuha ng sapat na nutrisyon sa kanilang pagkain. Ang mga magulang, partikular sa mga malalayong komunidad, ay nahihirapan sa pagbibigay ng tamang pagkain at nutrisyon para sa kanilang mga anak. Ayon kay Dr. Maria Lopez, isang pediatrician, "Ang malnutrisyon ay may malalim na epekto sa kalusugan ng mga bata at sa kanilang kinabukasan."\n\npagbibigay ng tamang pagkain at nutrisyon para sa kanilang mga anak. Ayon kay Dr. Maria Lopez, isang pediatrician, "Ang malnutrisyon ay may malalim na epekto sa kalusugan ng mga bata at sa kanilang kinabukasan."\n\nBilang tugon, naglunsad ang pamahalaan ng mga programa upang matulungan ang mga pook na may mataas na insidente ng malnutrisyon, ngunit marami pa rin ang nagsasabi na hindi sapat ang mga hakbang na ito. Ang mga hindi maabot na lugar at ang kakulangan ng mga resources ay nagsisilbing mga hadlang sa mga layunin ng mga naturang proyekto.\n\nAng isyung ito ay tumutukoy hindi lamang sa pisikal na kalusugan ng mga bata kundi pati na rin sa pangmatagalang epekto nito sa edukasyon at kalagayan ng ekonomiya ng bansa.','Paano isinunod-sunod ang mga impormasyon sa balita upang ipakita ang kabuuang epekto ng malnutrisyon?','Sinimulan sa mga patotoo ng magulang, sinundan ng datos, at nagtapos sa personal na kwento.','Sinimulan sa datos ng kaso, sinundan ng sanhi, epekto, at tugon ng pamahalaan.','Sinimulan sa kasaysayan ng malnutrisyon sa bansa, sinundan ng panayam.','Sinimulan sa epekto, sinundan ng datos at tinapos sa opinyon ng manunulat.','B','Ang estruktura ng balita ay sumusunod sa lohikal na pagkakasunod: balita (datos mula sa DOH) → sanhi (kakulangan ng nutrisyon, kahirapan) → epekto (kalusugan, kinabukasan) → tugon (programa ng pamahalaan). Isa itong halimbawa ng balitang tuwiran at estruktural, batay sa mga bahagi ng balita (Ulo, Katawan, Detalye).',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,14,'Bilang ng Malnutrisyon bumulusok sa Pinas\n\nLumubo ang bilang ng mga batanag nagkakaroon ng malnutrisyon ayon sa datos na Department of Health (DOH) natinatayang 3 milyong bata mula Enero hangang Marso nitong taon.\n\nMarami sa mga batang ito ang hindi nakakakuha ng sapat na nutrisyon sa kanilang pagkain. Ang mga magulang, partikular sa mga malalayong komunidad, ay nahihirapan sa pagbibigay ng tamang pagkain at nutrisyon para sa kanilang mga anak. Ayon kay Dr. Maria Lopez, isang pediatrician, "Ang malnutrisyon ay may malalim na epekto sa kalusugan ng mga bata at sa kanilang kinabukasan."\n\npagbibigay ng tamang pagkain at nutrisyon para sa kanilang mga anak. Ayon kay Dr. Maria Lopez, isang pediatrician, "Ang malnutrisyon ay may malalim na epekto sa kalusugan ng mga bata at sa kanilang kinabukasan."\n\nBilang tugon, naglunsad ang pamahalaan ng mga programa upang matulungan ang mga pook na may mataas na insidente ng malnutrisyon, ngunit marami pa rin ang nagsasabi na hindi sapat ang mga hakbang na ito. Ang mga hindi maabot na lugar at ang kakulangan ng mga resources ay nagsisilbing mga hadlang sa mga layunin ng mga naturang proyekto.\n\nAng isyung ito ay tumutukoy hindi lamang sa pisikal na kalusugan ng mga bata kundi pati na rin sa pangmatagalang epekto nito sa edukasyon at kalagayan ng ekonomiya ng bansa.','Anong katangian ng isang balita ang makikita sa paggamit ng panayam kay Dr. Maria Lopez?','Impormal na tono ng balitang bago at napapanahon','Panig na pumapabor sa pamahalaang bayan.','Kredibilidad sa pagkakaroon ng tamang sanggunian','Paggamit ng batayan upang maging kapana-panabik','C','Ang pagsama ng panayam mula sa eksperto ay nagpapataas ng kredibilidad ng balita, na isang mahalagang katangian. Pinapakita nito ang pagiging factual at objective ng balita, hindi lamang opinyon ng reporter.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,15,'Bilang ng Malnutrisyon bumulusok sa Pinas\n\nLumubo ang bilang ng mga batanag nagkakaroon ng malnutrisyon ayon sa datos na Department of Health (DOH) natinatayang 3 milyong bata mula Enero hangang Marso nitong taon.\n\nMarami sa mga batang ito ang hindi nakakakuha ng sapat na nutrisyon sa kanilang pagkain. Ang mga magulang, partikular sa mga malalayong komunidad, ay nahihirapan sa pagbibigay ng tamang pagkain at nutrisyon para sa kanilang mga anak. Ayon kay Dr. Maria Lopez, isang pediatrician, "Ang malnutrisyon ay may malalim na epekto sa kalusugan ng mga bata at sa kanilang kinabukasan."\n\npagbibigay ng tamang pagkain at nutrisyon para sa kanilang mga anak. Ayon kay Dr. Maria Lopez, isang pediatrician, "Ang malnutrisyon ay may malalim na epekto sa kalusugan ng mga bata at sa kanilang kinabukasan."\n\nBilang tugon, naglunsad ang pamahalaan ng mga programa upang matulungan ang mga pook na may mataas na insidente ng malnutrisyon, ngunit marami pa rin ang nagsasabi na hindi sapat ang mga hakbang na ito. Ang mga hindi maabot na lugar at ang kakulangan ng mga resources ay nagsisilbing mga hadlang sa mga layunin ng mga naturang proyekto.\n\nAng isyung ito ay tumutukoy hindi lamang sa pisikal na kalusugan ng mga bata kundi pati na rin sa pangmatagalang epekto nito sa edukasyon at kalagayan ng ekonomiya ng bansa.','Paano mo maaaring gamitin ang estruktura ng balitang ito upang makabuo ng isang kampanya sa paaralan ukol sa kalusugan ng kabataan?','Gumamit ng salaysay mula sa mga guro na may personal na karanasan lamang ng guro.','Magpabatid ng impormasyon gamit ang angkop datos, epekto, sanggunian at mungkahing solusyon.','Gumawa ng sanaysay na may emosyonal na panawagan lamang hinggil na napakinggang usapan ng mga guro.','Magpokus lamang sa mga positibong aspeto ng kalusugan upang makaiwas sa masasamang dulot malnutrisyon sa tao.','B','Ang malinaw na estruktura ng balita—mula sa datos, sanhi, epekto, at tugon—ay isang epektibong gabay para sa mga kampanyang pangkaalaman. Sa ganitong paraan, mas maiintindihan at mararamdaman ng mga kabataan ang kahalagahan ng isyu, at maaaring makabuo ng mga kongkretong hakbang.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,16,'Bilang ng Malnutrisyon bumulusok sa Pinas\n\nLumubo ang bilang ng mga batanag nagkakaroon ng malnutrisyon ayon sa datos na Department of Health (DOH) natinatayang 3 milyong bata mula Enero hangang Marso nitong taon.\n\nMarami sa mga batang ito ang hindi nakakakuha ng sapat na nutrisyon sa kanilang pagkain. Ang mga magulang, partikular sa mga malalayong komunidad, ay nahihirapan sa pagbibigay ng tamang pagkain at nutrisyon para sa kanilang mga anak. Ayon kay Dr. Maria Lopez, isang pediatrician, "Ang malnutrisyon ay may malalim na epekto sa kalusugan ng mga bata at sa kanilang kinabukasan."\n\npagbibigay ng tamang pagkain at nutrisyon para sa kanilang mga anak. Ayon kay Dr. Maria Lopez, isang pediatrician, "Ang malnutrisyon ay may malalim na epekto sa kalusugan ng mga bata at sa kanilang kinabukasan."\n\nBilang tugon, naglunsad ang pamahalaan ng mga programa upang matulungan ang mga pook na may mataas na insidente ng malnutrisyon, ngunit marami pa rin ang nagsasabi na hindi sapat ang mga hakbang na ito. Ang mga hindi maabot na lugar at ang kakulangan ng mga resources ay nagsisilbing mga hadlang sa mga layunin ng mga naturang proyekto.\n\nAng isyung ito ay tumutukoy hindi lamang sa pisikal na kalusugan ng mga bata kundi pati na rin sa pangmatagalang epekto nito sa edukasyon at kalagayan ng ekonomiya ng bansa.','Kung ikaw ay isang patnugot ng pahayagan, ano ang maaari mong idagdag sa balitang ito upang mas mailahad ang kabuuang larawan ng isyu?','Magsama ng opinyon ng manunulat upang tumindig ang balita','Magdagdag ng impormasyon mula sa mga batang nakaranas ng malnutrisyon','Isama ang istorya ng mga dayuhan para ikumpara sa Pilipinas','Tanggalin ang datos upang magmukhang mas madali ang solusyon','B','Ang pagsama ng human-interest angle—mga testimonya o personal na karanasan mula sa mismong apektado—ay makatutulong upang mapalalim ang ugnayan ng mambabasa sa isyu. Hindi nito sinisira ang estruktura ng balita; sa halip, pinayayaman nito ang nilalaman sa aspeto ng panlipunang konteksto.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,17,'Dapat nang ipagbawal ang same-sex marriage sa ating bansa upang mapanatili ang mga tradisyon at moralidad na matagal nang ipinaglalaban ng ating lipunan. Ang kasal ay isang sagradong institusyon na nakabatay sa natural na relasyon ng lalaki at babae, kaya''t hindi dapat baguhin o gawing iba ang kahulugan nito. Ang pagpapasa ng batas na magpapahintulot sa same-sex marriage ay maaaring magdulot ng pagkalito at magbukas ng pintuan sa iba pang hindi naaangkop na mga kasunduan. Dapat nating pahalagahan ang pamilya bilang pundasyon ng ating komunidad at itaguyod ang mga pagpapahalaga ng ating kultura at relihiyon. Ang ating bansa ay may mga matibay na paniniwala at tradisyon na nararapat protektahan mula sa mga pagbabago na maaaring magbanta sa ating pagkakakilanlan. Sa ganitong paraan, mas magiging matatag ang ating lipunan sa mga pagsubok ng panahon.','Paano makatutulong ang pag-unawa sa estruktura ng tekstong persuweysib sa pagbuo ng isang balanseng pananaw sa isyung panlipunan tulad ng same-sex marriage?','Tinuturuan tayong tanggapin na may isang tamang pananaw lang sa bawat isyu.','Nagbibigay ito ng paraan upang maniwala agad sa sinumang matibay ang argumento.','Nakatutulong ito upang kilatisin ang punto, ebidensiya, at lohika ng parehong panig.','Pinipilit tayong maniwala sa opinyon ng may-akda upang hikayatin tayo.','C','Ang pag-unawa sa punto, ebidensiya, at analisis ay nagbibigay-daan sa mas mapanuring pag-iisip. Sa halip na basta tanggapin ang argumento, naaanalisa ito—may pagkakataon tayong tukuyin kung ito ba’y may bias, sapat ang ebidensiya, o kulang sa pananaw.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,18,'Dapat nang ipagbawal ang same-sex marriage sa ating bansa upang mapanatili ang mga tradisyon at moralidad na matagal nang ipinaglalaban ng ating lipunan. Ang kasal ay isang sagradong institusyon na nakabatay sa natural na relasyon ng lalaki at babae, kaya''t hindi dapat baguhin o gawing iba ang kahulugan nito. Ang pagpapasa ng batas na magpapahintulot sa same-sex marriage ay maaaring magdulot ng pagkalito at magbukas ng pintuan sa iba pang hindi naaangkop na mga kasunduan. Dapat nating pahalagahan ang pamilya bilang pundasyon ng ating komunidad at itaguyod ang mga pagpapahalaga ng ating kultura at relihiyon. Ang ating bansa ay may mga matibay na paniniwala at tradisyon na nararapat protektahan mula sa mga pagbabago na maaaring magbanta sa ating pagkakakilanlan. Sa ganitong paraan, mas magiging matatag ang ating lipunan sa mga pagsubok ng panahon.','Alin sa mga sumusunod ang malinaw na punto ng tekstong persuweysib?','Dapat ipaglaban ang karapatan ng bawat isa na magmahal.','Dapat ipagbawal ang same-sex marriage upang mapanatili ang tradisyon at moralidad.','Ang kasal ay simbolo lamang at hindi dapat seryosohin.','Dapat bigyang-priyoridad ang edukasyon kaysa sa mga isyung panlipunan.','B','Ito ang pangunahing punto ng tekstong persuweysib — ang pagbibigay diin sa pagtutol sa same-sex marriage upang mapanatili ang tradisyon, moralidad, at kultura. Ito ang pundasyong argumento na inuulit at pinapalakas sa bawat talata.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,19,'Dapat nang ipagbawal ang same-sex marriage sa ating bansa upang mapanatili ang mga tradisyon at moralidad na matagal nang ipinaglalaban ng ating lipunan. Ang kasal ay isang sagradong institusyon na nakabatay sa natural na relasyon ng lalaki at babae, kaya''t hindi dapat baguhin o gawing iba ang kahulugan nito. Ang pagpapasa ng batas na magpapahintulot sa same-sex marriage ay maaaring magdulot ng pagkalito at magbukas ng pintuan sa iba pang hindi naaangkop na mga kasunduan. Dapat nating pahalagahan ang pamilya bilang pundasyon ng ating komunidad at itaguyod ang mga pagpapahalaga ng ating kultura at relihiyon. Ang ating bansa ay may mga matibay na paniniwala at tradisyon na nararapat protektahan mula sa mga pagbabago na maaaring magbanta sa ating pagkakakilanlan. Sa ganitong paraan, mas magiging matatag ang ating lipunan sa mga pagsubok ng panahon.','Kung ikaw ay gagawa ng isang kontra-persuweysibong teksto, ano ang una mong kailangang gawin batay sa pagkakaunawa sa tekstong ito?','Balewalain ang argumento ng kabilang panig.','Gumamit ng mas emosyonal na pananalita kaysa sa orihinal.','Alamin at tukuyin kung saan nagkulang o may bias ang ebidensiya.','Magkwento ng personal na karanasan bilang sentro ng argumento.','C','Sa paggawa ng kontra-persuweysibong teksto, mahalaga ang pag- unawa sa estruktura ng naunang argumento upang matukoy ang kahinaan ng punto at maglatag ng sariling lohikal na ebidensiya. Ito ang susi sa mas makatuwirang diskurso.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,20,'Ang pagpapasa ng batas ukol sa diborsyo sa Pilipinas ay mahalaga upang matulungan ang mga indibidwal na nasa masalimuot at abusadong relasyon. Sa kasalukuyan, ang mga mag-asawang hindi na magkakasundo at hindi na masaya ay nahihirapang maghiwalay dahil sa kakulangan ng legal na opsyon, maliban sa annulment na isang mahaba at magastos na proseso. Ang diborsyo ay magbibigay ng pagkakataon sa mga tao na makapagbago at magpatuloy sa mas maligaya at mas ligtas na buhay, lalo na sa mga biktima ng pang-aabuso. Huwag nating kalimutan na ang kaligayahan at kapakanan ng bawat isa, lalo na ng mga kababaihan at bata, ay mas mahalaga kaysa sa pagpapatuloy ng isang relasyon na puno ng tensyon at karahasan. Ang pagpapasa ng diborsyo ay isang hakbang tungo sa mas makatarungan at makatawid na sistema ng batas na tumutugon sa pangangailangan ng bawat isa sa atin. Kung nais nating magtaguyod ng isang lipunang nagpapahalaga sa kalayaan at dignidad ng bawat isa, nararapat lamang na bigyan ng pagkakataon ang diborsyo bilang isang opsyon sa mga mag-asawang hindi na masaya at nagkakaroon ng hindi pagkakaunawaan.','Paano mo maikokonekta ang estruktura ng tekstong ito sa pagbibigay ng solusyon sa isang isyung panlipunan?','Ang estruktura ng tekstong ito ay nagpapalakas lamang ng opinyon, kaya hindi ito nakatutulong sa usaping diborstyo sa ating bansa sa kasalukuyan.','Sa pamamagitan ng lohikal na pangangatwiran at datos, naipapakita kung paano ang diborsyo ay isang makatarungang solusyon sa isyu ng abusadong relasyon.','Hindi sapat ang estruktura ng tekstong argumentatibo sa pagbibigay ng tunay na solusyon.','Mas mainam ang mas emosyonal na paraan upang tugunan ang mga isyung panlipunan kaysa argumentatibo.','B','Ang tekstong argumentatibo ay may malinaw na tesis, proposisyon, datos, at pangangatuwiran na ginagamit upang maipaliwanag ang isyu at imungkahi ang solusyon, sa kasong ito, ang pagsasabatas ng diborsyo.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,21,'Ang pagpapasa ng batas ukol sa diborsyo sa Pilipinas ay mahalaga upang matulungan ang mga indibidwal na nasa masalimuot at abusadong relasyon. Sa kasalukuyan, ang mga mag-asawang hindi na magkakasundo at hindi na masaya ay nahihirapang maghiwalay dahil sa kakulangan ng legal na opsyon, maliban sa annulment na isang mahaba at magastos na proseso. Ang diborsyo ay magbibigay ng pagkakataon sa mga tao na makapagbago at magpatuloy sa mas maligaya at mas ligtas na buhay, lalo na sa mga biktima ng pang-aabuso. Huwag nating kalimutan na ang kaligayahan at kapakanan ng bawat isa, lalo na ng mga kababaihan at bata, ay mas mahalaga kaysa sa pagpapatuloy ng isang relasyon na puno ng tensyon at karahasan. Ang pagpapasa ng diborsyo ay isang hakbang tungo sa mas makatarungan at makatawid na sistema ng batas na tumutugon sa pangangailangan ng bawat isa sa atin. Kung nais nating magtaguyod ng isang lipunang nagpapahalaga sa kalayaan at dignidad ng bawat isa, nararapat lamang na bigyan ng pagkakataon ang diborsyo bilang isang opsyon sa mga mag-asawang hindi na masaya at nagkakaroon ng hindi pagkakaunawaan.','Paano makatutulong ang pagkilala sa rebuttal ng isang argumentatibong teksto sa pagpapalalim ng diskurso sa isang kontrobersyal na isyu?','Pinapahina nito ang argumento kaya mas mabuting iwasan.','Nagsisilbi itong paraan upang tanggapin ang panig ng kalaban nang buo.','Pinatitibay nito ang argumento ng may-akda sa pamamagitan ng pagharap at pagpapabulaan sa posibleng pagtutol.','Hindi ito mahalaga sa isang argumentatibo, mas mahalaga ang emosyon.','C','Ang rebuttal ay mahalagang bahagi ng estruktura dahil dito pinapakita ng may-akda ang kakayahang tumugon sa posibleng pagtutol sa kanyang panig — isang katangian ng critical thinking at epektibong persuasion.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,22,'Ang pagpapasa ng batas ukol sa diborsyo sa Pilipinas ay mahalaga upang matulungan ang mga indibidwal na nasa masalimuot at abusadong relasyon. Sa kasalukuyan, ang mga mag-asawang hindi na magkakasundo at hindi na masaya ay nahihirapang maghiwalay dahil sa kakulangan ng legal na opsyon, maliban sa annulment na isang mahaba at magastos na proseso. Ang diborsyo ay magbibigay ng pagkakataon sa mga tao na makapagbago at magpatuloy sa mas maligaya at mas ligtas na buhay, lalo na sa mga biktima ng pang-aabuso. Huwag nating kalimutan na ang kaligayahan at kapakanan ng bawat isa, lalo na ng mga kababaihan at bata, ay mas mahalaga kaysa sa pagpapatuloy ng isang relasyon na puno ng tensyon at karahasan. Ang pagpapasa ng diborsyo ay isang hakbang tungo sa mas makatarungan at makatawid na sistema ng batas na tumutugon sa pangangailangan ng bawat isa sa atin. Kung nais nating magtaguyod ng isang lipunang nagpapahalaga sa kalayaan at dignidad ng bawat isa, nararapat lamang na bigyan ng pagkakataon ang diborsyo bilang isang opsyon sa mga mag-asawang hindi na masaya at nagkakaroon ng hindi pagkakaunawaan.','Alin sa sumusunod ang tumutukoy sa tesis ng tekstong binasa?','Mahalaga ang diborsyo upang mapanatili ang pagkakaisa ng pamilya at mapigilan ang pagkawatak-watak.','Ang diborsyo ay magastos at hindi nararapat isabatas sa Pilipinas dahil nagdudulot ng masama sa tao.','Ang diborsyo ay dapat ipasa bilang legal na opsyon upang maprotektahan ang mga taong nasa mapanirang relasyon.','Ang kaligayahan ng bawat isa ay dapat isakripisyo para sa pamilyang buo.','C','Ito ang pinakadiwa ng argumento o tesis — ang pagpapahayag ng paninindigan na kinakailangang isabatas ang diborsyo bilang alternatibo upang protektahan ang mga indibidwal sa hindi na maayos na relasyon.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,23,'Abril 10, 2025\n\nG. Juan Dela Cruz Tagapamanihala ng Sangay Metro Manila, Philippines 0997-988-8987\n\nPaksa: Paghingi ng Pahintulot para sa Isang Organisadong Seminar\n\nMahal na G. Dela Cruz,\n\nMagandang araw po! Ako po ay sumusulat upang humiling ng inyong pahintulot at suporta para sa isang seminar na inihanda ng aming paaralan, ang Seminar sa Pagpapabuti ng Mga Kasanayan sa Mahal na G. Dela Cruz,\n\nMagandang araw po! Ako po ay sumusulat upang humiling ng inyong pahintulot at suporta para sa isang seminar na inihanda ng aming paaralan, ang Seminar sa Pagpapabuti ng Mga Kasanayan sa\n\nPagtuturo na gaganapin sa Mayo 15, 2025 sa aming paaralan. Layunin po ng seminar na ito na mapalawak ang kaalaman ng mga guro sa makabago at mas epektibong pamamaraan ng pagtuturo.\n\nAng mga detalye ng seminar ay ang mga sumusunod: • Petsa: Mayo 15, 2025 • Oras: 8:00 AM - 4:00 PM • Lugar: Juan Dimasalang Integrated School\n\nMga Layon: 1. Magbigay ng mga kasanayan at kaalaman sa mga guro 2. Ipakilala ang mga makabagong teknolohiya sa pagtuturo 3. Magkaroon ng mga interaktibong aktibidad para sa pagpapalawak ng kasanayan\n\nKami po ay umaasa na inyong maaprubahan ang aming kahilingan at matulungan kami sa pagpapalaganap ng kaalaman at kasanayan sa mga guro ng aming paaralan.\n\nMaraming salamat po at nawa’y maging matagumpay ang aming proyekto.\n\nLubos na gumagalang,\n\nTJ Cruz Punongguro','Paano ipinapakita sa liham ang layunin ng isang korespondensiyang opisyal?','Sa pamamagitan ng salaysay tungkol sa mga personal na karanasan ng punongguro.','Sa pagsasama ng mga detalye ng seminar upang malinaw na maipabatid ang layunin ng sulat.','Sa paggamit ng matatalinghagang salita upang mas maging kaakit-akit ang liham.','Sa pagbanggit ng damdamin ng guro ukol sa edukasyon.','B','Mahalaga sa isang korespondensiyang opisyal ang malinaw na layunin, at ito ay ipinakita sa pamamagitan ng detalyadong paglalahad ng seminar—petsa, oras, lugar, at mga layunin—na tumutukoy sa tiyak na dahilan ng sulat.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,24,'Abril 10, 2025\n\nG. Juan Dela Cruz Tagapamanihala ng Sangay Metro Manila, Philippines 0997-988-8987\n\nPaksa: Paghingi ng Pahintulot para sa Isang Organisadong Seminar\n\nMahal na G. Dela Cruz,\n\nMagandang araw po! Ako po ay sumusulat upang humiling ng inyong pahintulot at suporta para sa isang seminar na inihanda ng aming paaralan, ang Seminar sa Pagpapabuti ng Mga Kasanayan sa Mahal na G. Dela Cruz,\n\nMagandang araw po! Ako po ay sumusulat upang humiling ng inyong pahintulot at suporta para sa isang seminar na inihanda ng aming paaralan, ang Seminar sa Pagpapabuti ng Mga Kasanayan sa\n\nPagtuturo na gaganapin sa Mayo 15, 2025 sa aming paaralan. Layunin po ng seminar na ito na mapalawak ang kaalaman ng mga guro sa makabago at mas epektibong pamamaraan ng pagtuturo.\n\nAng mga detalye ng seminar ay ang mga sumusunod: • Petsa: Mayo 15, 2025 • Oras: 8:00 AM - 4:00 PM • Lugar: Juan Dimasalang Integrated School\n\nMga Layon: 1. Magbigay ng mga kasanayan at kaalaman sa mga guro 2. Ipakilala ang mga makabagong teknolohiya sa pagtuturo 3. Magkaroon ng mga interaktibong aktibidad para sa pagpapalawak ng kasanayan\n\nKami po ay umaasa na inyong maaprubahan ang aming kahilingan at matulungan kami sa pagpapalaganap ng kaalaman at kasanayan sa mga guro ng aming paaralan.\n\nMaraming salamat po at nawa’y maging matagumpay ang aming proyekto.\n\nLubos na gumagalang,\n\nTJ Cruz Punongguro','Paano maaaring gamitin ang estruktura ng liham na ito bilang modelo sa pagsulat ng iba pang korespondensiyang opisyal sa hinaharap?','Gamitin ang istruktura nito upang makabuo ng sulat na may emosyonal na tono.','Sundin ang pormal na pagbati, malinaw na layunin, detalyadong katawan, at magalang na pagtatapos upang magkaroon ng maayos na komunikasyon.','Iwasan ang detalyado at gawin na lang maikli para mas madali basahin.','Gumamit ng impormal na paraan upang maging mas magaan ang dating ng sulat.','B','Ang estruktura ng liham ay maayos, malinaw, at pormal, kaya ito ay mainam na huwaran sa pagsulat ng iba pang korespondensiyang opisyal, lalo na kung may kahilingang nais ipaabot.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,1,25,'Abril 10, 2025\n\nG. Juan Dela Cruz Tagapamanihala ng Sangay Metro Manila, Philippines 0997-988-8987\n\nPaksa: Paghingi ng Pahintulot para sa Isang Organisadong Seminar\n\nMahal na G. Dela Cruz,\n\nMagandang araw po! Ako po ay sumusulat upang humiling ng inyong pahintulot at suporta para sa isang seminar na inihanda ng aming paaralan, ang Seminar sa Pagpapabuti ng Mga Kasanayan sa Mahal na G. Dela Cruz,\n\nMagandang araw po! Ako po ay sumusulat upang humiling ng inyong pahintulot at suporta para sa isang seminar na inihanda ng aming paaralan, ang Seminar sa Pagpapabuti ng Mga Kasanayan sa\n\nPagtuturo na gaganapin sa Mayo 15, 2025 sa aming paaralan. Layunin po ng seminar na ito na mapalawak ang kaalaman ng mga guro sa makabago at mas epektibong pamamaraan ng pagtuturo.\n\nAng mga detalye ng seminar ay ang mga sumusunod: • Petsa: Mayo 15, 2025 • Oras: 8:00 AM - 4:00 PM • Lugar: Juan Dimasalang Integrated School\n\nMga Layon: 1. Magbigay ng mga kasanayan at kaalaman sa mga guro 2. Ipakilala ang mga makabagong teknolohiya sa pagtuturo 3. Magkaroon ng mga interaktibong aktibidad para sa pagpapalawak ng kasanayan\n\nKami po ay umaasa na inyong maaprubahan ang aming kahilingan at matulungan kami sa pagpapalaganap ng kaalaman at kasanayan sa mga guro ng aming paaralan.\n\nMaraming salamat po at nawa’y maging matagumpay ang aming proyekto.\n\nLubos na gumagalang,\n\nTJ Cruz Punongguro','Kung ikaw ay isang tagapamahala at nakatanggap ng liham na tulad nito, anong aspekto ng sulat ang dapat mong suriin upang makapagdesisyon nang maayos?','Ang layunin ng seminar, konkretong benepisyo, at organisadong detalye ng aktibidad.','Ang pormalidad ng pirma ng sumulat.','Ang damdaming inilagay ng sumulat sa kanyang mensahe.','Ang haba at lalim ng mga salitang ginamit sa sulat.','A','Bilang tagapamahala, kailangang pagtuunan ng pansin ang nilalaman, layunin, at benepisyo ng kahilingan, na siyang batayan kung dapat bang aprubahan ang seminar. Pamagat: "Ang Epekto ng Programang Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program (4Ps) sa Antas ng Edukasyon at Kalusugan sa Barangay Masagana" Mananaliksik: Dela Cruz, J. at Reyes, M. M. Institusyon: Unibersidad ng Pilipinas Diliman Taon: 2023 Abstrak: Ang pag-aaral na ito ay sumuri sa epekto ng Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program (4Ps) sa antas ng edukasyon at kalusugan ng mga benepisyaryong pamilya sa Barangay Masagana. Gamit ang mixed-methods approach, ang pag-aaral ay nagsagawa ng survey sa 200 pamilyang 4Ps at nagsagawa ng focus group discussions sa 20 piling mga magulang. Ipinakita ng resulta ng survey ang bahagyang pagtaas sa enrollment rate ng mga batang nasa elementarya at sekondarya (mula 85% bago ang 4Ps tungo sa 92% pagkatapos ng 3 taon). Gayundin, naitala ang minor na pagbaba sa bilang ng mga batang nakararanas ng malnutrisyon (mula 28% tungo sa 25%). Ang qualitative data mula sa FGD ay nagpahiwatig na ang tulong pinansyal ay nakatulong sa pagbili ng mga gamit sa paaralan at pagpapatingin sa health center, ngunit mayroon pa ring mga hamon sa access sa de-kalidad na edukasyon at sapat na nutrisyon. Ang pag-aaral ay nagrerekomenda ng masusing pagsubaybay at pagpapabuti ng programa upang masiguro ang pangmatagalang positibong epekto sa komunidad.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,26,NULL,'Batay sa abstrak, ano ang pangunahing implikasyon ng programang 4Ps sa antas ng edukasyon sa Barangay Masagana?','Bumaba ang enrollment rate ng mga mag-aaral.','Walang nagbago sa enrollment rate ng mga mag-aaral.','Bahagyang tumaas ang enrollment rate ng mga mag-aaral.','Lubhang tumaas ang enrollment rate ng mga mag-aaral.','C','. Ayon sa resulta ng survey na nakasaad sa abstrak, nagkaroon ng "bahagyang pagtaas sa enrollment rate ng mga batang nasa elementarya at sekondarya (mula 85% bago ang 4Ps tungo sa 92% pagkatapos ng 3 taon)." Ipinapahiwatig nito na ang 4Ps ay may positibong, kahit na hindi lubhang malaki, na epekto sa pagpapatala ng mga mag-aaral sa paaralan sa Barangay Masagana.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,27,NULL,'Ayon sa abstrak, ano ang isang kritikal na obserbasyon o hamon na nananatili sa komunidad ng Barangay Masagana kahit mayroong programang 4Ps?','Lubos na bumaba ang bilang ng mga batang nakararanas ng malnutrisyon.','Lahat ng mga benepisyaryong pamilya ay mayroon nang sapat na nutrisyon.','Mayroong mga hamon sa access sa de-kalidad na edukasyon at sapat na nutrisyon.','Wala nang problema sa pagbili ng mga gamit sa paaralan ang mga benepisyaryo.','C','Ayon sa abstrak, ang qualitative data mula sa Focus Group Discussions (FGD) ay nagpahiwatig na bagama''t nakatulong ang tulong pinansyal sa pagbili ng mga gamit sa paaralan at pagpapatingin sa health center, "mayroon pa ring mga hamon sa access sa de-kalidad na edukasyon at sapat na nutrisyon." Ito ay isang kritikal na obserbasyon na nagpapakita na kahit mayroong 4Ps, hindi pa lubusang nasosolusyunan ang mga problemang ito sa komunidad ng Barangay Masagana.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,28,NULL,'Kung ikaw ay isang lider sa Barangay Masagana, batay sa datos mula sa abstrak, ano ang pinakamahalagang susunod na hakbang na maaari mong isaalang-alang upang mas mapabuti ang sitwasyon ng iyong komunidad kaugnay ng 4Ps?','Itigil ang pakikilahok sa 4Ps dahil hindi naman ito nagdulot ng malaking pagbabago ayon sa abstrak at wala itong magandang maidudulot.','Makipagtulungan sa mga mananaliksik at ahensya ng gobyerno upang tugunan ang mga hamon sa de-kalidad na edukasyon at sapat na nutrisyon na natukoy sa pag-aaral.','Maglunsad ng mas maraming survey upang kumpirmahin ang mga natuklasan ng pag-aaral tungkol sa mga hamon sa de-kalidad na edukasyon at sapat na nutrisyon.','Ipagpatuloy lamang ang kasalukuyang implementasyon ng programa nang walang pagbabago kagaya pa rin ng dati.','B','Ang abstrak ay malinaw na nagpapakita na bagama''t nagkaroon ng bahagyang positibong epekto ang 4Ps sa enrollment at bahagyang pagbaba sa malnutrisyon, nananatili pa rin ang mga kritikal na hamon sa access sa de-kalidad na edukasyon at sapat na nutrisyon. Bilang isang lider ng komunidad, ang pinakamahalagang responsibilidad ay tugunan ang mga pangangailangang ito ng iyong nasasakupan.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,29,NULL,'Kung ikaw ay sa isa miyembro ng 4P''S, paano ka makakatulong sa ginawang pag- aaral ng mananaliksik?','Maglunsad ng programa tungkol sa pagnenegosyo para sa mga miyembro ng 4P''s.','Maglunsad ng programa na makatutulong sa edukasyon at kalusugan ng mga miyembro ng 4P''S.','Maglunsad ng Oplan Bantay na kung saan babantayan mo ang ginagawa ng mga miyembro ng 4P''S.','Maglunsad ng programang pangkalusugan na siyang binibigyan ng diin para sa miyembro ng 4P''S.','B','Ang pag-aaral ng mananaliksik ay naglalayong suriin ang epekto ng 4Ps sa antas ng edukasyon at kalusugan. Bilang isang miyembro na nakikinabang sa programa at nakakaranas ng direktang epekto nito, ang iyong aktibong pakikilahok sa pagpapabuti ng edukasyon at kalusugan ng iyong kapwa miyembro ay isang mahalagang paraan upang suportahan ang layunin ng pag-aaral.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,30,NULL,'Nang tangkain ni Don Pedro at Don Diego na patayin si Don Juan dahil sa inggit, ano ang mararamdaman kung ikaw ang nasa sitwasyon ni Don Juan?','Magpapasalamat na lamang na ikaw ay nakaligtas at magpapatuloy sa iyong misyon.','Magtatataka kung bakit nila nagawa iyon sa kabila ng iyong kabutihan.','Magagalit at maghihiganti sa kanilang ginawa sa iyong kataksilan.','Maghihinagpis at mawawalan ng pag-asa sa kabila ng kanilang pagtataksil.','B','Si Don Juan sa kuwento ay kilala sa kanyang kabaitan at pagtulong sa kanyang mga kapatid. Ang pagtatangka nilang patayin siya dahil lamang sa inggit ay isang malaking pagtataksil. Ang unang reaksyon sa ganitong sitwasyon ay malamang na pagtataka at pagkalito kung bakit nagawa ng mga taong pinagpakitaan mo ng kabutihan ang gayong kasamaan.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,31,NULL,'Ipagpalagay natin na ginawan ka rin ng pagtataksil ng iyong sariling pamilya, ano ang nararapat mong gawin sa kanila?','Awayin sila at sumbatan sa kanilang ginawang pagtataksil.','Makipag-usap nang maayos para magkaroon ng kalinawan ang lahat','Huwag silang kibuin at kalimutan na naging pamilya mo sila.','Gawin mo rin sa kanila ang ginawa nila sa iyo para maging patas.','B','Komunikasyon ang susi: Ang pagtataksil sa loob ng pamilya ay isang masakit at komplikadong sitwasyon. Ang unang hakbang na nararapat gawin ay ang subukang makipag-usap nang mahinahon at bukas sa mga miyembro ng pamilya na sangkot. Mahalagang malaman ang kanilang panig, ang mga dahilan sa likod ng kanilang ginawa, at magkaroon ng pagkakataon na ipahayag din ang iyong nararamdaman',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,32,NULL,'Paano sinusuri ng Ibong Adarna ang konsepto ng kapangyarihan?','Ipinapakita nito na ang kapangyarihan ay nakukuha lamang sa pamamagitan ng lakas at tapang sa pakikipaglaban.','Sinusuri nito ang kapangyarihan bilang isang mana na ipinapasa mula sa magulang patungo sa anak.','Ipinapakita nito na ang kapangyarihan ay madalas na nauuwi sa pang-aabuso at pagiging sakim, tulad ng ipinakita ng ilang karakter sa kuwento.','Sinusuri nito ang kapangyarihan hindi lamang bilang politikal o pisikal, kundi pati na rin ang impluwensya ng pag-ibig, pananampalataya, at ang kahalagahan ng moral na integridad.','D','Sa kabuuan, ang Ibong Adarna ay isang alegorya na nag-e-explore sa iba''t ibang dimensyon ng kapangyarihan at ang kahalagahan ng paggamit nito nang responsable at may mabuting kalooban.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,33,NULL,'Ang isa sa mahahalagang kaisipan sa Florante at Laura ay ang kahalagahan ng pagmamahal sa bayan. Sa iyong sariling pananaw at karanasan, ano ang pinakamahalagang paraan na sa tingin mo ay maipapakita mo ang iyong pagmamahal sa Pilipinas sa kasalukuyang panahon?','Sa pamamagitan ng pagsali sa mga protesta at pagtuligsa sa gobyerno.','Sa pamamagitan ng pagbabayad ng tamang buwis at pagsunod sa batas.','Sa pamamagitan ng pagbabayad ng tamang buwis at pagsunod sa batas.','Sa pamamagitan ng pagtangkilik sa mga produktong dayuhan.','B','Habang ang pagsali sa mga protesta at pagtuligsa sa gobyerno ay isang mahalagang karapatan sa isang demokratikong lipunan at maaaring maging paraan upang ipahayag ang pagmamahal sa bayan sa pamamagitan ng paghahangad ng pagbabago at pagpapabuti, naniniwala ako na ang pundasyon ng pagmamahal sa bayan ay nakasalalay sa pagiging responsableng mamamayan.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,34,NULL,'Sa Florante at Laura, malinaw na ipinakita ang epekto ng kasamaan at pang- aabuso ng kapangyarihan, tulad ng ginawa ni Adolfo. Sa iyong sariling karanasan o pagmamasid, ano ang pinakamatinding negatibong epekto ng korapsiyon o pang-aabuso ng kapangyarihan na iyong nasaksihan o pinaniniwalaang umiiral sa ating lipunan?','Ang pag-unlad ng ekonomiya ng ating bansa.','Ang pagkakaroon ng maraming trabaho para sa mga mamamayan.','Ang pagtaas ng antas ng krimen at kahirapan sa bansa.','Ang pagiging maayos at mabilis ng serbisyo ng publiko.','C','Ang korupsiyon at pang-aabuso ng kapangyarihan ay may malalim at malawakang negatibong epekto sa isang lipunan. Narito kung bakit ito humahantong sa pagtaas ng krimen at kahirapan.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,35,NULL,'Sa Florante at Laura, malinaw na ipinakita ang epekto ng kasamaan at pang- aabuso ng kapangyarihan, tulad ng ginawa ni Adolfo. Sa iyong sariling karanasan o pagmamasid, ano ang pinakamatinding negatibong epekto ng korapsiyon o pang-aabuso ng kapangyarihan na iyong nasaksihan o pinaniniwalaang umiiral sa ating lipunan?','Sa parehong akda, ang simula ay naglalayong agad na ipakilala ang pangunahing tauhan at ang kanyang kabayanihan.','Sa Ibong Adarna, ang simula ay nagtatakda ng isang tiyak na suliranin samantalang sa Florante at Laura ang simula ay nagpapakita ng isang malalim na personal na pagdurusa.','Ang simula ng parehong akda ay pangunahing naglalarawan ng kagandahan ng kaharian at ang masayang pamumuhay ng mga tauhan.','Sa Florante at Laura, ang simula ay agad na nagpapakita ng tunggalian sa pagitan ng mabuti at masama, samantalang sa Ibong Adarna mas nakasentro sa mahiwagang elemento.','B','Ibong Adarna: Ang simula ng Ibong Adarna ay agad na nagpapakita ng tiyak na suliranin - ang pagkakasakit ng Haring Fernando at ang tanging lunas ay ang awit ng Ibong Adarna. Ito ang nagtutulak sa buong banghay ng kuwento, kung saan ang tatlong prinsipe ay maglalakbay upang hanapin ang mahiwagang ibon. Florante at Laura: Sa kabilang banda, ang simula ng Florante at Laura ay nagpapakita ng isang malalim na personal na pagdurusa ni Florante na nakagapos sa isang madilim na gubat.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,36,NULL,'Sa iyong pagsusuri, paano naiiba ang pagkakasunod-sunod ng mga pangyayari sa banghay ng Florante at Laura kumpara sa Ibong Adarna sa paglalahad ng mga sanhi at bunga ng mga aksyon ng mga tauhan?','Ang parehong akda ay nagpapakita ng direktang sanhi at bunga na relasyon sa pagitan ng mga aksyon ng tauhan at mga resulta nito.','Sa Ibong Adarna, ang mga pangyayari ay direkta at simple ang mga aksyon ng tauhan samantalang sa Florante at Laura, ang mga sanhi at bunga ay komplikado.','Ang Florante at Laura ay hindi nagbibigay-diin sa sanhi at bunga, samantalang ang Ibong Adarna ay malinaw na nagpapakita nito.','Walang makabuluhang pagkakaiba sa paraan ng paglalahad ng sanhi at bunga sa banghay ng dalawang akda.','B','Sa Ibong Adarna, ang mga pangyayari direkta at simple ang mga aksyon ng tauhan samantalang sa Florante at Laura, ang mga sanhi at bunga ay komplikado.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,37,NULL,'Sa El Filibusterismo, ang pagnanais ni Simoun na maghiganti dahil sa mga kasamaang sinapit niya at ng kanyang mga mahal sa buhay ay isang sentral na motibo. Kung ikaw ang nasa sitwasyon ni Simoun, ano ang pinakamahirap na moral na pagpapasya na iyong haharapin sa pagitan ng paghahanap ng katarungan at ang potensyal na pagdulot ng karahasan at inosenteng buhay?','Kung dapat bang magtiwala sa mga taong handang tumulong sa iyong plano.','Kung dapat bang ibunyag ang iyong tunay na pagkatao sa mga kaibigan.','Kung dapat bang gumamit ng marahas na paraan kahit may madamay na inosente.','Kung dapat bang ituloy ang paghihiganti kahit matagal na itong nangyari.','C','Bagama''t ang lahat ng mga pagpipilian ay mayroong bigat moral, ang pagpili na gumamit ng dahas na maaaring magresulta sa kamatayan o pagdurusa ng mga inosenteng tao ang siyang pinakamahirap timbangin.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,38,NULL,'Sa Noli Me Tangere, ang pagmamalupit at pang-aabuso ng mga prayle ay isang malinaw na pangyayari. Sa iyong sariling pananaw at karanasan.ano ang pinakamasamang uri ng pang-aabuso o kawalang-katarungan na iyong nasaksihan o pinaniniwalaang umiiral pa rin sa ating lipunan, na maiuugnay mo sa mga pangyayaring ito?','Kung Ang pagkakaroon ng iba''t ibang opinyon sa politika.','Ang hindi pagkakasundo sa pagitan ng magkakaibigan.','Ang pangungurakot sa gobyerno at pagmamalupit sa mahihirap.','Ang pagkakaroon ng iba''t ibang paniniwala sa relihiyon.','C','Bagama''t ang lahat ng mga pagpipilian ay maaaring magdulot ng hindi pagkakasundo o negatibong epekto, ang pangungurakot at pagmamalupit sa mahihirap ay sumasaklaw sa isang sistematikong pang-aabuso ng kapangyarihan na may malalim at malawakang epekto sa buhay ng maraming tao. Narito ang mga dahilan kung bakit ko ito itinuturing na pinakamasama at maiuugnay sa mga pangyayari sa Noli Me Tangere.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,39,NULL,'Alin sa sumusunod na pahayag ang pinakatamang naglalarawan sa pangunahing ugnayan ng Noli Me Tangere at El Filibusterismo bilang mga nobelang panlipunan?','Ang El Filibusterismo ay isang simpleng pagpapatuloy ng kuwento sa Noli Me Tangere na may parehong layunin at mensahe na kung saan may kaugnayan ang dalawang akda.','Ang Noli Me Tangere ay naglalantad ng mga sakit at depekto ng lipunang Pilipino samantalang ang El Filibusterismo ay nagpapakita ng mga tema ng rebolusyon at paghihiganti.','Ang Noli Me Tangere ay nakasentro lamang sa personal na buhay ng mga tauhan, habang ang El Filibusterismo ay mas nakatuon sa mga isyung pampulitika.','Walang malinaw at hindi direkta ang ugnayan sa pagitan ng dalawang nobela bilang mga akdang panlipunan.','B','Ang Noli Me Tangere ay pangunahing nakatuon sa paglalantad ng iba''t ibang "kanser" o mga sakit ng lipunang Pilipino noong panahon ng kolonyalismong Espanyol. Ang El Filibusterismo, sa kabilang banda, ay isang pagpapatuloy ngunit may ibang tono at layunin. Ito ay nagpapakita ng posibleng maging tugon o resulta ng mga sakit na inilatag sa Noli Me Tangere.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,40,NULL,'Suriin ang representasyon ng iba''t ibang sektor ng lipunang Pilipino sa Noli Me Tangere at El Filibusterismo. Ano ang pangunahing pagkakaiba sa kung paano inilalarawan ang kanilang papel at potensyal sa pagkamit ng pagbabagong panlipunan sa dalawang nobela?','Ang parehong nobela ay nagpapakita ng lahat ng sektor ng lipunan bilang aktibo at may malaking papel sa pagbabago.','Sa Noli Me Tangere, may pag-asa sa papel ng edukadong kabataan samantalang sa El Filibusterismo mas nakasentro sa rebolusyon dahil sa bigo ang mga reporma.','Ang El Filibusterismo ay mas positibo sa papel ng mga prayle sa pagtulong sa pag-unlad ng lipunan kaysa sa Noli Me Tangere na negatibo.','Walang makabuluhang pagkakaiba sa representasyon ng iba''t ibang sektor ng lipunan sa dalawang nobela.','B','Ang pangunahing pagkakaiba ay ang pagbabago sa pananaw tungkol sa paraan ng pagbabago. Sa Noli Me Tangere, mayroong pag-asa sa edukasyon at mapayapang reporma na pangungunahan ng edukadong kabataan. Sa El Filibusterismo, ang pagkabigo ng mga reporma ay humantong sa paniniwala na ang rebolusyon na lamang ang tanging daan, kahit na ito ay may kaakibat na karahasan at panganib sa mga inosente. Ang papel ng edukadong kabataan bilang ahente ng reporma ay nabawasan, at ang pokus ay lumipat sa isang marahas na pag-aalsa. Ang isang infographic tungkol sa mga benepisyo ng pagtatanim ng puno ay gumagamit ng iba''t ibang hugis ng dahon upang kumatawan sa iba''t ibang benepisyo (halimbawa, hugis puso para sa benepisyo sa kalusugan, hugis bilog para sa benepisyo sa kapaligiran, hugis parisukat para sa benepisyong ekonomiko).',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,41,'Ang isang infographic tungkol sa mga benepisyo ng pagtatanim ng puno ay gumagamit ng iba''t ibang hugis ng dahon upang kumatawan sa iba''t ibang benepisyo (halimbawa, hugis puso para sa benepisyo sa kalusugan, hugis bilog para sa benepisyo sa kapaligiran, hugis parisukat para sa benepisyong ekonomiko).','Paano nakatutulong ang paggamit ng iba''t ibang hugis ng dahon sa infographic sa iyong pag-unawa sa iba''t ibang benepisyo ng pagtatanim ng puno na inilalahad sa teksto?','Maaaring makalito ang paggamit ng iba''t ibang hugis at hindi makatulong sa pag- unawa.','Maaaring magsilbing benepisyo na nag-uugnay at nagpapabilis sa pag-unawa at paggunita','Ang paggamit hugis ng dahon ay walang kaugnayan sa kahulugan ng benepi','Maaaring magpakita ito ng iba''t ibang uri ng puno, hindi ng benepisyo.','B','Maaaring magsilbing benepisyo na nag-uugnay at nagpapabilis sa pag- unawa at paggunita. Ang paggamit ng iba''t ibang hugis ng dahon sa isang infographic ay isang visual na diskarte. Nakakatulong ito para mas madaling maunawaan at matandaan ang iba''t ibang benepisyo ng pagtatanim ng puno.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,42,NULL,'Paano maaaring makaapekto ang kulay ng kalangitan sa larawan (madilim at maulap) sa iyong pag-unawa sa mensahe ng artikulo tungkol sa Philippine Eagle?','Maaaring magpahiwatig ito na ang ibon ay masaya at malaya siya sa kanyang pamumuhay.','Maaaring magpahiwatig ito ng panganib, kawalan ng katiyakan, o ang maselang kalagayan ng uri nito.','Walang direktang kaugnayan ang kulay ng kalangitan sa nais na ipaunawa ng teksto.','Maaaring magpahiwatig ito ng kapayapaan at katahimikan sa natural na tirahan ng ibon.','B','Maaaring magpahiwatig ito ng panganib, kawalan ng katiyakan, o ang maselang kalagayan ng uri nito. Sa visual na komunikasyon, ang mga madilim at maulap na kulay sa kalangitan ay karaniwang ginagamit upang magbigay ng emosyon o tono na nagpapahiwatig ng kalungkutan, peligro, o pag-aalala. Sa konteksto ng isang artikulo tungkol sa Philippine Eagle, na kilala bilang isang critically endangered na uri, ang ganitong klaseng larawan ay nagpapalakas sa mensahe ng teksto.',NULL,0,0),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,43,NULL,'Paano maaaring mag-ambag ang matalim na tingin ng karakter sa poster sa pagbuo ng isang stereotipikal na paglalarawan sa kanyang personalidad bilang isang negosyante?','Nagpapakita lamang ito na ang karakter na ginamit ay mayroong magandang mata.','Walang direktang kaugnayan ang paraan ng pagtingin ng mata sa pagbuo ng estereotipo.','Ang matalim na tingin ay nagpapakita na ang karakter ay nangangailangan ng tulong.','Ang matalim na tingin ay maaaring magpahiwatig ng determinasyon, ambisyon, at focus.','D','Ang matalim na tingin ay maaaring magpahiwatig ng determinasyon, ambisyon, at focus,Sa visual na komunikasyon tulad ng mga poster, ang mga ekspresyon ng mukha ay gumaganap ng malaking papel sa pagbuo ng stereotypes o karaniwang paglalarawan. Ang matalim na tingin ay isang pamilyar na visual cue. Karaniwan itong iniuugnay sa mga taong may matinding determinasyon, ambisyon, at focus.',NULL,0,0),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,44,NULL,'Ano ang maaaring maambag ang paggamit ng tipo ng letra sa logo sa poster sa pagpapalakas ng isang stereotipikal na imahe ng isang negosyo o negosyante?','Ang matatapang at anggulo ng mga letra ay maaaring magpahiwatig ng lakas, katatagan, at pagiging direktso','Ang paggamit ng tipo ng ng letra sa logo ay nagpapakita lamang ito ng modernong disenyo.','Nagpapahiwatig na ang paggamit ng tipo ng letra sa logo na ang negosyo ay malapit nang magsara.','Walang kaugnayan ang tipo ng letra sa logo sa pagbuo ng estereotipo.','A','Ang matatapang at anggulong mga letra ay maaaring magpahiwatig ng lakas, katatagan, at pagiging direktso. Ang tipo ng letra (typeface o font) ay isang mahalagang elemento sa disenyo. Mayroon itong kakayahang maghatid ng mensahe at magpahiwatig ng personalidad ng isang tatak o indibidwal, tulad ng isang negosyante.',NULL,0,0),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,45,NULL,'Paano maaaring makaapekto ang kulay ng kape (ginto-kayumanggi) sa iyong pag- unawa sa mensahe ng patalastas?','Maaaring magpahiwatig ito na ang kape ay malamig at hindi masarap.','Maaaring magpahiwatig ito ng kalidad, pagiging mayaman sa lasa','Walang direktang kaugnayan ang kulay ng kape sa pag-unawa sa patalastas.','Maaaring magpahiwatig ito na ang kape ay mura at hindi gaanong kalidad.','B','Maaaring magpahiwatig ito ng kalidad, pagiging mayaman sa lasa. Sa mundo ng advertising, ang mga kulay ay may malaking papel sa pagbibigay ng mensahe. Ang kulay na ginto-kayumanggi (golden-brown) sa isang kape ay isang visual cue na malawakang ginagamit upang iugnay ang produkto sa mataas na kalidad at masarap na lasa.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,46,'Ipagpalagay na nakatanggap ka ng dalawang magkaibang liham opisyal. Ang unang liham ay mula sa Department of Education (DepEd) at ang ikalawang liham ay mula sa isang Non-Governmental Organization (NGO) na nagtataguyod ng karapatan ng kabataan.\n\nLiham mula sa DepEd: Ang logo ay nagtatampok ng isang bukas na aklat, isang sulo, at tatlong bituin na nakaayos sa isang pabilog na disenyo gamit ang mga kulay asul, pula, at dilaw. Ang letterhead ay nakasulat sa pormal na font at naglalaman ng buong pangalan ng departamento, ang kanilang opisyal na website, at address sa isang maayos at simetrikal na pagkakaayos.\n\nLiham mula sa NGO: Ang logo ay nagtatampok ng magkakawak-kamay na mga silweta ng iba''t ibang edad na bumubuo ng isang pabilog na hugis gamit ang mga kulay berde at puti. Ang letterhead ay nakasulat sa isang mas malambot at humanistikong font at naglalaman ng pinaikling pangalan ng organisasyon, ang kanilang slogan, email address, at social media handles sa isang mas impormal at bahagyang naka-kaliwang pagkakaayos.','Paano sinusuri ang paggamit ng mga simbolo sa logo ng DepEd (aklat, sulo, bituin) at paano ito naiuugnay sa pangunahing mandato at layunin ng ahensiya?','Ang mga simbolo na ginamit sa logo ng DepEd ay walang kaugnayan sa edukasyon.','Ang mga simbolo na ginamit sa logo ng DepEd ay kumakatawan lamang sa kasaysayan ng Pilipinas.','Ang mga simbolong ginamit sa logo ng DepEd ay ginamit lamang para sa artistikong disenyo.','Ang mga simbolong ginamit sa logo ng DepEd ay may makabaluhang kahulugan kaugnay sa edukasyon.','D','Ang mga simbolong ginamit sa logo ng DepEd ay may makabuluhang kahulugan kaugnay sa edukasyon. Ang mga simbolo sa logo ay hindi lamang palamuti. Ang bawat isa ay may malalim na kahulugan na sumasalamin sa misyon at bisyon ng isang organisasyon. Sa kaso ng DepEd, ang mga simbolo ay direktang nauugnay sa kanilang pangunahing tungkulin.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,47,'Ipagpalagay na nakatanggap ka ng dalawang magkaibang liham opisyal. Ang unang liham ay mula sa Department of Education (DepEd) at ang ikalawang liham ay mula sa isang Non-Governmental Organization (NGO) na nagtataguyod ng karapatan ng kabataan.\n\nLiham mula sa DepEd: Ang logo ay nagtatampok ng isang bukas na aklat, isang sulo, at tatlong bituin na nakaayos sa isang pabilog na disenyo gamit ang mga kulay asul, pula, at dilaw. Ang letterhead ay nakasulat sa pormal na font at naglalaman ng buong pangalan ng departamento, ang kanilang opisyal na website, at address sa isang maayos at simetrikal na pagkakaayos.\n\nLiham mula sa NGO: Ang logo ay nagtatampok ng magkakawak-kamay na mga silweta ng iba''t ibang edad na bumubuo ng isang pabilog na hugis gamit ang mga kulay berde at puti. Ang letterhead ay nakasulat sa isang mas malambot at humanistikong font at naglalaman ng pinaikling pangalan ng organisasyon, ang kanilang slogan, email address, at social media handles sa isang mas impormal at bahagyang naka-kaliwang pagkakaayos.','Batay sa iyong pagsusuri sa mga elemento at tekstong biswal ng logo at letterhead ng DepEd at ng NGO, alin sa sumusunod na pahayag ang pinakatamang nagbubuod sa pangunahing pagkakaiba sa kanilang biswal na pagkakakilanlan (visual identity) at kung paano ito sumasalamin sa kanilang magkaibang sektor at layunin?','Ang DepEd at NGO ay gumagamit ng parehong estilo ng biswal na pagkakakilanlan upang maging propesyonal.','Ang DepEd ay nagpapakita ng pormal at tradisyonal na biswal samantalang ang NGO ay nagpapakita ng palakaibigan at modernong biswal','Ang ginamit na biswal na pagkakakilanlan ng NGO ay mas nagpapakita ng pagiging propesyonal kaysa sa DepEd.','Walang malinaw na ugnayan sa pagitan ng biswal na pagkakakilanlan at ng sektor o layunin ng organisasyon.','B','Ang DepEd ay nagpapakita ng pormal at tradisyonal na biswal samantalang ang NGO ay nagpapakita ng palakaibigan at modernong biswal. Ang visual identity ng isang organisasyon ay direktang sumasalamin sa kanilang tungkulin, sektor, at layunin. Kung susuriin ang logo at letterhead ng DepEd at isang karaniwang NGO, makikita ang malaking pagkakaiba.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,48,'Binabasa mo ang isang bahagi ng tekstong akademik sa Biology na nagpapaliwanag sa proseso ng photosynthesis. Kasama sa teksto ang isang flowchart na nagpapakita ng iba''t ibang yugto ng proseso, na may mga arrow na nagpapakita ng direksyon ng daloy ng enerhiya at mga materyales.','Paano nakatutulong ang flowchart sa iyong pag-unawa sa proseso ng photosynthesis na inilalahad sa teksto?','Ang paggamit ng flowchart ay maaaring makalito at hindi makatulong sa pag- unawa sa inilahad.','Binibigyan nito ng biswal na representasyon ang pagkakasunod-sunod ng mga yugto at ang mga relasyon.','Ang flowchart ay nagpapakita lamang ng mga pangunahing sangkap ng photosynthesis.','Ang paggamit ng flowchart ay walang direktang kaugnayan sa pag-unawa ng teksto.','B','Binibigyan nito ng biswal na representasyon ang pagkakasunod-sunod ng mga yugto at ang mga relasyon. Ang isang flowchart ay isang uri ng diagram na gumagamit ng mga simbolo at arrow upang ipakita ang daloy o pagkakasunod-sunod ng isang proseso. Sa konteksto ng photosynthesis, na isang kumplikadong proseso ng kemikal, ang flowchart ay isang napakahalagang tool sa pag-unawa.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,49,'Binabasa mo ang isang bahagi ng tekstong akademik sa Biology na nagpapaliwanag sa proseso ng photosynthesis. Kasama sa teksto ang isang flowchart na nagpapakita ng iba''t ibang yugto ng proseso, na may mga arrow na nagpapakita ng direksyon ng daloy ng enerhiya at mga materyales.','Paano nakatutulong ang flowchart sa iyong pag-unawa sa proseso ng photosynthesis na inilalahad sa teksto?','Ang paggamit ng flowchart ay maaaring makalito at hindi makatulong sa pag- unawa.','Binibigyan nito ng biswal na representasyon ang pagkakasunod-sunod ng mga yugto at ang mga relasyon','Ang flowchart ay nagpapakita lamang ng mga pangunahing sangkap ng photosynthesis.','Ang paggamit ng flowchart ay walang direktang kaugnayan sa pag-unawa ng teksto.','B','Binibigyan nito ng biswal na representasyon ang pagkakasunod-sunod ng mga yugto at ang mga relasyon. Ang isang flowchart ay isang diagram na gumagamit ng mga hugis at arrow upang ipakita ang sunud-sunod na daloy ng isang proseso. Sa konteksto ng photosynthesis, isang kumplikadong prosesong biyolohikal, napakahalaga ng flowchart.',NULL,0,0),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,2,50,NULL,'Paano nakatutulong ang talahanayan sa iyong pag-unawa ang mga pagkakaiba sa pagitan ng iba''t ibang uri ng pamahalaan na inilalahad sa teksto?','Mas mahusay na maunawaan ang mga konsepto sa pamamagitan lamang ng teksto.','Ang talahanayan ay nagpapakita at naglalaman lamang ng mga termino at depinisyon.','Organisadong ipinapakita ang mga katangian ng bawat uri ng pamahalaan sa parehong mga kategorya','Maaaring maging nakakalito ang pagtingin sa maraming impormasyon sa isang talahanayan.','C','Organisadong ipinapakita ang mga katangian ng bawat uri ng pamahalaan sa parehong mga kategorya. Ang talahanayan (o table) ay isang epektibong tool sa pag-oorganisa ng impormasyon, lalo na kapag naghahambing ng maraming bagay. Sa konteksto ng pag-aaral ng iba''t ibang uri ng pamahalaan.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,51,'Ang Ibong Adarna ay isang korido na puno ng pantasya at kababalaghan. Karaniwang inilarawan ang mga tagpo gamit ang makukulay na detalye, tulad ng ibong nagbabago ng kulay at kagubatang mahiwaga. Madalas din itong may estereotipong karakter: ang matapang na prinsipe at ang babaeng marikit ngunit tahimik at naghihintay.\n\nSa kabilang banda, ang Florante at Laura, bilang isang awit, ay gumagamit ng mapanlikhang biswal upang mailarawan ang kagubatan, digmaan, at damdamin ng mga tauhan. Narito rin ang estereotipong lalaking mandirigma at babaeng tapat na umiibig.\n\nSamantala, ang Noli Me Tangere at El Filibusterismo ay mga nobelang panlipunan na higit na makatotohanan ang biswal—mga eksena sa simbahan, paaralan, at tahanan. Ang mga estereotipo dito ay panlipunan: ang prayleng mapang-api, ang babaeng konserbatibo, at ang kabataang rebolusyonaryo.','Ano ang pangunahing pagkakaiba ng teknikal na biswal ng Ibong Adarna at Noli Me Tangere?','Ang Adarna ay kathang-isip, habang ang Noli ay makatotohanan','Ang Adarna ay realistiko, habang ang Noli ay pantastiko','Pareho silang pantasya at puno ng kababalaghan','Wala silang pagkakaiba dahil parehong kuwento ng pag-ibig','A','Paliwanag: Ibong Adarna ay puno ng pantasya at makulay na biswal; Noli ay may makatotohanang larawan ng lipunan sa panahon ng mga Kastila.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,52,'Ang Ibong Adarna ay isang korido na puno ng pantasya at kababalaghan. Karaniwang inilarawan ang mga tagpo gamit ang makukulay na detalye, tulad ng ibong nagbabago ng kulay at kagubatang mahiwaga. Madalas din itong may estereotipong karakter: ang matapang na prinsipe at ang babaeng marikit ngunit tahimik at naghihintay.\n\nSa kabilang banda, ang Florante at Laura, bilang isang awit, ay gumagamit ng mapanlikhang biswal upang mailarawan ang kagubatan, digmaan, at damdamin ng mga tauhan. Narito rin ang estereotipong lalaking mandirigma at babaeng tapat na umiibig.\n\nSamantala, ang Noli Me Tangere at El Filibusterismo ay mga nobelang panlipunan na higit na makatotohanan ang biswal—mga eksena sa simbahan, paaralan, at tahanan. Ang mga estereotipo dito ay panlipunan: ang prayleng mapang-api, ang babaeng konserbatibo, at ang kabataang rebolusyonaryo.','Paano naiiba ang estereotipo ng babae sa korido at nobela?','Sa korido, ang babae ay mahinhin at tahimik; sa nobela, madalas ay konserbatibo ngunit may sariling paninindigan','Sa korido, ang babae ay lider; sa nobela, siya ay pasibo','Sa korido, babae ay rebolusyonaryo; sa nobela, siya ay engkanto','Pareho silang babaeng mandirigma','A','Sa korido, ang babae ay kadalasang naghihintay at tahimik; sa nobela, may mga karakter tulad ni Maria Clara na konserbatibo pero may mas malalim na papel sa lipunang kinabibilangan.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,53,'Ang Ibong Adarna ay isang korido na puno ng pantasya at kababalaghan. Karaniwang inilarawan ang mga tagpo gamit ang makukulay na detalye, tulad ng ibong nagbabago ng kulay at kagubatang mahiwaga. Madalas din itong may estereotipong karakter: ang matapang na prinsipe at ang babaeng marikit ngunit tahimik at naghihintay.\n\nSa kabilang banda, ang Florante at Laura, bilang isang awit, ay gumagamit ng mapanlikhang biswal upang mailarawan ang kagubatan, digmaan, at damdamin ng mga tauhan. Narito rin ang estereotipong lalaking mandirigma at babaeng tapat na umiibig.\n\nSamantala, ang Noli Me Tangere at El Filibusterismo ay mga nobelang panlipunan na higit na makatotohanan ang biswal—mga eksena sa simbahan, paaralan, at tahanan. Ang mga estereotipo dito ay panlipunan: ang prayleng mapang-api, ang babaeng konserbatibo, at ang kabataang rebolusyonaryo.','Ano ang epekto ng teknikal na biswal sa pag-unawa ng estereotipo sa apat na akda?','Naglilihim ito ng tunay na mensahe sa totoong pangyayari','Pinatitindi nito ang pagkakakilanlan ng tauhan at tagpuan','Walang kinalaman ang biswal sa estereotipo','Mas pinapaganda lamang nito ang akda','B','Ang teknikal na biswal ay mahalaga upang mailahad ang personalidad at tungkulin ng mga tauhan – nakakatulong ito upang mapalalim ang pag-unawa sa estereotipo.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,54,'MARIANG MAKILING (Kuwentong-bayan mula sa Laguna)\n\nSi Mariang Makiling ay isang magandang diwata na naninirahan sa bundok ng Makiling. Kilala siya bilang tagapagtanggol ng mga mahihirap at matulunging nilalang. Madalas siyang makita na nagbibigay ng pagkain, halamang-gamot, o tulong sa mga nangangailangan. Gayunman, isang araw ay nawala siya matapos siyang traydorin ng mga tao sa nayon — ninakaw nila ang kanyang mga ibinigay o sinungaling silang nagpakabait.\n\nSimula noon, hindi na siya muling nakita. Nanatili ang alamat ni Mariang Makiling bilang simbolo ng kabutihan, katarungan, at paglayo sa kasakiman.','Kung ikaw ay gagawa ng character profile ni Mariang Makiling, alin sa mga aspektong ito ang pinakamahalagang isama?','Ganda ng kanyang bahay at ang daming mga magagarang kasuotan','Ugali, kakayahan, at epekto ng kanyang aksyon sa Lipunan','Bayan na kaniyang pinagmulan at naiambag','Pinagmulan ng lahi at istilo ng kasuotan','B','Ang character profile ay dapat sumasaklaw sa ugali, kakayahan, at papel sa lipunan, hindi lang pisikal.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,55,'MARIANG MAKILING (Kuwentong-bayan mula sa Laguna)\n\nSi Mariang Makiling ay isang magandang diwata na naninirahan sa bundok ng Makiling. Kilala siya bilang tagapagtanggol ng mga mahihirap at matulunging nilalang. Madalas siyang makita na nagbibigay ng pagkain, halamang-gamot, o tulong sa mga nangangailangan. Gayunman, isang araw ay nawala siya matapos siyang traydorin ng mga tao sa nayon — ninakaw nila ang kanyang mga ibinigay o sinungaling silang nagpakabait.\n\nSimula noon, hindi na siya muling nakita. Nanatili ang alamat ni Mariang Makiling bilang simbolo ng kabutihan, katarungan, at paglayo sa kasakiman.','Paano nauugnay ang kabutihan ni Mariang Makiling sa komunikasyong etikal?','Ipinalagay niya sa Facebook ang mga makasalanan','Ipinakita niya na ang tulong ay may hangganan','Pinagsabihan niya ang lahat','Umiiwas na siyang makipag-usap','B','Ang kanyang gawa ay isang di-verbal na komunikasyong may etikang batayan — tumutulong, ngunit alam ang hangganan.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,56,'MARIANG MAKILING (Kuwentong-bayan mula sa Laguna)\n\nSi Mariang Makiling ay isang magandang diwata na naninirahan sa bundok ng Makiling. Kilala siya bilang tagapagtanggol ng mga mahihirap at matulunging nilalang. Madalas siyang makita na nagbibigay ng pagkain, halamang-gamot, o tulong sa mga nangangailangan. Gayunman, isang araw ay nawala siya matapos siyang traydorin ng mga tao sa nayon — ninakaw nila ang kanyang mga ibinigay o sinungaling silang nagpakabait.\n\nSimula noon, hindi na siya muling nakita. Nanatili ang alamat ni Mariang Makiling bilang simbolo ng kabutihan, katarungan, at paglayo sa kasakiman.','Ano ang ugnayan ng pagkawala ni Mariang Makiling sa pananagutan ng mga tao?','Nawala siya dahil pagod na siya sa kanyang paglalakbay','Umalis siya bilang kaparusahan sa pag-abuso ng tiwala','Gusto niya ng bakasyon dahil nauumay na siya','Lumipat siya ng nayon dahil ayaw niya na sa mga tao','B','Bilang tagapagtanggol, ang kanyang pagkawala ay pagpapakita ng konsekwensya ng mga maling gawa.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,57,'MARIANG MAKILING (Kuwentong-bayan mula sa Laguna)\n\nSi Mariang Makiling ay isang magandang diwata na naninirahan sa bundok ng Makiling. Kilala siya bilang tagapagtanggol ng mga mahihirap at matulunging nilalang. Madalas siyang makita na nagbibigay ng pagkain, halamang-gamot, o tulong sa mga nangangailangan. Gayunman, isang araw ay nawala siya matapos siyang traydorin ng mga tao sa nayon — ninakaw nila ang kanyang mga ibinigay o sinungaling silang nagpakabait.\n\nSimula noon, hindi na siya muling nakita. Nanatili ang alamat ni Mariang Makiling bilang simbolo ng kabutihan, katarungan, at paglayo sa kasakiman.','Paano mo mailalarawan ang karakter ni Mariang Makiling bilang modelo ng kabutihang etikal sa modernong panahon?','Matulungin pero marunong humiwalay sa toxic','Mapagbigay ngunit mabilis magalit','Masungit pero matalino','Tahimik at hindi nagpaparamdam','A','Siya ay mapagbigay, ngunit may hangganan – tulad ng modernong ethical behavior na may boundaries.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,58,'MARIANG MAKILING (Kuwentong-bayan mula sa Laguna)\n\nSi Mariang Makiling ay isang magandang diwata na naninirahan sa bundok ng Makiling. Kilala siya bilang tagapagtanggol ng mga mahihirap at matulunging nilalang. Madalas siyang makita na nagbibigay ng pagkain, halamang-gamot, o tulong sa mga nangangailangan. Gayunman, isang araw ay nawala siya matapos siyang traydorin ng mga tao sa nayon — ninakaw nila ang kanyang mga ibinigay o sinungaling silang nagpakabait.\n\nSimula noon, hindi na siya muling nakita. Nanatili ang alamat ni Mariang Makiling bilang simbolo ng kabutihan, katarungan, at paglayo sa kasakiman.','Kung ilalahad mo sa social media ang profile ni Mariang Makiling, anong isasaalang-alang mo?','Respeto sa kanyang simbolismo at mensahe ng panlipunang aral','Gamitin ang pangalan niya para sa kanyang nilalaman.','Walang kailangan – basta i-post','Pampa-viral ang kuwento','A','Ang ethical communication ay nangangailangan ng paggalang sa paksa lalo’t ito ay bahagi ng kultura at aral ng bayan.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,59,'','Habang gumagamit ka ng letterhead sa larawan, napansin mong walang malinaw na pangalan ng institusyon sa ibabaw ng dokumento. Ano ang pinakamainam na gawin bago ipadala ang opisyal na liham?','Gumamit ng ibang letterhead mula sa internet','Idagdag ang tamang pangalan ng institusyon sa letterhead ayon sa opisyal na format','Ipadala na lang ang liham kahit walang pangalan','Gumamit ng simpleng papel na walang letterhead','B','Ang problema sa kakulangan ng impormasyon sa letterhead ay dapat ayusin bago ito gamitin upang mapanatili ang propesyonalismo at pagiging lehitimo ng dokumento.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,60,'','Nakita mo na ang logo sa letterhead ay may mababang resolusyon at lumalabo kapag na-print. Ano ang pinakamabisang solusyon?','Gumamit ng mas makapal na tinta sa pagpi-print','Palitan ng ibang logo na kahawig nito','Humingi ng high-resolution na kopya ng opisyal na logo mula sa tanggapan','Hayaan na lang dahil mababasa pa rin naman ang liham','C','Upang masigurong malinaw at propesyonal ang presentasyon, mahalaga na gumamit ng mataas na kalidad na logo sa letterhead, lalo na para sa mga opisyal na liham.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,61,'','Kung nais mong malaman kung anong font at layout ang opisyal na ginagamit para sa letterhead sa larawan, saan pinakamainam na humingi ng impormasyon?','Sa kaibigan na marunong sa graphic design','Maghanap ng mga template sa internet','Sa opisyal na administrative office o secretariat ng institusyon','Sa ibang paaralan na may kaparehong disenyo','C','Mahalaga na ang impormasyon para sa opisyal na dokumento ay nagmumula sa awtorisadong pinagmumulan upang matiyak ang katumpakan at pagiging opisyal nito.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,62,'','Kung hindi mo alam kung saan dapat ilagay ang petsa sa liham na may ganitong letterhead, ano ang pinakamainam na hakbang upang malaman ang tamang posisyon?','Manghula kung saan ilalagay','Ilagay sa pinakataas ng papel','Magsaliksik o humingi ng sample mula sa opisina bilang gabay','Ilagay sa kahit anong lugar na walang sulat','C','Ang pagsangguni sa aktwal na sample o gabay ay nagpapakita ng kasanayan sa paghahanap ng tamang impormasyon at pagtiyak na susunod sa opisyal na format.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,63,'','Bakit mahalaga na ang lahat ng opisyal na liham ay gumamit ng pare-parehong letterhead tulad ng nasa larawan?','Para maganda tingnan ang lahat ng dokumento','Upang mapanatili ang iisang identidad at kredibilidad ng institusyon','Para mas mabilis matapos ang paggawa ng liham','Para matandaan ng mambabasa ang kulay ng letterhead','B','Ang pare-parehong gamit ng letterhead ay hindi lamang para sa estetika kundi para sa pagpapatibay ng brand identity at tiwala ng publiko sa mga opisyal na komunikasyon.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,64,'Bilang bahagi ng proyekto sa Filipino sa Ikalabindalawang Baitang, ang pangkat ni Joaquin, Trina, at Mario ay naghain ng panukalang pananaliksik na pinamagatang "Epekto ng Social Media sa Akademikong Pagganap ng mga Mag-aaral sa Senior High School ng Paaralang Luntian."\n\nNilalaman ng kanilang panukala ang: • Panimula – dahilan at layunin ng pananaliksik • Kahalagahan ng Pag-aaral – epekto sa mag-aaral, guro, at institusyon • Metodolohiya – survey at pakikipanayam bilang pangunahing pamamaraan • Inaasahang Output – pagsusuri ng ugnayan ng oras sa social media at marka ng mga mag-aaral • Ipinasa nila ang panukala gamit ang Google Docs, at ibinahagi ito sa kanilang email group at Google Classroom, na may maayos na format at wastong citation. Siniguro rin nilang may pahintulot ang mga kalahok sa isasagawang interbyu.\n\nInilahad ng grupo ang kanilang pananaliksik sa klase gamit ang Google Slides, na may malinaw na pagbabahagi ng datos, layunin, at etikal na konsiderasyon.','Bakit mahalagang isaalang-alang ang etikal na kasanayan sa pananaliksik?','Para maprotektahan ang karapatan at privacy ng mga kalahok','Para hindi mapansin ng guro ang pagkakamali','Para magmukhang magaling ang grupo','Para maipasa agad ang papel','A','Ang etikal na kasanayan ay nangangalaga sa dignidad at privacy ng mga kalahok sa pananaliksik.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,65,'Bilang bahagi ng proyekto sa Filipino sa Ikalabindalawang Baitang, ang pangkat ni Joaquin, Trina, at Mario ay naghain ng panukalang pananaliksik na pinamagatang "Epekto ng Social Media sa Akademikong Pagganap ng mga Mag-aaral sa Senior High School ng Paaralang Luntian."\n\nNilalaman ng kanilang panukala ang: • Panimula – dahilan at layunin ng pananaliksik • Kahalagahan ng Pag-aaral – epekto sa mag-aaral, guro, at institusyon • Metodolohiya – survey at pakikipanayam bilang pangunahing pamamaraan • Inaasahang Output – pagsusuri ng ugnayan ng oras sa social media at marka ng mga mag-aaral • Ipinasa nila ang panukala gamit ang Google Docs, at ibinahagi ito sa kanilang email group at Google Classroom, na may maayos na format at wastong citation. Siniguro rin nilang may pahintulot ang mga kalahok sa isasagawang interbyu.\n\nInilahad ng grupo ang kanilang pananaliksik sa klase gamit ang Google Slides, na may malinaw na pagbabahagi ng datos, layunin, at etikal na konsiderasyon.','Paano naipakita ng grupo ang kanilang pananagutan sa akademikong gawain?','Gamitin Pagtatago ng datos upang hindi ito makita ng kanilang mga kaklase','Pagpapasa nang hindi kumpleto at walang batayan na mga panukala','Paggamit ng tamang plataporma, wastong citation, at pagsunod sa gabay','Pagkopya ng mga nakasulat sa internet','C','Ang pagsunod sa format, citation, at pagsumite gamit ang pormal na paraan ay patunay ng pananagutan.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,66,'Bilang bahagi ng proyekto sa Filipino sa Ikalabindalawang Baitang, ang pangkat ni Joaquin, Trina, at Mario ay naghain ng panukalang pananaliksik na pinamagatang "Epekto ng Social Media sa Akademikong Pagganap ng mga Mag-aaral sa Senior High School ng Paaralang Luntian."\n\nNilalaman ng kanilang panukala ang: • Panimula – dahilan at layunin ng pananaliksik • Kahalagahan ng Pag-aaral – epekto sa mag-aaral, guro, at institusyon • Metodolohiya – survey at pakikipanayam bilang pangunahing pamamaraan • Inaasahang Output – pagsusuri ng ugnayan ng oras sa social media at marka ng mga mag-aaral • Ipinasa nila ang panukala gamit ang Google Docs, at ibinahagi ito sa kanilang email group at Google Classroom, na may maayos na format at wastong citation. Siniguro rin nilang may pahintulot ang mga kalahok sa isasagawang interbyu.\n\nInilahad ng grupo ang kanilang pananaliksik sa klase gamit ang Google Slides, na may malinaw na pagbabahagi ng datos, layunin, at etikal na konsiderasyon.','Ano ang epekto ng malinaw na pananaliksik sa tagapakinig?','Nauunawaan at naaalala nila ang mensahe','Naiinip sila sa kailang mga ginagawa','Nalilito sila sa kanilang mga ginagawa','Nawawala ang interes na sumali','A','Ang malinaw na presentasyon ay tumutulong upang maunawaan at matandaan ang nilalaman ng pananaliksik.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,67,'Bilang bahagi ng proyekto sa Filipino sa Ikalabindalawang Baitang, ang pangkat ni Joaquin, Trina, at Mario ay naghain ng panukalang pananaliksik na pinamagatang "Epekto ng Social Media sa Akademikong Pagganap ng mga Mag-aaral sa Senior High School ng Paaralang Luntian."\n\nNilalaman ng kanilang panukala ang: • Panimula – dahilan at layunin ng pananaliksik • Kahalagahan ng Pag-aaral – epekto sa mag-aaral, guro, at institusyon • Metodolohiya – survey at pakikipanayam bilang pangunahing pamamaraan • Inaasahang Output – pagsusuri ng ugnayan ng oras sa social media at marka ng mga mag-aaral • Ipinasa nila ang panukala gamit ang Google Docs, at ibinahagi ito sa kanilang email group at Google Classroom, na may maayos na format at wastong citation. Siniguro rin nilang may pahintulot ang mga kalahok sa isasagawang interbyu.\n\nInilahad ng grupo ang kanilang pananaliksik sa klase gamit ang Google Slides, na may malinaw na pagbabahagi ng datos, layunin, at etikal na konsiderasyon.','Ano ang maaaring kahihinatnan kung hindi isinasaalang-alang ang komunikatibong kasanayan sa presentasyon?','Magiging mas engaging at produktibo ang output nila','Baka hindi maintindihan ang layunin ng pananaliksik','Magiging viral ang ginawang presentasyon','Tataas ang grado','B','Kapag magulo ang pagpapahayag, maaaring hindi maintindihan ang layunin ng panukala.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,68,'Bilang bahagi ng proyekto sa Filipino sa Ikalabindalawang Baitang, ang pangkat ni Joaquin, Trina, at Mario ay naghain ng panukalang pananaliksik na pinamagatang "Epekto ng Social Media sa Akademikong Pagganap ng mga Mag-aaral sa Senior High School ng Paaralang Luntian."\n\nNilalaman ng kanilang panukala ang: • Panimula – dahilan at layunin ng pananaliksik • Kahalagahan ng Pag-aaral – epekto sa mag-aaral, guro, at institusyon • Metodolohiya – survey at pakikipanayam bilang pangunahing pamamaraan • Inaasahang Output – pagsusuri ng ugnayan ng oras sa social media at marka ng mga mag-aaral • Ipinasa nila ang panukala gamit ang Google Docs, at ibinahagi ito sa kanilang email group at Google Classroom, na may maayos na format at wastong citation. Siniguro rin nilang may pahintulot ang mga kalahok sa isasagawang interbyu.\n\nInilahad ng grupo ang kanilang pananaliksik sa klase gamit ang Google Slides, na may malinaw na pagbabahagi ng datos, layunin, at etikal na konsiderasyon.','Paano maaaring mailahad ang pananaliksik sa paraang etikal at makatao?','I-post ito sa social media nang walang paalam at pahintulot','Ipakita ang impormasyon nang may respeto, pag-iingat, at pahintulot','Ipakita ang datos at pangalan ng kalahok kahit walang pahintulot','Gumamit ng memes para maaliw ang audience','B','Ang paggalang sa karapatan ng kalahok at tamang paggamit ng impormasyon ay bahagi ng etikal na pagbabahagi.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,69,NULL,'Paano naipapakita ng pagtatanghal ang ugnayan ng panitikan at pagkakakilanlan ng Pilipino?','Sa pagsasabuhay ng mga positibong katangian ng tauhan sa kultura ng mga Pilipino','Sa paggamit ng dayalogong banyaga kung magsasalita lalo na sa karamihan','Sa paglalantad ng mga masamang asal ng tauhan','Sa paggamit ng mga makabagong salita','A','Sa pagtatanghal ng mga positibong katangian ng tauhan, gaya ni Don Juan, naipapakita rin ang pagpapahalaga sa kaugalian at pagkakakilanlan ng mga Pilipino.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,70,NULL,'Bakit mahalagang isaalang-alang ang etikal na kasanayan sa pagtatanghal na ibinabahagi sa social media?','Para maipakita ang respeto sa akda at sa tagapanood','Para magmukhang magaling ang gumaganap nito','Para may masabi ang audience','Para maging viral','A','Mahalaga ang etikal na kasanayan upang maiwasan ang maling representasyon, mapanatili ang respeto sa orihinal na akda, at pangalagaan ang dignidad ng lahat ng kalahok sa pagtatanghal.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,71,'Ang pangkat ni Althea, Jeric, at Lino mula sa Grade 9 – Luna ay naghanda ng talumpating argumentatibo na pinamagatang “Karangalan at Kabayanihan: Ang Diwa ng Kulturang Pilipino sa Florante at Laura.” Sa kanilang talumpati, binigyang-diin nila ang mga temang katapatan, pag-ibig sa bayan, sakripisyo, at karangalan na makikita sa akda ni Francisco Balagtas. Iginiit ni Althea na hanggang ngayon, ang ganitong mga katangian ay makikita sa mga Pilipinong OFW, frontliners, at ordinaryong mamamayan. Inilahad nila ang talumpati sa harap ng klase gamit ang malinaw na tinig, maayos na kumpas, at epektibong eye contact. Ang video ng kanilang pagbigkas ay ini-upload sa official school YouTube channel, na may tamang title card, citation ng akda, at maayos na deskripsyon. Bago ito ibinahagi, nagsumite sila ng parental consent at sinigurong hindi sila lumabag sa anumang etikal na alituntunin ng paaralan.','Paano naipapakita sa talumpati ang koneksyon ng kulturang Pilipino sa Florante at Laura?','Sa pagbibigay ng mga halimbawa ng kabayanihan at sakripisyo sa kasalukuyan','Sa pagsasalita ng banyagang wika taliwas sa kagustuhan ng lahat.','Sa paghalakhak habang nagbabasa dahil nakauugnay ka sa pangayayari.','Sa pagkopya sa ibang presentasyon nang maging kaaya-aya ang talumpati.','A','Pagbibigay ng halimbawa sa kasalukuyan. Paliwanag: Iniuugnay ng grupo ang mga tema sa Florante at Laura sa mga OFW, frontliners, at mamamayang Pilipino sa kasalukuyan.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,72,'Ang pangkat ni Althea, Jeric, at Lino mula sa Grade 9 – Luna ay naghanda ng talumpating argumentatibo na pinamagatang “Karangalan at Kabayanihan: Ang Diwa ng Kulturang Pilipino sa Florante at Laura.” Sa kanilang talumpati, binigyang-diin nila ang mga temang katapatan, pag-ibig sa bayan, sakripisyo, at karangalan na makikita sa akda ni Francisco Balagtas. Iginiit ni Althea na hanggang ngayon, ang ganitong mga katangian ay makikita sa mga Pilipinong OFW, frontliners, at ordinaryong mamamayan. Inilahad nila ang talumpati sa harap ng klase gamit ang malinaw na tinig, maayos na kumpas, at epektibong eye contact. Ang video ng kanilang pagbigkas ay ini-upload sa official school YouTube channel, na may tamang title card, citation ng akda, at maayos na deskripsyon. Bago ito ibinahagi, nagsumite sila ng parental consent at sinigurong hindi sila lumabag sa anumang etikal na alituntunin ng paaralan.','Bakit mahalaga ang etikal na kasanayan sa pagbabahagi ng talumpati sa social media?','Pagpapalaganap Para dumami ang likes at dumami ang mga magbahagi nito sa social media','Para hindi malabag ang karapatan ng mga kalahok at mapanatili ang kredibilidad','Para maging masaya ang mga manonood','Para makakuha ng sponsors na tutulong sa kanila','B','Ang pagsunod sa etikal na alituntunin, gaya ng paghingi ng pahintulot, ay nagsisiguro ng responsableng pagbabahagi ng nilalaman.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,73,'Ang pangkat ni Althea, Jeric, at Lino mula sa Grade 9 – Luna ay naghanda ng talumpating argumentatibo na pinamagatang “Karangalan at Kabayanihan: Ang Diwa ng Kulturang Pilipino sa Florante at Laura.” Sa kanilang talumpati, binigyang-diin nila ang mga temang katapatan, pag-ibig sa bayan, sakripisyo, at karangalan na makikita sa akda ni Francisco Balagtas. Iginiit ni Althea na hanggang ngayon, ang ganitong mga katangian ay makikita sa mga Pilipinong OFW, frontliners, at ordinaryong mamamayan. Inilahad nila ang talumpati sa harap ng klase gamit ang malinaw na tinig, maayos na kumpas, at epektibong eye contact. Ang video ng kanilang pagbigkas ay ini-upload sa official school YouTube channel, na may tamang title card, citation ng akda, at maayos na deskripsyon. Bago ito ibinahagi, nagsumite sila ng parental consent at sinigurong hindi sila lumabag sa anumang etikal na alituntunin ng paaralan.','Ano ang maaaring maging epekto nang maayos na komunikatibong pagbigkas ng talumpati sa mga tagapakinig?','Boring, walang kabuhay-buhay at mahirap itong intindihin','Mali-mali ang mga interpretasyon na ibinigay','Magkakaroon ng malinaw na pag-unawa at damdaming makabayan','Mawawalan ng interes ang klase','C','Ang maayos na komunikasyon sa pagtalumpati ay nagbubunsod ng mas malalim na pag-unawa sa nilalaman at pagpapahalaga sa kulturang Pilipino.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,74,'Bilang bahagi ng proyekto sa Araling Panlipunan at Filipino, ang mag-aaral na si Angela Dela Cruz ay gumawa ng isang vlog na pinamagatang "Kalayaan at Katarungan: Mga Panawagan Noon at Ngayon".\n\nSa kanyang vlog, inihalintulad niya ang mga usaping panlipunan sa Noli Me Tangere at El Filibusterismo — tulad ng kawalan ng hustisya, panggigipit sa mahihirap, at korapsyon sa simbahan at pamahalaan — sa mga isyu sa kasalukuyan gaya ng red- tagging, paglabag sa karapatang pantao, at disimpormasyon.\n\nIbinahagi ni Angela ang kanyang vlog sa school’s official Facebook page, kalakip ang deskripsyon ng content, citation ng mga sanggunian, at pahintulot ng kanyang mga magulang.\n\nGumamit siya ng malinaw na boses, angkop na wika, at matatag na argumento, habang isinasaalang-alang ang komunikatibong husay at etikal na pagtalakay sa sensitibong isyu.','Bakit mahalagang iugnay ang mga tema ng Noli at El Fili sa mga isyung panlipunan ngayon?','Para ipakita na patuloy pa ring umiiral ang mga hamon sa lipunan','Para makagawa ng trending na mga vlog at mas sumikat pa','Para magmukhang updated ang nobela at napapanahon','Para makakuha ng mataas na views at likes','A','Mahalaga ang pag-uugnay ng mga tema mula sa nobela upang maunawaan na ang mga isyu noon ay may katulad pa ring anyo ngayon, kaya nararapat itong pagtuunan ng pansin.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS1-FIL',3,3,75,'Bilang bahagi ng proyekto sa Araling Panlipunan at Filipino, ang mag-aaral na si Angela Dela Cruz ay gumawa ng isang vlog na pinamagatang "Kalayaan at Katarungan: Mga Panawagan Noon at Ngayon".\n\nSa kanyang vlog, inihalintulad niya ang mga usaping panlipunan sa Noli Me Tangere at El Filibusterismo — tulad ng kawalan ng hustisya, panggigipit sa mahihirap, at korapsyon sa simbahan at pamahalaan — sa mga isyu sa kasalukuyan gaya ng red- tagging, paglabag sa karapatang pantao, at disimpormasyon.\n\nIbinahagi ni Angela ang kanyang vlog sa school’s official Facebook page, kalakip ang deskripsyon ng content, citation ng mga sanggunian, at pahintulot ng kanyang mga magulang.\n\nGumamit siya ng malinaw na boses, angkop na wika, at matatag na argumento, habang isinasaalang-alang ang komunikatibong husay at etikal na pagtalakay sa sensitibong isyu.','Paano ipinakita ni Angela ang etikal na kasanayan sa paggawa ng vlog?','Nagsumite ng pahintulot, gumamit ng citation, at tinalakay ang isyu nang may respeto','Kumuha ng video sa ibang tao nang walang paalam','Gumamit ng viral content at memes para mas astig','Nagpakalat ng impormasyon kahit hindi tiyak ang mga nakalap','A','Ipinakita ni Angela ang etikal na pananagutan sa paglalathala ng sensitibong content sa pamamagitan ng pagsunod sa mga tamang hakbang sa pagbabahagi ng impormasyon. Susing Sagot: Level 1 – Unistructural 1. A 26. B 51. C 2. C 27. A 52. B 3. B 28. D 53. A 4. C 29. B 54. B 5. A 30. B 55. C 6. C 31. B 56. C 7. C 32. D 57. B 8. C 33. C 58. A 9. A 34. C 59. B 10. C 35. A 60. B 11. C 36. C 61. C 12. D 37. C 62. B 13. C 38. C 63. A 14. C 39. B 64. B 15. B 40. B 65. C 16. C 41. B 66. C 17. B 42. C 67. D 18. B 43. A 68. C 19. C 44. D 69. C 20. A 45. B 70. C 21. A 46. D 71. C 22. D 47. D 72. D 23. B 48. C 73. A 24. B 49. C 74. D 25. C 50. D 75. C Susing Sagot: Level 2 – Multi- structural 1. B 26. C 51. A 2. C 27. A 52. B 3. B 28. B 53. C 4. B 29. B 54. B 5. D 30. C 55. C 6. B 31. C 56. C 7. A 32. B 57. B 8. B 33. D 58. B 9. C 34. C 59. A 10. D 35. C 60. A 11. B 36. D 61. A 12. B 37. D 62. C 13. D 38. C 63. B 14. D 39. A 64. A 15. A 40. A 65. B 16. B 41. C 66. B 17. C 42. A 67. B 18. C 43. A 68. A 19. B 44. C 69. B 20. C 45. C 70. A 21. A 46. A 71. B 22. D 47. B 72. A 23. A 48. D 73. A 24. A 49. B 74. B 25. D 50. B 75. A Susing Sagot: Level 1 – Relational & Extended Abstract 1. C 26. C 51. A 2. D 27. C 52. A 3. B 28. B 53. B 4. C 29. B 54. B 5. C 30. B 55. B 6. D 31. B 56. B 7. C 32. D 57. A 8. C 33. B 58. A 9. C 34. C 59. B 10. B 35. B 60. C 11. A 36. B 61. C 12. B 37. C 62. C 13. B 38. C 63. B 14. C 39. B 64. A 15. B 40. B 65. C 16. B 41. B 66. A 17. C 42. B 67. B 18. B 43. D 68. B 19. C 44. A 69. A 20. B 45. B 70. A 21. C 46. D 71. A 22. C 47. B 72. B 23. B 48. B 73. C 24. B 49. B 74. A 25. A 50. C 75. A SANGGUNIAN Anonymous. (2005). Ibong Adarna. Vibal Publishing House. Balagtas, F. (2004). Florante at Laura. Rex Book Store. Balagtas, F. (n.d.). Orosman at Zafira. Bautista, L. (2002). Dekada ''70. Cacho Publishing House. Dela Cruz, J., & Reyes, M. (2023). Ang Epekto ng Programang Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program (4Ps) sa Antas ng Edukasyon at Kalusugan sa Barangay Masagana [Di- nalathalang undergraduate thesis/master’s thesis/dissertation]. Unibersidad ng Pilipinas Diliman. Demetrio, F. R., Cordero-Fernando, G., & Zialcita, F. N. (1991). The Hudhud of Dinulawan and Bugan at Gonhadan. In The Soul Book (pp. 95–102). GCF Books. Rizal, J. (2008). El Filibusterismo. Rex Book Store. (Orihinal na gawa noong 1891) Rizal, J. (2008). Noli Me Tangere. Rex Book Store. (Orihinal na gawa noong 1887) Villanueva, R. O. (1997). Si Mariang Makiling. Adarna House. For inquiries or feedback, please write or call: Office Address: Zone 1 Upper Balulang Cagayan de Oro City Telephone: (088) 881-3137 E-mail Address: region10@deped.gov.ph',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,1,NULL,'Scientific investigation is a systematic process used to explore and answer questions about the natural world. It involves gathering evidence, analyzing information, and drawing conclusions through observation, experimentation, and data collection. Which of the following correctly identifies the first two steps of a scientific investigation?','Collect data and interpret findings','Analyze the results and write a conclusion','Conduct experiments and create a hypothesis','State the aim or problem and list the materials and equipment','D','The first steps in any scientific investigation involve clearly defining the aim or problem that the investigation intends to address. This provides direction and focus for the study. Following this, identifying and listing the necessary materials and equipment ensures proper preparation to conduct the investigation effectively. These steps lay the foundation for a systematic and successful scientific process.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,2,NULL,'The three primary states of matter—solid, liquid, and gas—differ in terms of particle arrangement, energy, and movement. Based on this understanding, answer the following question regarding the states of matter. Which of the following lists correctly describes the three primary states of matter and their characteristics?','Solid (fixed shape and volume), Liquid (fixed volume, takes shape of container), Gas (no fixed shape or volume)','Solid (no fixed shape or volume), Liquid (fixed shape, no fixed volume), Gas (fixed shape and volume)','Solid (take shape of container), Liquid (fixed shape and volume), Gas (fixed volume, no fixed shape)','Solid (no shape, no volume), Liquid (fixed volume, fixed shape), Gas (fixed shape, no volume)','A','The correct characteristics of the states of matter are: solids have a fixed shape and volume, liquids have a fixed volume but take the shape of their container, and gases have neither a fixed shape nor a fixed volume, expanding to fill their entire container. This understanding of the states of matter is essential for exploring various scientific concepts and applications everyday',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,3,NULL,'The periodic table is not only a tool for organizing elements but also a valuable resource for identifying various chemical and periodic properties of elements. Understanding these properties helps in predicting how elements will behave in chemical reactions. Based on this understanding, answer the following question regarding the properties of elements in the periodic table. Which of the following properties typically increases as you move from left to right across a period in the periodic table?','Atomic radius','Electron affinity','Ionization energy','Metallic character','C','As you move from left to right across a period in the periodic table, the ionization energy generally increases. This is because the increasing number of protons in the nucleus creates a stronger positive charge, making it more difficult to remove an electron. Conversely, atomic radius tends to decrease, metallic character decreases, and electron affinity varies, but ionization energy consistently increases across a period.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,4,NULL,'Which of the following best describes the general physical and chemical properties of metals?','Metals are dull and do not reflect light.','Metals exist primarily as gases at room temperature and have low densities.','Metals are brittle, have poor conductors of heat and electricity, and have low melting points.','Metals are malleable and ductile, good conductors of heat and electricity, and have high melting points.','D','o Metals are malleable and ductile, good conductors of heat and electricity, and have high malleability and ductility mean metals can be hammered into sheets or drawn into wires without breaking. o Metals such as copper and silver are excellent conductors of heat and electricity, making them ideal for electrical wiring and cookware. o Most metals have high melting points and are solid at room temperature (except mercury). They also tend to have a lustrous (shiny) appearance, which helps distinguish them from nonmetal.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,5,NULL,'Which of the following statements best describes the general physical and chemical properties of metals?','Metals are soft and break easily.','Metals are dull and do not conduct electricity.','Metals are shiny, conduct heat and electricity, and are usually solid.','Metals are shiny, good conductors of heat and electricity, malleable, ductile, and tend to lose electrons in reactions.','D','Metals are shiny, good conductors of heat and electricity, malleable, ductile, and tend to lose electrons in reactions.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,6,NULL,'A group of students are studying different types of chemical reactions in your chemistry class. Combustion is also a chemical reaction which substance reacts with oxygen. Their teacher asked them to describe important types of chemical reactions, including combination, decomposition, single replacement, and double replacement. Understanding these reactions will help them explain their applications in real life. Which of the following best describes a combustion reaction?','A reaction in which one element replaces another in a compound.','A reaction where a compound breaks down into simpler substances','A reaction where two compounds exchange components to form two new compounds.','A reaction that occurs when a substance reacts with oxygen to produce energy, usually in the form of heat and light.','D','A combustion reaction involves a substance combining with oxygen, resulting in the release of energy, typically as heat and light. Common examples include burning fossil fuels and wood. Options A, B, and C describe other types of reactions (decomposition, single replacement, and double replacement, respectively) and do not accurately represent the characteristics of a combustion reaction.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,7,NULL,'In chemistry class, Jimbo is learning about different types of chemical reactions. Their teacher has provided him with a list of reactions, and his task is to identify the type of each reaction based on its characteristics. Understanding these types will help Jimbo in experiments and real-life applications. Which type of chemical reaction is represented by the following equation: 2H2+O2 → 2H2O?','Decomposition reaction','Double replacement reaction','Single replacement reaction','Synthesis reaction/Combination reaction','D','The given equation represents a synthesis reaction (also known as a combination reaction), where two or more reactants (hydrogen and oxygen) combine to form a single product (water). In a synthesis reaction, elements or simpler compounds combine to form a more complex compound. Options A, B, and C refer to other types of reactions: decomposition involves breaking down a compound, single replacement involves one element displacing another in a compound, and double replacement involves the exchange of components between two compounds.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,8,NULL,'A student is presented with a description of two different organisms. Organism X is described as composed of only one individual cell. Organism Y is described as composed of many cells working together. The student is asked to categorize Organism X based on its cellular structure. Based on the description, Organism X, which consists of a single cell, should be classified as:','Unicellular','Multicellular','Tissue-based','Complex organism','A','The question directly defines the terms "unicellular" and "multicellular" in the initial statement (L1). Organism X is explicitly stated to be composed of a single cell. Therefore, by directly applying the definition provided, Organism X fits the description of a unicellular organism. Multicellular organisms are made up of many cells. "Complex organism" is a broader term that can apply to both unicellular and multicellular organisms. "Tissue-based" organisms are, by definition, multicellular as tissues are groups of similar cells.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,9,NULL,'A student is asked to identify a single organelle that is consistently found in animal cells. Which of the following represents the correct order of these biological levels of organization, starting with the simplest?','organ system → organ → tissue → cell','organ → organ system → cell → tissue','tissue → cell → organ system → organ','cell → tissue → organ → organ system','D','The biological levels of organization are hierarchical, meaning they build upon one another. The simplest level among the choices provided is the cell, the basic unit of life. Similar cells working together form a tissue. Different tissues working together to perform a specific function form an organ. Finally, multiple organs working together to carry out major life functions form an organ system. Therefore, the correct order from simplest to most complex is cell, tissue, organ, and then organ system.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,10,NULL,'Kylen is learning about two types of cell division: mitosis and meiosis. They are given the information that one of these processes results in daughter cells with the same number of chromosomes as the parent cell. The other process results in daughter cells with half the number of chromosomes as the parent cell. The student is asked to identify which process leads to daughter cells with a reduced chromosome number. Which type of cell division results in daughter cells that have half the number of chromosomes as the original parent cell?','Mitosis','Cytokinesis','Meiosis','Binary fission','C','Mitosis is a type of cell division that produces two daughter cells with the same number of chromosomes as the parent cell. 1 This is crucial for growth and repair in multicellular organisms. Meiosis, on the other hand, is a specialized type of cell division that occurs in sexually reproducing organisms 2 to produce gametes (sperm and egg cells). 3 Meiosis reduces the chromosome number by half, ensuring that when fertilization occurs, the resulting zygote has the correct number of chromosomes. 4 Binary fission is a type of cell division used by prokaryotic organisms (like bacteria). Cytokinesis is the final stage of cell division, where the cytoplasm of the parent cell divides to form two separate daughter cells; it 5 occurs after both mitosis and meiosis. Therefore, meiosis is the process that results in daughter cells with a halved chromosome number.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,11,NULL,'Rhoda is learning about the plant transport system. She is given the information that roots absorb water from the soil, and leaves produce sugars through photosynthesis. The student is asked to identify the primary role of the stem in connecting these two processes. Given that roots absorb water and leaves produce sugars, what is the main function of the stem in facilitating the plant transport system?','To anchor the plant in the soil.','To absorb sunlight for photosynthesis','To produce reproductive structures like flowers.','To provide a pathway for the movement of water and sugars between roots and leaves.','D','The plant transport system relies on the coordinated action of the roots, stem, and leaves. Roots absorb water and minerals from the soil. Leaves are the primary sites of photosynthesis, where sugars are produced. The stem acts as the crucial connecting link, containing the vascular tissues (xylem and phloem) that form a continuous transport network throughout the plant. Xylem in the stem transports water and minerals absorbed by the roots upwards to the leaves, while phloem in the stem transports sugars produced in the leaves downwards to the roots and other parts of the plant. Options A), B), and C) describe primary functions of leaves, roots, and sometimes stems (in the case of flowers), respectively, but not the stem''s central role in transport.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,12,NULL,'Roger is learning about the carbon and oxygen cycles in nature. They are given the information that plants take in carbon dioxide from the atmosphere and release oxygen during photosynthesis. Animals, on the other hand, take in oxygen and release carbon dioxide during respiration. The student is asked to identify the primary role of animals in the carbon-oxygen cycle based on this information. Given that plants take in carbon dioxide and release oxygen, what is the main role of animals in the carbon-oxygen cycle?','To absorb water from the soil, which is needed for photosynthesis.','To break down dead organic matter, releasing nutrients back into the soil','To release carbon dioxide back into the atmosphere through respiration.','To provide structural support for plants, allowing them to grow taller and photosynthesize more.','C','The carbon-oxygen cycle involves the movement of carbon atoms through various spheres of the Earth. Plants play a crucial role by removing carbon dioxide from the atmosphere during photosynthesis and incorporating it into organic molecules. Animals, through the process of respiration, break down these organic molecules, releasing carbon dioxide back into the atmosphere. This process balances the carbon dioxide removed by plants.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,13,NULL,'Consider the chemical equation for photosynthesis is; 6CO2 + 6H2 O + Light Energy → C6H12O6 +6O2. A student is learning about the processes of photosynthesis and respiration. They are given the information that one of these processes uses carbon dioxide and water as inputs to produce glucose and oxygen. The student is asked to identify which process utilizes these specific raw materials. Which of the following biological processes uses carbon dioxide and water as its primary raw materials?','Digestion','Respiration','Decomposition','Photosynthesis','D','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to create glucose (a type of sugar) and oxygen. Respiration, on the other hand, uses glucose and oxygen as raw materials to produce carbon dioxide, water, and energy (ATP). Digestion is the breakdown of food into smaller molecules for absorption. Decomposition is the breakdown of dead organic matter. Therefore, photosynthesis is a process that uses carbon dioxide and water as its primary raw materials.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,14,NULL,'A biology class is exploring the factors affecting carrying capacity. Given the definition of carrying capacity as the maximum population size an environment can sustainably support, they are tasked with identifying a primary factor that would directly cause a decrease in an ecosystem''s carrying capacity for a specific herbivore population. Which of the following factors would most directly lead to a reduction in the carrying capacity of an ecosystem for a specific herbivore population?','An increase in the population of their predators.','A decrease in the overall temperature of the ecosystem.','An increase in the reproductive rate of the herbivores.','A decrease in the availability of their primary food source (plants).','D','Carrying capacity is fundamentally limited by the availability of essential resources. For an herbivore population, the primary resource limiting is their food source (plants). If the number of available plants decreases due to factors like drought, disease, or competition from other herbivores, the ecosystem can sustainably support a smaller population of the herbivore. An increase in predators (A) would likely decrease the herbivore population size but not necessarily the carrying capacity of the environment itself (though indirectly it might affect it in the long term). An increase in the herbivore''s reproductive (B) might affect the ecosystem in various ways but is not as direct a limiting factor for herbivores as their food supply (C) would likely lead to exceeding the carrying capacity and subsequent population decline. A decrease in temperature',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,15,NULL,'A Lita is learning about different methods used in food production. They are given the information that one method involves growing plants without soil, using mineral nutrient solutions in a water solvent. Lita is asked to identify the name of this specific food production technique. Which of the following scientific procedures involves growing plants without soil, using nutrient-rich water solutions?','Crop rotation','Hydroponics','Selective breeding','Traditional farming','B','Hydroponics is a method of growing plants using mineral nutrient solutions in water, without soil. This technique allows for precise control over the nutrients available to the plants and can often result in faster growth and higher yields in certain environments. Traditional farming involves growing plants in soil. Selective breeding is a process of choosing organisms with desired traits to breed, aiming to enhance those traits in offspring. Crop rotation is the practice of planting different crops sequentially on the same land to improve soil health and manage pests and diseases. Therefore, hydroponics is the scientific procedure that matches the description of growing plants without soil using nutrient solutions',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,16,NULL,'A child is sitting quietly on a swing. The swing is at rest, and the child is not moving. Which of the following statements best describes the forces acting on the swing?','The swing is experiencing balanced forces because it is at rest','The swing is experiencing balanced forces because it is moving','The swing is experiencing an unbalanced force because it is in motion','The swing is experiencing an unbalanced force because the wind is blowing','A','The swing is experiencing balanced forces because it is at rest o When an object is at rest, it means that all the forces acting on it cancel each other out—they are balanced o In this case, the downward force of gravity pulling the child down is balanced by the upward tension in the swing’s ropes. o Since there''s no motion, and no net force acting on the swing, it''s a classic example of equilibrium. o If the swing were moving or swaying, or if an external force like wind were strong enough to cause motion, that could lead to unbalanced forces—but that’s not the case in this situation.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,17,NULL,'A car is traveling down a straight road and suddenly turns left to avoid an obstacle. What can be concluded about the forces acting on the car during the turn?','The car''s speed decreased because the forces were balanced.','The car''s speed remained constant because it was moving in a straight line.','The forces acting on the car were balanced, causing it to change direction smoothly','The forces acting on the car were unbalanced, resulting in a change in its direction of motion','D','o When the car turns left to avoid an obstacle, it experiences a change in its direction of motion. This change occurs because the forces acting on the car are unbalanced. In order to turn, the car must exert a force that alters its trajectory, which is achieved through steering and the friction between the tires and the road. o The unbalanced forces (the steering force and friction) enable the car to change direction, demonstrating that when forces are not balanced, they can indeed cause a change in an object’s speed or direction of motion. The correct answer highlights this relationship and reinforces the understanding of how unbalanced forces influence motion in real-world scenarios',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,18,NULL,'A jogger runs 4 kilometers north and then 3 kilometers south. What is the distance traveled by the jogger and what is their displacement from the starting point?','Distance: 1 kilometer; Displacement: 3 kilometers north','Distance: 1 kilometer; Displacement: 7 kilometers north','Distance: 7 kilometers; Displacement: 7 kilometers north','Distance: 7 kilometers; Displacement: 1 kilometer north','D','o Distance refers to the total length of the path traveled, regardless of direction. In this case, the jogger runs 4 kilometers north and then 3 kilometers south, resulting in a total distance of 4+3=7; 4+3=7 kilometers. o Displacement, on the other hand, is the straight-line distance from the starting point to the ending point in a specified direction. After running 4 kilometers north and then returning 3 kilometers south, the jogger ends up 1 kilometer north of the starting point. Therefore, the displacement is 1 kilometer to the north. o The correct answer illustrates the distinction between distance (the total path traveled) and displacement (the shortest distance in a specific direction from the starting point), which are key concepts in understanding motion in physics. A cyclist rides 5 kilometers east, then turns around and rides 2 kilometers west',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,19,NULL,'If the force is constant, then acceleration decreases as mass increases. On the other hand, if the force applied to an object is increased of fixed mass, its acceleration increases. According to Newton’s second law of motion, the greater the mass of an object, the more force it takes to achieve the same acceleration. A car accelerates from a stop to a speed of 20 meters per second in 5 seconds. If the mass of the car is 1,000 kilograms, what is the acceleration of the car, and how do the concepts of acceleration and mass relate to each other?','Acceleration is 20 meters per second squared; mass is irrelevant to motion.','Acceleration is 5 meters per second squared; mass has no effect on acceleration.','Acceleration is 4 meters per second squared; mass increases the speed of an object.','Acceleration is 4 meters per second squared; mass affects how quickly an object can change its speed.','D','o Acceleration is 4 meters per second squared; mass affects how quickly an object can change its speed. o To calculate acceleration, we use the formula: o Acceleration = Change in Velocity Time ▪ Acceleration= Time Change in Velocity ▪ In this case, the change in velocity is from 0 m/s to 20 m/s, which is a change of 20 m/s. The time taken for this change is 5 seconds. o Using the formula: Acceleration = 20 m/s 5s= 4m/s2 o Acceleration= 5s 20m/s =4m/s2 o Mass is a measure of the amount of matter in an object, which influences how much force is required to accelerate the object. Thus, mass affects how quickly an object can change its speed, meaning that for a given force, a more massive object will accelerate less than a less massive object. o The correct answer emphasizes the relationship between acceleration and mass, reinforcing the understanding of these fundamental concepts in physics.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,20,NULL,'A metal spoon is placed in a hot cup of coffee. After a few minutes, the spoon feels warm to the touch. Which of the following statements best explains how heat is transferred to the spoon, considering the particle model and the processes of convection and conduction?','The heat is transferred through radiation from the coffee to the spoon','The heat is transferred through convection as the hot water with coffee circulates around the spoon.','The heat is transferred through convection as the spoon moves the coffee around.','The heat is transferred through conduction as the particles in the hot water with coffee collide with the particles in the spoon.','D','o The heat is transferred through conduction as the particles in the coffee collide with the particles in the spoon. o Conduction is the process of heat transfer through direct contact between particles. In this case, the hot coffee contains particles that are moving rapidly due to the heat. When the spoon is placed in the coffee, the faster-moving particles of the coffee collide with the particles of the spoon, transferring thermal energy to the spoon and making it warm to the touch. o The particle model helps explain this process: it illustrates that matter is made up of particles that are in constant motion. When particles collide, energy is transferred, which is how heat moves through conduction. o Convection, on the other hand, involves the movement of fluid (like coffee) itself and the transfer of heat through the bulk motion of that fluid, which is not the primary mechanism at play in this scenario. o Thus, the correct answer highlights the conduction process and the particle model''s role in explaining how heat is transferred to the spoon.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,21,NULL,'A roller coaster car is at the top of a hill before it begins its descent. Which of the following statements accurately describes the concepts of kinetic energy and potential energy in this context?','The roller coaster car has high kinetic energy and low potential energy at the top of the hill.','The roller coaster car has high potential energy and high kinetic energy at the bottom of the hill.','The roller coaster car has high potential energy at the top of the hill and low kinetic energy, which increases as it descends.','The roller coaster car has equal amounts of kinetic and potential energy at all points along the track.','C','o In this scenario, potential energy is the energy stored in the roller coaster car due to its position at the top of the hill. The higher the car is positioned, the more potential energy it has because it has the potential to convert that stored energy into kinetic energy as it moves downward. As the roller coaster car begins to descend, its potential energy decreases while its kinetic energy— the energy of motion—begins to increase. At the top of the hill, the car has low kinetic energy since it is momentarily at rest before it starts moving downwards. As it goes down the hill, the car speeds up, resulting in an increase in kinetic energy. o Option A is incorrect because at the top of the hill, the car has high potential energy, not kinetic energy. Option B is misleading; while the car does have high kinetic energy at the bottom of the hill, it has low potential energy at that point, not at the top. Option D is incorrect because the amounts of kinetic and potential energy change as the roller coaster moves along the track. Thus, the correct answer effectively illustrates the relationship between kinetic and potential energy in a practical context, reinforcing students'' understanding of these fundamental concepts in physics.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,22,NULL,'Eva is conducting a science experiment that involves using electrical equipment. Which of the following practices represents a safe measure for handling electricity during the experiment? A. Wet hands before touching electrical equipment to improve conductivity. B. Use frayed or damaged wires to connect devices, as they are still functional. C. Always ensure that electrical equipment is turned off before making any adjustments or connections.','Wet hands before touching electrical equipment to improve conductivity.','Use frayed or damaged wires to connect devices, as they are still functional.','Always ensure that electrical equipment is turned off before making any adjustments or connections.','Touch the wires to check if electricity is flowing.','C','o Always ensure that electrical equipment is turned off before making any adjustments or connections. o When handling electricity, safety is paramount. The correct answer emphasizes a crucial safety measure: ensuring that all electrical equipment is turned off before making any adjustments or connections. This practice helps prevent electric shocks and accidents that can occur if the equipment is alive while being manipulated. o Option A is dangerous because wet hands can increase the risk of electrical shock. Option B is also unsafe, as using frayed or damaged wires can lead to short circuits or electrocution. Option D is not advisable, as sharing electrical equipment can lead to confusion and potential hazards if multiple users interact with the equipment simultaneously. o By recognizing the importance of turning off electrical equipment before making any changes, the correct answer reinforces the fundamental safety measures needed to handle electricity safely in any experiment or practical application.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,23,NULL,'A science teacher is explaining the concept of electromagnetic radiation to students. Which of the following statements best describes electromagnetic radiation and its characteristics?','Electromagnetic radiation is a type of matter that can only travel through solid materials.','Electromagnetic radiation consists of waves of electric and magnetic fields that travel through space at the speed of light.','Electromagnetic radiation is a form of energy that can only be detected by the human eye.','Electromagnetic radiation is the flow of charged particles through a conductor.','B','o The correct answer accurately describes electromagnetic radiation as a form of energy that propagates through space in the form of waves. These waves are characterized by oscillating electric and magnetic fields that are perpendicular to each other and to the direction of wave propagation. Electromagnetic radiation includes a wide spectrum of wavelengths, from radio waves to gamma rays, all of which travel at the speed of light in a vacuum. o Option A is incorrect because electromagnetic radiation does not require a medium (like solid materials) to travel; it can propagate through a vacuum. Option C is misleading, as it implies that electromagnetic radiation can only be detected by the human eye, whereas many forms, such as radio waves and x-rays, are not visible but can be detected by other means. Option D inaccurately describes electromagnetic radiation as the flow of charged particles, which pertains to electric current rather than wave propagation. o Thus, the correct answer effectively captures the essence of electromagnetic radiation, reinforcing students'' understanding of this fundamental concept in physics.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,24,NULL,'The three primary states of matter—solid, liquid, and gas—differ in particle arrangement, energy, and movement. Which of the following lists correctly identifies the three primary states of matter and their characteristics?','Solid (no shape, no volume), Liquid (fixed volume, fixed shape), Gas (fixed shape, no volume)','Solid (takes shape of container), Liquid (fixed shape and volume), Gas (fixed volume, no fixed shape)','Solid (no fixed shape and volume), Liquid (fixed shape, no fixed volume), Gas (fixed shape and volume)','Solid (fixed shape and volume), Liquid (fixed volume, takes shape of container), Gas (no fixed shape or volume)','D','✓ Solids have particles that are tightly packed in a fixed arrangement. fixed shape and fixed volume ✓ Liquids have particles that are close together but can move past one another. fixed volume but take the shape of their container ✓ Gases have particles that are far apart and move freely. no fixed shape and no fixed volume',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,1,25,NULL,'Atoms are the fundamental building blocks of matter and are essential to understanding chemistry and physics. Describing the basic structure and components of an atom provides insight into how matter behaves and interacts. Based on this understanding, answer the following question regarding the description of atoms. Which of the following statements accurately describes the basic structure of an atom?','An atom consists of a central nucleus made up of electrons, surrounded by protons and neutrons.','An atom is composed of a nucleus containing protons and neutrons, with electrons orbiting around the nucleus at definite energy levels.','An atom has a solid structure with a fixed shape, and it is made entirely of neutrons.','An atom consists of a nucleus filled with electrons, while protons and neutrons float around in an empty space.','B','Option B accurately describes the basic structure of an atom: it is composed of a nucleus that contains protons (positively charged) and neutrons (neutral), with electrons (negatively charged) orbiting around the nucleus in defined energy levels or shells. This understanding is crucial for grasping the principles of atomic theory and the behaviour of matter.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,26,NULL,'Marvie is asked to identify the immediate organizational level that is formed when multiple tissues work together for a common function. Which of the following biological levels of multiple tissues that cooperate to perform a specific set of functions?','Cell','Organ','Biosphere','Organ System','B','The biological levels of organization are interconnected. Cells are the basic units of life. Similar cells with a common function are organized into tissues. When different types of tissues work together to perform a specific job in the body, they form an organ. Multiple organs working together create an organ system, and all living things and their environments collectively form the biosphere. Therefore, the immediate level formed by the cooperation of multiple tissues is an organ.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,27,NULL,'What is the outermost boundary that encloses all the components of a cell and separates it from the external environment?','Nucleus','Organelle','Cytoplasm','Cell Membrane','D','The cell membrane is a semi-permeable barrier that surrounds the cell, maintaining its structural integrity and controlling the passage of substances in and out. It acts as the cell''s protective boundary, separating the internal cell environment from the external surroundings. o The nucleus is just one organelle within the cell that houses genetic material, it''s not the outermost structure. o Organelles are specialized structures inside the cell, each with a distinct function (e.g., mitochondria, ribosomes). o Cytoplasm is the gel-like substance that fills the cell and cushions organelles reside inside the membrane',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,28,NULL,'A student is asked to identify the fundamental molecule that carries the genetic information responsible for the transmission of traits. What is the primary molecule within a cell that contains the instructions for inherited traits?','Lipid','Protein','Carbohydrate','Deoxyribonucleic Acid (DNA)','D','Deoxyribonucleic Acid (DNA) is the molecule that carries genetic information, often referred to as the "blueprint of life." This information is organized into genes, which determine specific traits. Chromosomes are structures within the cell''s nucleus that are made up of tightly coiled DNA. While chromosomes are crucial for the organization and transmission of DNA during cell division, DNA itself is the fundamental molecule that holds the genetic code. Proteins, lipids, and carbohydrates have various other essential functions in the cell but do not primarily carry the inherited genetic information.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,29,NULL,'Adea is asked to identify the two primary types of cell division. They can recall one of the processes. Which of the following represents one of the two main types of cell division?','Mitosis','Budding','Binary fission','Fragmentation','A','The two main types of cell division in eukaryotic organisms are mitosis and meiosis. Mitosis is the process of cell division that results in two daughter cells with identical genetic material. Meiosis is the process of cell division that results in four daughter cells with half the number of chromosomes of the parent cell1 (gametes)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,30,NULL,'Felrod is reviewing the basic components of the digestive system and is asked to identify the primary function of a specific organ. What is the main role of the stomach in the digestive system?','To eliminate solid waste from the body','To produce bile for the digestion of fats.','To absorb most of the nutrients from digested food.','To mechanically and chemically break down food.','D','The stomach is a J-shaped organ in the digestive system that plays a crucial role in the initial breakdown of food. Through muscular contractions (mechanical digestion) and the secretion of acids and enzymes (chemical digestion), the stomach churns and mixes food, breaking it down into a semi-liquid mixture called chyme. Option (A) describes the primary function of the small intestine. Option (B) describes the function of the liver (producing a bile, which is stored in the gallbladder). Option (D) describes the function of the large intestine. Therefore, the main role of the stomach is the mechanical and chemical breakdown of food.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,31,NULL,'Coleen is learning about the interaction between body systems and is asked to identify a key substance that is initially processed by the digestive system and then eliminated by the excretory system. Which of the following represents a primary type of waste product that originates from the digestive system and is eventually removed from the body by the excretory system?','Urea','Sweat','Feces','Carbon dioxide','C','The digestive system takes food and processes it to extract nutrients. The indigestible materials and some metabolic wastes are then eliminated from the body as feces through the large intestine, which is considered part of the excretory system in this context of elimination. Carbon dioxide is a waste product of cellular respiration and is primarily eliminated by the respiratory system. Urea is a nitrogenous waste product formed from the breakdown of proteins and is primarily eliminated by the urinary system (kidneys). Sweat is produced by the integumentary system and eliminates water, salts, and small amounts of urea. Therefore, feces are the primary waste product originating from the digestive system that is eliminated by the excretory system (via the large intestine/egestion)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,32,NULL,'Seth is learning about how traits are passed down in families and is shown a simple pedigree chart. The chart shows a single trait where having at least one copy of a dominant allele results in the expression of that trait. The student is asked to identify what is being tracked in this type of chart. A pedigree chart tracking a simple dominant/recessive characteristic across generations of a family primarily represents the:','Specific DNA sequences of family members.','Environmental factors influencing trait expression.','Number of chromosomes inherited by everyone.','Pattern of how a particular trait appears in each generation','D','A pedigree chart is a diagram that shows the inheritance of a particular trait, genetic disease, or the expression of a specific characteristic across multiple generations of a family. It uses standardized symbols to represent individuals and their relationships and shading or other indicators to show which individuals express the trait being studied. While the underlying cause is the inheritance of alleles (including dominant and recessive ones), the chart itself represents the observed pattern of the trait''s appearance in each generation. Options (A), (B), and (D) refer to the underlying genetic mechanisms, environmental influences, or chromosomal inheritance, which are related but not what the pedigree chart directly represents in terms of observable data.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,33,NULL,'Jovy is learning about mutations and is asked to identify a single, specific environmental factor known to increase the rate of mutations in DNA. Which of the following is a specific environmental factor that can cause an increase in the rate of mutations in DNA?','Regular exercise','A diet rich in antioxidants','Exposure to ultraviolet (UV) radiation.','High levels of glucose in the bloodstream.','C','Mutations are changes in the DNA sequence of an organism. These changes can be caused by various factors, including errors during DNA replication 1 and exposure to certain environmental agents called mutagens. Ultraviolet (UV) radiation from sunlight is a well-known physical mutagen that can damage DNA by causing thymine dimers (bonds between adjacent thymine bases), leading to errors during DNA replication. High levels of glucose, a diet rich in antioxidants, and regular exercise are generally not considered direct causes of DNA mutations, although some may have indirect effects on cellular health.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,34,NULL,'Isaiah is learning about the flow of energy in an ecosystem and is introduced to the concept of a food pyramid. They are asked to identify what each level in this pyramid primarily represents. In a food pyramid, what does each trophic level primarily represent?','The complexity of the organisms'' life cycles.','The total biomass of organisms at that level.','The number of individual organisms at that level','The amount of energy contained within the organisms at that level.','D','A food pyramid (or ecological pyramid) is a graphical representation of the biomass or bio productivity at each trophic level in each ecosystem. 1 However, the fundamental concept of trophic levels is based on the flow of energy. The base of the pyramid represents the producers (plants) that convert sunlight into chemical energy. Each subsequent level represents consumers that obtain energy by feeding on organisms at lower trophic levels. There is a significant loss of energy (like heat) at each transfer, which is why the amount of energy decreases as you move up the pyramid. While biomass and the number of organisms are often related to energy, the trophic levels themselves are defined by the organism''s position in the energy flow. The complexity of life cycles is not the primary representation of trophic levels.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,35,NULL,'Cecil is learning about the classification of living organisms and is introduced to two major systems: the six-kingdom system and the three-domain system. They are asked to identify the primary reason why the three-domain system is considered a more fundamental way to classify life than the six-kingdom system. What is the main reason the three-domain system is considered a more fundamental classification of life than the six-kingdom system?','It is easier for students to memorize.','It was developed more recently by a larger group of scientists','It includes more categories for classifying a wider variety of organisms.','It is based primarily on differences in genetic material (specifically ribosomal RNA)','D','While the six-kingdom system (Archaebacteria, Eubacteria, Protista, Fungi, Plantae, Animalia) is widely used, the three-domain system (Bacteria, Archaea, Eukarya) is considered more fundamental because it reflects the evolutionary relationships between organisms based on key differences in their genetic material, particularly ribosomal RNA (rRNA) sequences. This molecular evidence revealed that Archaea, initially grouped with Bacteria in the kingdom Monera, are more closely related to Eukarya. The three-domain system acknowledges this deeper evolutionary divergence.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,36,NULL,'Maxton is learning about two fundamental biological processes that involve energy transformation in living organisms. They are asked to identify the process that primarily involves the conversion of light energy into chemical energy. Which of the following biological processes is best defined as the conversion of light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose?','Digestion','Respiration','Fermentation','Photosynthesis','D','Photosynthesis is the process used by plants, algae, and some bacteria to convert light energy into chemical energy. This energy is stored in the bonds of glucose (a sugar) that is synthesized from carbon dioxide and water. Respiration is the process where organisms break down glucose (and other organic molecules) to release stored chemical energy in the form of ATP. Digestion is the breakdown of food into smaller molecules for absorption. Fermentation is an anaerobic process that releases energy from glucose without the use of oxygen. Therefore, photosynthesis is the process that specifically involves the conversion of light energy into chemical energy.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,37,NULL,'Analiza is learning about human impacts on ecosystems and is asked to identify one direct negative consequence of deforestation on the animals living in a forest. What is one direct negative effect of deforestation on animal populations within a forest ecosystem?','An increase in the overall number of animal species.','An expansion of available food resources for all animals','An improvement in air quality due to the removal of trees.','A reduction in their habitat and potential loss of shelter.','D','Deforestation, the clearing of forests, directly removes the natural environment that forest animals rely on for survival. Trees provide shelter from predators and the elements, nesting sites, and a structural framework for the ecosystem. When forests are cleared, animals lose their habitat and the shelter it provides, making them more vulnerable to predation, exposure, and displacement. Option (A) is incorrect as deforestation typically leads to a decrease in biodiversity. Option (B) is incorrect because the removal of trees often reduces food sources for many forest animals. Option (C) is incorrect as deforestation generally leads to a decrease in air quality due to the loss of trees that absorb carbon dioxide and release oxygen',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,38,NULL,'Dandy is learning about the field of biotechnology and is asked to identify the core concept that defines this area of study. Which of the following best defines biotechnology?','The study of ancient organisms through fossil analysis.','The engineering of large-scale structures like bridges and buildings.','The branch of physics that deals with the properties of biological molecules.','The use of living organisms or their components to develop products or processes','D','Biotechnology is a broad interdisciplinary field that involves the application of biological systems, living organisms, or derivatives thereof, to make or modify products or processes for specific use. This can include a wide range of applications in medicine, agriculture, industry, and environmental science. Option (A) describes paleontology. Option (C) describes civil engineering. Option (D) is related to biophysics. Therefore, the correct definition of biotechnology is the utilization of biological systems for practical applications.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,39,NULL,'During a science class demonstration, a teacher rolls a ball across the floor. The ball eventually comes to a stop. Which of the following statements best describes the concept of inertia as it relates to the motion of the ball?','The ball maintained its velocity without any forces acting on it.','The ball came to a stop because it had a high amount of inertia.','The ball continued to roll indefinitely because there was no friction acting on it.','The ball’s motion was affected by unbalanced forces, demonstrating inertia.','D','Inertia is the tendency of an object to remain at rest or in motion unless acted upon by an unbalanced force. In this scenario, the ball begins rolling due to an initial force applied by the teacher. However, the friction between the ball and the floor acts as an unbalanced force that opposes its motion. This frictional force ultimately causes the ball to stop.The correct answer highlights the relationship between inertia and the effect of unbalanced forces. While inertia itself is the property that resists changes to motion, the stopping of the ball is a practical demonstration that unbalanced forces (like friction) can overcome inertia, emphasizing the fundamental principle of motion in physics.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,40,NULL,'Rea conducts an experiment where she heats a metal rod at one end and observes the temperature increase along the length of the rod. Which of the following statements best describes heat in the context of this experiment as a transfer of energy?','Heat is the energy that causes the metal rod to expand when it is heated.','Heat is the energy that is stored in the metal rod and is released as it cools.','Heat is a measure of the temperature of the metal rod and does not involve energy transfer.','Heat is the transfer of thermal energy from the hotter end of the rod to the cooler end due to particle motion.','D','In this scenario, heat refers to the transfer of thermal energy from the hot end of the metal rod to the cooler end. This transfer occurs due to the motion of particles within the metal. As the particles at the heated end gain energy, they move faster and collide with adjacent particles, transferring energy along the rod. This process continues until thermal equilibrium is reached, meaning the temperatures along the rod become more uniform. The other options do not accurately describe heat as a transfer of energy. Option A incorrectly states that heat is energy stored in the rod, while option B mischaracterizes heat as a measure of temperature. Option C describes thermal expansion but does not capture the essence of heat as energy transfer. Thus, the correct answer emphasizes the fundamental nature of heat as a transfer of energy due to particle motion.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,41,NULL,'In a typical household, various appliances and systems rely on electricity to function. Which of the following options best identifies common uses of electricity at home and in the community?','Electricity is only used for lighting and cooking in homes.','Electricity is used exclusively in urban areas; rural areas do not utilize electricity','Electricity is primarily used for charging mobile phones and does not have other significant uses.','Electricity powers appliances, heating and cooling systems, entertainment devices, and community infrastructure such as streetlights and hospitals.','D','The correct answer provides a comprehensive view of the diverse applications of electricity in both residential and community settings. In homes, electricity powers various appliances (such as refrigerators, washing machines, and microwaves), heating and cooling systems (like air conditioners and heaters), and entertainment devices (like televisions and computers). Additionally, in the community, electricity is essential for public infrastructure, including streetlights, traffic signals, and hospitals, which rely on electricity for operations, safety, and public services. Option A is incorrect because it limits the use of electricity to only lighting and cooking, ignoring many other essential applications. Option C is misleading, as it suggests that charging mobile phones is the primary use of electricity, overlooking the broader context. Option B is false, as electricity is utilized in both urban and rural areas, with rural areas also benefitting from electrical power for various needs. Thus, the correct answer emphasizes the multifaceted roles of electricity in enhancing everyday life at home and in the community.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,42,NULL,'Divergent boundaries where tectonic plates are pulling apart from each other, often creating new crust and fascinating geological features. Which of the following describes a divergent boundary?','Plates move apart, creating new crust.','Plates slide past each other, causing earthquakes','Plates move toward each other and create mountains.','Plates sink into the mantle, causing volcanic eruptions.','A','Divergent boundaries are characterized by tectonic plates moving away from each other, resulting in the formation of new crust as magma rises. Options B and D describe characteristics of convergent boundaries, while option C describes transformation boundaries.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,43,NULL,'In regions like the Philippines, located along the Pacific Ring of Fire, tectonic activity is particularly pronounced due to its position on multiple plate boundaries. This results in frequent earthquakes, active volcanoes, and unique geological formations, underscoring the immense power and impact of plate tectonics on our planet. Which of the following is a key piece of evidence for tectonic activity in the Philippines?','The abundance of lakes and rivers.','The flat plains are found in central Luzon.','The consistent climate across the islands.','The presence of multiple active volcanoes.','D','Because the presence of multiple active volcanoes in the Philippines is a clear indicator of tectonic activity, particularly associated with subduction zones. Option B is incorrect as flat plains do not indicate tectonic activity. Option A, while lakes and rivers are important geographical features, they do not directly indicate plate boundaries. Option C is incorrect because while the climate may vary, it does not serve as evidence of tectonic activity or plate boundaries.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,44,NULL,'Tides are the regular rise and fall of sea levels caused by the gravitational forces of the Moon and the Sun, as well as Earth''s rotation. Which of the following statements accurately describes the cause of tides?','Tides are caused only by the gravitational pull of the Sun.','Tides happen randomly without any relation to celestial bodies.','Tides occur due to the Earth''s rotation alone, independent of the Moon.','Tides are influenced by the gravitational pulls of both the Moon and the Sun.','D','Tides are indeed caused by the gravitational interactions between the Earth and both the Moon, and the Sun. Option A is incorrect because the Sun''s gravitational pull does affect tides, but the Moon has a more significant impact. Option B is incorrect as tides are not caused by the Earth''s rotation alone; the Moon''s gravitational pull is essential. Option C is incorrect because tides are predictable and directly related to the positions of the Moon and Sun relative to the Earth.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,45,NULL,'The interactions between El Niño and Southern Oscillation is crucial for predicting changes in weather patterns, which can have profound effects on agriculture, water supply and disaster preparedness in various regions around the world. Which of the following statements accurately describes the effects of El Niño and the Southern Oscillation on global weather systems?','They consistently cause dry conditions everywhere.','They have no impact on global weather patterns whatsoever.','They lead to increased rainfall in the western Pacific and drought in the Americas.','They result in wetter conditions in some areas while causing droughts in others.','D','El Niño and the Southern Oscillation are known to create variability in weather patterns, resulting in increased rainfall in certain regions (like the Americas) while causing droughts in others (such as Southeast Asia and Australia). Option A is incorrect because the phenomena do not create dry conditions everywhere; they have varied effects. Option B is incorrect because it misrepresents the locations affected; El Niño typically causes drought in the western Pacific and increased rainfall in the eastern Pacific. Option C is incorrect as these phenomena have significant and well-documented impacts on global weather patterns.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,46,NULL,'Which of the following statements best describes how El Niño and the Southern Oscillation (ENSO) influence global weather systems?','They consistently cause dry conditions everywhere','They have no impact on global weather patterns whatsoever','They result in wetter conditions in some areas while causing droughts in others','They lead to increased rainfall in the western Pacific and drought in the Americas','C','They result in wetter conditions in some areas while causing droughts in others. The El Niño–Southern Oscillation (ENSO) is a climate phenomenon that disrupts typical wind and ocean circulation patterns across the Pacific. During El Niño, warm ocean waters shift eastward, affecting atmospheric dynamics and altering precipitation patterns. These shifts result in flooding in some regions (e.g., western coasts of South America) and severe droughts in others (e.g., Southeast Asia and Australia). Option A and D are incorrect because ENSO events do not produce uniform weather effects nor are they insignificant. Option B is misleading; El Niño tends to reduce rainfall in the western Pacific while increasing it in central and eastern parts of the basin.',NULL,0,0),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,47,NULL,'Understanding the factors that affect typhoons is essential for predicting their formation, intensity, and potential impacts, which can aid in disaster preparedness and response efforts. Which of the following factors is most critical for the development and intensity of typhoons?','Low atmospheric humidity','Flat landforms without obstacles','Cool ocean surface temperatures','Warm ocean surface temperatures','D','Because warm ocean surface temperatures (at least 26.5°C or 80°F) are essential for providing the heat and moisture needed to fuel typhoons. Option A is incorrect because low humidity would hinder, not support, typhoon development. Option B is also incorrect because while flat landforms may not hinder a typhoon, it is the warm ocean temperatures that are critical for the storm''s formation and intensity. Option C is incorrect as cool ocean temperatures do not provide the necessary energy for typhoons.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,48,NULL,'Recognizing the names and symbols of elements in the periodic table is a foundation for understanding chemistry and its applications. This knowledge helps identify common elements and their properties. Based on this understanding, answer the following question regarding the names and symbols of the first 20 elements in the periodic table. Which of the following pairs correctly identifies a common element and its symbol from the first 20 elements of the periodic table?','Gold (Au) and Silver (Ag)','Lithium (Li) and Neon (Ne)','Carbon (C) and Helium (He)','Aluminum (Al) and Calcium (Ca)','C','It identifies two of the first 20 elements in the periodic table: Carbon (C) and Helium (He). Lithium (Li) and Neon (Ne) are also correct, but Aluminum (Al) is not in the first 20 (it is element 13), and Gold (Au) and Silver (Ag) are not from the first 20 elements (Gold is element 79 and Silver is element 47). This question requires students to demonstrate knowledge of elemental symbols and their corresponding names, thus fostering critical thinking about the periodic table.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,49,NULL,'Atoms are made up of a central nucleus and surrounding electron shells. The nucleus contains protons and neutrons, while electrons orbit the nucleus in definite energy levels. Which of the following statements accurately describes this atomic structure?','The nucleus contains only neutrons, while electrons are located randomly throughout the atom without any structure.','The nucleus is made up of electrons only, and protons and neutrons are found in the surrounding electron shells.','The nucleus contains protons and neutrons, while electrons are in the same region as the nucleus.','The nucleus is at the center of the atom, containing protons and neutrons, and the electron shells are concentric circles surrounding the nucleus where electrons are found.','B','This statement correctly identifies the structure of an atom: the nucleus is central and contains protons and neutrons, while electrons occupy shells that surround the nucleus in defined paths or energy levels.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,2,50,NULL,'Metallic bonding, characterized by a "sea of electrons" that are free to move, contributes to various properties such as conductivity, malleability, and ductility. Based on this understanding, answer the following question regarding the properties of metals. Which of the following statements correctly explains why metals are good conductors of electricity?','Metals have tightly bound electrons that do not move, preventing the flow of electricity.','Metals contain no electrons, so they rely on the movement of ions to conduct electricity.','Metals have a fixed arrangement of ions that block the movement of electrons, making them poor conductors.','The structure of metals allows for free-moving electrons, which can carry electric current throughout the metal.','D','Because the structure of metals allows for free-moving electrons, often referred to as a "sea of electrons." This mobility enables metals to conduct electricity efficiently, as the electrons can move freely in response to an electric field. This property is a direct result of metallic bonding, which differs from the bonding in nonmetals and ionic compounds, where electrons are not free to move in the same manner.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('JHS','LS2',1,3,51,NULL,'A solution is a homogeneous mixture composed of two or more substances. In a solution, one substance (the solute) is dissolved in another substance (the solvent). The properties of a solution are uniform throughout, meaning the solute is distributed evenly within the solvent. Common examples include saltwater, where salt (solute) is dissolved in water (solvent), and sugar dissolved in tea. Which of the following best defines a solution in scientific terms?','A chemical reaction that produces gas','A combination of liquids that do not mix','A physical reaction between two solids that forms a new substance','A mixture where one substance is completely dissolved in another','D','A solution in scientific terms, emphasizing that it is a mixture where one substance (solute) is completely dissolved in another (solvent). This distinguishes solutions from other types of mixtures, such as suspensions or emulsions, where components may not be evenly distributed or may separate over time. Options A, C, and C describe different scientific concepts and do not accurately represent the definition of a solution.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,52,NULL,'As part of a science team tasked with analyzing various substances found at home and school, your goal is to identify whether these substances are acids, bases, or salts, and to list their physical and chemical properties. Which of the following pairs correctly matches a substance type with one of its physical or chemical properties?','Bases - Sour taste','Acids - Slippery to the touch','Acids - Turn blue litmus paper red','Salts - Conduct electricity when dissolved in water','C','Acids are known for turning blue litmus paper red, which is a clear indicator of their acidic nature. Option A incorrectly associates bases with a sour taste, which is characteristic of acids. Option B incorrectly describes bases, which feel slippery. Option D, while true that salt can conduct electricity when dissolved in water, does not provide a definitive matching pair of substance types and property as requested. Thus, option C is the only correct match.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,53,NULL,'Jove is observing a science experiment where various substances are mixed together to identify indicators of a chemical reaction. During the experiment, she notices changes in color, the formation of a solid substance at the bottom of the container, and the production of gas bubbles. What do these observations—change of color, formation of precipitates, and release of gas—indicate about the substances involved in the experiment?','The substances are simply evaporating.','The substances are rusting and corroding.','The substances are physically mixed without any change.','A chemical reaction is occurring between the substances.','D','The observations of a change in color, formation of precipitates (solid substances that form when two liquids react), and the release of gas bubbles are all indicators of a chemical reaction. These signs suggest that new substances are being formed as a result of the interaction between the original substances. Option A refers to a physical process rather than a chemical reaction. Option B describes a specific type of chemical change but does not encompass the broader indicators observed, while Option C incorrectly suggests no change is happening.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,54,NULL,'Robert is presented with a partially ordered list of biological levels of organization: cell, organ system, tissue. They are asked to identify the single missing level that fits logically within this sequence. Which of the following biological levels of organization is missing from the sequence? cell → tissue → organ system to create correctly ordered progression from simpler to more complex?','Organ','Molecule','Organelle','Biosphere','A','The biological levels of organization follow a hierarchical structure based on increasing complexity. Starting with the basic unit of life, the cell, similar cells are organized into tissues. Different types of tissues then work together to form an organ, which performs specific functions. Multiple organs that cooperate make up an organ system. Therefore, the missing level that logically fits between tissue and organ system in the given sequence is the organ.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,55,NULL,'Given that mitosis produces genetically identical daughter cells, what is the direct and primary outcome of this process for a multicellular organism''s growth and repair?','Increased genetic diversity among cells.','Creation of specialized cells with altered DNA.','Replacement of damaged cells with genetically different cells.','Production of new cells with the same genetic information as the original cells.','D','Mitosis is a type of cell division that results in two daughter cells, each having the same number and kind of chromosomes as the parent nucleus, typical of ordinary tissue growth because the daughter cells are genetically identical to the parent cell, mitosis serves as the mechanism for increasing the number of cells in an organism for growth while ensuring that the new cells have the same functional capacity as the cells they replace during repair. Option (A) is incorrect because mitosis maintains genetic consistency, not diversity. Option (B) describes cell differentiation, a process often following mitosis but not the direct outcome of the genetic identity produced by mitosis itself. Option (C) is incorrect because repair involves replacing damaged cells with genetically similar cells to maintain tissue function.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,56,NULL,'Given that tissue X transports water upwards from the roots and tissue Y transports sugars throughout the plant, which labeled tissue in the plant stem cross-section is the xylem?','Tissue Y','Tissue X','Both Tissue X and Tissue Y','Neither Tissue X nor Tissue Y','B','The plant transport system consists of two main vascular tissues: xylem and phloem. Xylem is the tissue responsible for transporting water and dissolved minerals upwards from the roots to the rest of the plant. Phloem is the tissue responsible for transporting sugars (produced during photosynthesis in the leaves) throughout the plant. The stem explicitly states that Tissue X transports water upwards. Therefore, Tissue X represents the xylem.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,57,NULL,'Given that habitat destruction reduces the space and resources for survival and reproduction, what is the most direct outcome of extensive habitat loss on the species living in those areas?','Migration of all species to new, suitable environments','Increased genetic diversity within the remaining populations.','Rapid adaptation of all species to the altered habitat conditions','A decrease in population size, potentially leading to extinction.','D','Habitat destruction directly impacts the ability of species to find food, shelter, and mates, and to successfully reproduce. When habitats are lost or severely fragmented, the carrying capacity of the environment for those species decreases significantly. This leads to a decline in population size. If the population shrinks too much, it becomes more vulnerable to other threats like genetic drift, inbreeding, and environmental stochasticity, ultimately increasing the risk of extinction. Option (A) is unrealistic as many species are not capable of migrating effectively or finding suitable new habitats. Option (B) is incorrect because habitat loss usually leads to decreased genetic diversity due to smaller population sizes and isolation. Option (C) is also unlikely as adaptation to drastically altered habitats is a slow process and many species cannot adapt quickly enough to survive rapid habitat loss.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,58,NULL,'A person is pushing a shopping cart down a grocery store aisle. At the same time, a magnet is attracting a metal object on the other side of the aisle. Which of the following statements correctly identifies the types of forces involved in this scenario?','Both the person and the magnet are using contact forces.','Both the person and the magnet are using non-contact forces.','The person is using a non-contact force, and the magnet is using a contact force.','The person is using a contact force, and the magnet is using a non-contact force.','D','In this scenario, the person pushing the shopping cart is applying a contact force, as they physically touch and exert pressure on the cart to move it. This type of force requires direct physical contact between objects. On the other hand, the magnet attracting a metal object is an example of a non-contact force. Non-contact forces, such as magnetic forces, gravitational forces, and electrostatic forces, can act on objects without physical contact. The magnet exerts its force on the metal object from a distance, demonstrating the power of non-contact forces.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,59,NULL,'Imagine a passenger sitting on a bus that suddenly brakes. The passenger lurches forward against the seatbelt. Which statement best explains this behavior in terms of inertia?','The passenger continues moving forward because the bus is accelerating.','The passenger is pushed forward because the seatbelt applies a force on them.','The passenger moves forward because of inertia, which causes them to resist the change in motion.','The passenger flies forward because the bus stops suddenly without any forces acting on them.','C','Inertia is the property of an object that causes it to resist changes in its state of motion. In this scenario, when the bus suddenly brakes, it decelerates rapidly. However, the passenger''s body tends to maintain its state of motion due to inertia, wanting to continue moving forward at the same speed. The seatbelt helps apply a force to counteract this forward motion, but until the seatbelt engages, the passenger feels as if they are lurching forward. This example illustrates the concept of inertia effectively, demonstrating how it affects the behavior of objects in motion when external forces are applied. The correct answer emphasizes the role of inertia in understanding the physics behind every day experiences.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,60,NULL,'A person walks 10 meters east and then turns around and walks 4 meters west. If they are asked to describe their overall journey in terms of distance and displacement, which statement accurately reflects the difference between these two concepts?','Distance is 6 meters; Displacement is 14 meters east.','Distance is 6 meters; Displacement is 10 meters west.','Distance is 10 meters; Displacement is 10 meters east.','Distance is 14 meters; Displacement is 6 meters east','D','Distance refers to the total length of the path traveled, regardless of direction. In this case, the person walks 10 meters east and then 4 meters west, resulting in a total distance of 10 +4 =14; 10+4=14 meter. Displacement, on the other hand, is the straight-line distance from the starting point to the ending point in a specified direction. After walking 10 meters east and then 4 meters back to the west, the person ends up 10 −4 = 6 meters east of their starting point. Therefore, the displacement is 6 meters to the east. The correct answer highlights the distinction between distance (the total path traveled) and displacement (the shortest distance in a specific direction from the starting point), reinforcing the understanding of these fundamental concepts in physics.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,61,NULL,'A chef is cooking pasta in a pot of boiling water on the stove. Which of the following statements correctly identifies the types of heat transfer involved in this cooking process?','Heat is transferred through conduction from the stove to the pot, and then through convection within the water.','Heat is transferred through radiation from the stove to the pot, and then through conduction to the water.','Heat is transferred through convection from the pot to the stove, and then through conduction to the water.','Heat is transferred through conduction from the pot to the stove, and then through radiation to the water.','A','In this scenario, conduction is the process that occurs first when heat is transferred from the stove to the pot. The direct contact between the hot stove and the pot allows thermal energy to move through the metal of the pot, heating it up. Once the pot is heated, convection occurs within the boiling water. As the water at the bottom of the pot heats up, it becomes less dense and rises, while cooler, denser water descends to take its place. This circulation of water transfers heat throughout the pot, cooking the pasta evenly.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,62,NULL,'The Philippine Trench and the Manila Trench are deep ocean features located near the Philippines. These trenches provide geological evidence of a specific tectonic plate boundary interaction. Which tectonic process is primarily responsible for their formation?','Two plates sliding past each other horizontally','Two continental plates colliding and forming mountains','One tectonic plate sinking beneath another','Two oceanic plates moving away from each other','C','The formation of ocean trenches is a classic result of subduction zones, where one tectonic plate sinks beneath another due to convergent boundary activity. Near the Philippines, the Philippine Sea Plate is being forced beneath the Eurasian Plate, creating deep trenches like the Philippine Trench and Manila Trench.This geological interaction causes intense seismic activity and forms extremely deep, narrow depressions in the ocean floor. Choices A and D describe transform and divergent boundaries, which typically form faults and mid-ocean ridges—not trenches. Choice B pertains to continental collision zones like the Himalayas, which produce mountain ranges instead of ocean trenches',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,63,NULL,'A person pushes a heavy box across the floor with a force of 50 newtons for a distance of 3 meters. Which of the following statements best describes the concept of work in this scenario?','No work is done because the box did not move.','Work is done only when the box is lifted off the ground','Work is done only if the force is greater than 50 newtons.','Work is done because a force is applied, and the box is displaced.','D','Work is defined in physics as the product of the force applied to an object and the displacement of that object in the direction of the force. The formula for work is given by: Work = Force× Displacement × cos ⁡(θ) Work=Force×Displacement×cos(θ) where θ θ is the angle between the force and the direction of displacement. In this scenario, the person applies a force of 50 newtons, and the box is displaced by 3 meters. Since the force is applied in the same direction as the displacement (assuming no angle or vertical lifting), work is indeed done. Option A is incorrect because work is done when there is displacement. Option B is also incorrect, as work can occur in horizontal motion, not just vertical lifting. Option C is misleading because work can be done with any amount of force, if there is displacement. Thus, the correct answer emphasizes the relationship between force, displacement, and the concept of work, reinforcing the understanding of this important principle in physics.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,64,NULL,'During a physics lesson, a teacher explains that electricity is fundamentally the flow of electrons. Which of the following statements best illustrates the concept of electricity in terms of electron flow?','Electricity is the transfer of heat energy through materials.','Electricity is the movement of protons through a wire, creating energy.','Electricity is the static charge that builds up on the surface of materials','Electricity is the flow of electrons from a higher concentration to a lower concentration, which creates an electric current.','D','The correct answer accurately describes electricity as the movement of electrons, which are negatively charged particles. In conductive materials, such as metals, electrons can move freely. When there is a difference in electron concentration (voltage) across a conductor, electrons flow from the area of higher concentration (negative side) to the area of lower concentration (positive side), generating an electric current.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,65,NULL,'A health professional is discussing the various types of electromagnetic radiation and their practical applications. Which of the following statements accurately identifies the uses of different types of electromagnetic radiation?','X-rays are used for cooking food, and radio waves are used for diagnostic imaging','Gamma rays are used for communication, while radio waves are used for medical imaging','Radio waves are used primarily for cooking food, while x-rays are used for communication.','X-rays are used in medicine for imaging and diagnosis, while gamma rays are used in radiation therapy and radio waves are used in telecommunications.','D','Gamma rays have the highest energy among electromagnetic waves and are often used in radiation therapy to target and destroy cancer cells. Gamma radiation is also used for sterilizing medical equipment and in nuclear medicine for imaging (e.g., PET scans)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,66,NULL,'When a single lithospheric plate containing both continental and oceanic crust collides with another plate, the likelihood of one type of crust subducting beneath the other is primarily determined by the difference in their...','Surface area','Mineral color','Relative age','Overall density','D','This is the correct answer because overall density is the critical factor that dictates which type of crust will subduct. As previously explained, oceanic crust is denser than continental crust. When a plate containing both types of crust collides with another plate, the denser oceanic portion is more prone to sinking (subducting) beneath the less dense continental portion or even beneath another oceanic plate.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,67,NULL,'The deep ocean trenches found near the Philippines, such as the Philippine Trench and the Manila Trench, are primarily evidence of which tectonic plate boundary process?','One tectonic plate sinking beneath another','Two plates sliding past each other horizontally.','Two oceanic plates moving away from each other','Two continental plates colliding and forming mountains.','A','This is the correct answer because deep ocean trenches are the hallmark of subduction zones, where one tectonic plate is forced to bend downward and slide beneath another plate into the Earth''s mantle. The Philippine Trench is formed where the denser Philippine Sea Plate is subducting beneath the Philippine Mobile Belt. The Manila Trench is formed where the South China Sea Basin is subducting beneath the Philippine Mobile Belt',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,68,'• Answer: A • Explanation: This is the correct answer because deep ocean trenches are the hallmark of subduction zones, where one tectonic plate is forced to bend downward and slide beneath another plate into the Earth''s mantle. The Philippine Trench is formed where the denser Philippine Sea Plate is subducting beneath the Philippine Mobile Belt. The Manila Trench is formed where the South China Sea Basin is subducting beneath the Philippine Mobile Belt • Reference: PHIVOLCS-DOST (Philippine Institute of Volcanology and Seismology). (2020). Active faults and trenches in the Philippines. Department of Science and Technology. https://www.phivolcs.dost.gov.ph','If the main movement along a fault line is vertical, with the rock layer above the fault plane sliding downward relative to the layer below, this type of fault is identified as','Oblique fault','Reverse fault','Normal fault','Strike-slip fault','C','This is the correct answer because a normal fault is specifically defined by the downward movement of the hanging wall (the rock layer above the fault plane) relative to the footwall (the rock layer below the fault plane). This type of movement is a direct result of tensional forces pulling the Earth''s crust apart.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,69,NULL,'When an earthquake begins and you are indoors, the single most important initial safety measure to take to minimize the risk of injury from falling objects is to...','Run outside to an open space.','Stand in a doorway for support.','Immediately find cover under a sturdy object.','Move to the nearest window to see what is happening.','C','This is the correct answer because the primary immediate danger during an earthquake inside a building is being struck by falling objects and debris. Getting under a sturdy object like a desk or table provides crucial protection for your head and body. The "DROP, COVER, and HOLD ON" method emphasizes finding cover as the essential first step.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,70,NULL,'Understanding the relationship between solar energy, atmospheric circulation, and seasonal weather patterns, particularly in the context of monsoons and the ITCZ, is essential for predicting climate-related impacts on agriculture, water resources, and disaster management. How do solar energy and atmospheric circulation influence seasonal weather patterns, particularly regarding monsoons and the ITCZ?','They solely affect temperature without influencing rainfall patterns.','They create static weather patterns that do not change with the seasons.','They ensure uniform weather conditions across the globe regardless of the season.','They drive temperature differences that result in wind patterns, leading to seasonal variations in precipitation.','D','The correct answer is D because solar energy causes temperature differences that drive atmospheric circulation, resulting in seasonal changes in wind patterns and variations in precipitation, such as the heavy rainfall brought by monsoons and ITCZ. Option A is incorrect because these factors influence both temperature and rainfall. Option B is incorrect because solar energy and atmospheric circulation lead to dynamic, changing weather patterns. Option C is incorrect because weather conditions are not uniform around the globe; they vary significantly due to these influences.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,71,NULL,'Understanding the local impacts of global climate change and taking individual actions to mitigate global warming is essential for fostering a sustainable future and protecting local environments. Which of the following actions can individuals take to help reduce the impact of global warming?','Supporting renewable energy and using public transportation','Increasing the use of single-use plastics and driving everywhere.','Ignoring energy efficiency and keeping appliances on all the time.','Disregarding recycling programs and buying products with excess packaging.','C','The correct answer is C because supporting renewable energy and using public transportation are effective ways individuals can reduce their carbon footprint and help mitigate global warming. Option A is incorrect because increasing the use of single-use plastics and driving everywhere contributes to environmental degradation. Option B is incorrect as ignoring energy efficiency and keeping appliances on increases energy consumption and greenhouse gas emissions. Option D is also incorrect because disregarding recycling and buying products with excess packaging contributes to waste and environmental harm.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,72,NULL,'Understanding the factors that affect typhoons is essential for predicting their formation, intensity, and potential impacts, which can aid in disaster preparedness and response efforts. Which of the following statements correctly describes the relationship between bodies of water, landforms, and typhoons?','Typhoons weaken over warm ocean waters and gain strength over land.','Typhoons form only over land and are unaffected by ocean temperatures.','Landforms prevent the formation of typhoons by blocking moisture from ocean sources.','Warm ocean waters provide energy for typhoons, while landforms can disrupt their intensity when making landfall.','D','Because warm ocean waters are essential for the formation and strengthening of typhoons, while landforms can disrupt the storm''s structure and intensity when the typhoon moves onto land. Option A is incorrect because typhoons gain strength over warm waters. Option B is incorrect as typhoons form over warm ocean waters, not exclusively over land. Option C is incorrect because landforms do not prevent typhoons from forming; instead, they can affect the storm''s impact once it makes landfall.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,73,NULL,'The primary factor that explains why oceanic crust lies beneath continental crust at their boundaries. Which of the following characteristics is the main reason oceanic crust typically subducts (sinks) beneath continental crust?','Age','Color','Density','Thickness','C','This is the correct answer because the density difference is the most significant factor determining the behavior of oceanic and continental crust at convergent plate boundaries. Oceanic crust is denser (around 3.0 g/cm³) due to its composition of heavier elements like magnesium and iron. Continental crust is less dense (around 2.7 g/cm³) due to its composition of lighter elements like silicon and aluminum. Because oceanic crust is denser, it "floats" lower on the semi-molten mantle beneath the Earth''s lithosphere. When oceanic and continental plates collide, the denser oceanic crust is forced beneath the less dense continental crust in a process called subduction.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,74,NULL,'Observing a global map, you notice a strong pattern: most of the world''s active volcanoes and major earthquake zones are located. Which of the following is the basis for the global distribution of active volcanoes and earthquake epicenters?','The centers of large continents.','The deep interiors of major ocean basins.','Areas with consistently flat and low-lying land.','The boundaries between oceanic and continental tectonic plates.','D','This is the correct answer because the intense geological activity that produces volcanoes and earthquakes is primarily concentrated at the edges of tectonic plates, where these plates interact. These boundaries often involve the meeting of oceanic and continental crust. Convergent boundaries (where plates collide), especially subduction zones involving oceanic crust, are major sites of both volcanism and earthquakes. Divergent boundaries (where plates move apart) also experience volcanic activity and earthquakes as new crust is formed. Transform boundaries (where plates slide past each other) are characterized by significant earthquake activity.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',1,3,75,NULL,'Considering that the Philippine Fault System is characterized by significant horizontal movement of landmasses, the predominant type of fault observed in the Philippines, based on the direction of its main slip, is most likely','Normal fault','Oblique fault','Reverse fault','Strike-slip fault','D','This is the correct answer because the stem specifically mentions "horizontal movement of landmasses" and the question asks for the "predominant type of fault" based on the main slip. Strike-slip faults are defined by their primary horizontal movement, where rock blocks slide past each other along the fault line. The Philippine Fault System''s major characteristic is this left-lateral strike-slip motion, making this type of fault the most expected and significant in the region due to the ongoing tectonic forces.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,1,NULL,'A group of students is conducting an experiment to measure the volume of different liquids and record their observations in a table. They are using a graduated cylinder marked with milliliters (mL). Which of the following best explains why it is important to use standard units like milliliters (mL) for the measurements?','To ensure that the measurements are random and varied.','To make the results easy to compare with other experiments.','To allow the use of any arbitrary unit that fits their preference.','To avoid using mathematical calculations during the experiment.','B','Using standard units like milliliters (mL) ensures consistency and accuracy in measurements. It allows scientists and researchers to compare results across different experiments and laboratories worldwide. Standardized measurements help avoid confusion and ensure data is reliable, replicable, and universally understood.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,2,NULL,'During an investigation on how temperature affects the dissolving time of sugar in water, students used 50 grams of sugar and 200 mL of water at four temperatures: 30°C, 40°C, 50°C, and 60°C. They measured how long it took for the sugar to dissolve completely at each temperature. Which of the following shows the best way to measure and organize the data accurately?','Using a spoon to estimate sugar and listing the results randomly.','Using a digital scale for sugar but writing the results in a messy chart.','Me Guessing the amount of water and writing the results in a paragraph.','Using a measuring cylinder for water and recording the results in a clear table.','D','Best practice in scientific investigations involves making accurate measurements using standard units and tools, such as a calibrated measuring cylinder for liquid volume and a digital scale for mass. Organizing the collected data systematically (e.g., in tables or charts) ensures clarity and easier analysis. Option B reflects both accuracy in measurement and proper organization of data, fulfilling these criteria.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,3,NULL,'Based on the data, which of the following statements best explains the concepts of accuracy and precision?','The ruler is both accurate and precise because the measurements are close to the actual length and consistent.','All three tools show equal precision and accuracy because the measurements are consistent and close to the actual length.','The laser distance measurer is accurate because its measurements are closest to the actual length but not precise due to variation.','The tape measure is precise but not accurate because the measurements are close to each other but deviate from the actual length.','D','To evaluate accuracy and precision, let''s define both terms: Accuracy: How close the measurements are to the actual value (10.35 cm). Precision: How consistent the measurements are with each other (small variation among repeated values). Let’s analyze each tool: Ruler Measurements: 10.2 cm, 10.3 cm, 10.1 cm Mean: (10.2 + 10.3 + 10.1) / 3 = 10.2 cm Precision: Moderate (range = 0.2 cm) Accuracy: Not very accurate (10.2 is a bit off from 10.35) Tape Measure Measurements: 10.5 cm, 10.2 cm, 10.4 cm Mean: (10.5 + 10.2 + 10.4) / 3 ≈ 10.37 cm Precision: Good (small variation) Accuracy: Close but not very accurate (still slightly off) Laser Distance Measurer Measurements: 10.35 cm, 10.34 cm, 10.36 cm Mean: ≈ 10.35 cm Precision: Very high (variation = 0.02 cm) Accuracy: Very high (matches the actual value)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,4,'Observe the following illustrations, each depicting the particle arrangement and motion in a different state of matter','Which statement correctly describes the arrangement, spacing, and relative motion of particles in solids, liquids, and gases?','In solids, particles are far apart and move quickly. In liquids, particles are tightly packed and vibrate in place. In gases, particles have a fixed arrangement and do not move.','In solids, particles are tightly packed and can move freely. In liquids, particles are arranged randomly and have fixed positions. In gases, particles are very close together and vibrate quickly.','In solids, particles are arranged in a fixed structure and vibrate slightly about their fixed positions. In liquids, particles are close together but can slide past each other. In gases, particles are far apart, move rapidly, and have no fixed shape or volume.','In solids, particles are closely packed together, vibrate in place, and have no space between them. In liquids, particles are far apart, move freely, and fill the shape of their container. In gases, particles are loosely packed, have high energy, and spread out to occupy the entire volume of their container.','C','Solids: o Particles are arranged in a fixed structure (regular pattern). o They vibrate slightly about fixed positions because the strong intermolecular forces keep them locked in place. Liquids: o Particles are close together (slightly less packed than solids). o They can slide past each other, allowing liquids to flow and take the shape of their container while keeping a fixed volume. Gases: o Particles are far apart with a lot of empty space between them. o They move rapidly in all directions because they have high kinetic energy. o They have no fixed shape or volume and expand to fill any container.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,5,'Observe the following illustrations, each depicting the particle arrangement and motion in a different state of matter','A student observes particles under a simulation: Observation 1: Particles vibrate in place and keep their shape. Observation 2: Particles slide past one another and take the shape of their container. Observation 3: Particles spread out to fill the entire space and move very fast. Which statement best explains the relationship between particle arrangement and motion in these observations?','Particle arrangement has no effect on motion.','Tighter arrangement allows sliding; looser arrangement causes vibration only.','Tighter arrangement means faster movement; looser arrangement means slower movement.','Tighter arrangement limits movement to vibrations; looser arrangement allows more freedom of motion.','D','In Observation 1, particles vibrate in place because they are closely packed in a solid. The strong forces between them restrict their movement. In Observation 2, particles slide past each other because liquids have medium particle spacing, allowing them to move more freely than solids but still stay close together. In Observation 3, particles move rapidly and spread out because gases have very wide spacing and very weak forces between particles, allowing maximum movement. This matches the idea that more spacing between particles = more freedom of motion.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,6,'Observe the following illustrations, each depicting the particle arrangement and motion in a different state of matter','Based on the diagram provided, which choice correctly matches the labels M, N, and O to the three states of matter?','M – Gas, N – Solid, O – Liquid','M – Solid, N – Liquid, O – Gas','M – Liquid, N – Gas, O – Solid','M – Gas, N – Liquid, O – Solid','A','M – Gas: o Gas particles are far apart with a lot of empty space between them. o They move rapidly and randomly in all directions, which is why arrows point outward in different directions. N – Solid: o Solid particles are tightly packed in a regular, fixed arrangement. o They do not move from their positions but vibrate slightly, showing very little motion. O – Liquid: o Liquid particles are close together but not in a fixed pattern. o They can slide past one another, which allows liquids to flow and take the shape of their container.',NULL,0,0),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,7,'The Particle Model of Matter is a fundamental concept in understanding the nature of substances and their behaviors in different states. It describes matter as being composed of tiny particles, and explains how their arrangement, movement, and interactions determine the properties of each state.','The Particle Model of Matter helps us understand how matter behaves. Which statement shows basic ideas of this model?','All particles stay still and do not have energy.','Matter is made of particles that are all the same and do not touch or affect each other.','Particles in solids, liquids, and gases are arranged and behave in exactly the same way.','Different kinds of matter have particles with different sizes, shapes, and arrangements. These differences affect their properties.','D','o The Particle Model of Matter explains how all matter is made up of tiny particles and how their arrangement, movement, and spacing determine the state and behavior of the material (solid, liquid, or gas). o Solids have tightly packed particles. o Liquids have particles that are close but move past each other. o Gases have particles that are far apart and move freely. Differences in arrangement and movement explain differences in shape, compressibility, and flow.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,8,'The Particle Model of Matter is a fundamental concept in understanding the nature of substances and their behaviors in different states. It describes matter as being composed of tiny particles, and explains how their arrangement, movement, and interactions determine the properties of each state.','The Particle Model of Matter helps us understand how particles behave in solids, liquids, and gases. What basic idea does it give about gases compared to solids and liquids?','Gas particles are bigger than solid and liquid particles, so they cannot fill any space.','Gas particles are packed closely and only shake in place, while particles in solids and liquids move freely.','Gas particles do not move and do not take up space, while solid and liquid particles are always moving.','Gas particles are far apart and move rapidly, allowing them to fill their container; liquid particles are close together but can slide past each other; solid particles are tightly packed and fixed in place.','D','Gases → The Particle Model of Matter states that gas particles have large spaces between them and move very quickly in all directions. This allows gases to expand and completely fill the shape and volume of any container. Liquids → Liquid particles are still close together but not fixed in place. They can slide past one another, which is why liquids can flow and take the shape of their container while keeping a fixed volume. Solids → Solid particles are tightly packed in a fixed arrangement. They cannot move from their positions, but they can vibrate in place, which is why solids have a fixed shape and volume.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,9,'Changes of state in matter are essential concepts in understanding how substances transition between solid, liquid, and gas phases. These transitions involve changes in particle arrangement and energy. The following questions explore these concepts in detail. Based on your understanding, answer the questions below regarding the changes of state from solid to liquid to vapor, and vice versa.','When matter changes from solid to liquid to gas, what happens to the particles?','They stay packed and fixed.','They stay the same and lose energy.','They gain energy and move farther apart.','They lose energy and move closer together','C','Particles gain energy as the state changes from solid → liquid → gas. This makes them move more and spread out: o Solid: tightly packed, vibrate in place. o Liquid: move around more freely. o Gas: move fast and spread far apart.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,10,'Changes of state in matter are essential concepts in understanding how substances transition between solid, liquid, and gas phases. These transitions involve changes in particle arrangement and energy. The following questions explore these concepts in detail. Based on your understanding, answer the questions below regarding the changes of state from solid to liquid to vapor, and vice versa.','During the transition from a solid to a liquid, how does the arrangement and behavior of particles change?','Particles become compressed and lose energy.','Particles stay in fixed positions but vibrate faster.','Particles become tightly packed and stop moving.','Particles become less orderly and can slide past one another.','D','When a substance transitions from a solid to a liquid (melting), heat energy is absorbed. This causes the particles to: o Gain energy and move more freely. o Break out of their fixed positions in the solid structure. o Become less orderly, allowing them to slide past each other—which is why liquids can flow and take the shape of their container.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,11,'Changes of state in matter are essential concepts in understanding how substances transition between solid, liquid, and gas phases. These transitions involve changes in particle arrangement and energy. The following questions explore these concepts in detail. Based on your understanding, answer the questions below regarding the changes of state from solid to liquid to vapor, and vice versa.','When matter changes from vapor to liquid to solid, which of the following options correctly describes multiple independent true facts about the particles?','Particles do not change their energy or arrangement during the phase changes.','Particles gain energy when vapor turns into liquid and move farther apart; particles stay loose in solid.','Particles lose energy but stay far apart when vapor becomes liquid; particles gain energy and move freely when liquid freezes.','Particles lose energy when vapor turns into liquid; particles get closer together; particles lose more energy when liquid freezes; particles become tightly packed and fixed in solid.','D','o Energy change: Particles lose energy as matter cools from vapor liquid solid. o Arrangement: Particles become closer together and more fixed with each phase change. o Vapor: Particles are far apart and move freely. o Liquid: Particles are closer, but still move around. o Solid: Particles are tightly packed in a fixed structure.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,12,NULL,'A chef places a block of butter in a hot pan. After a few minutes, the butter changes from a hard, solid block into a smooth liquid that spreads across the pan. The chef explains that heat energy affects the motion of particles in matter. Based on the scenario, which statement correctly describes both the change in state and the particle behavior of the butter?','The butter undergoes condensation; particles slow down and move closer together.','The butter undergoes freezing; particles lose energy and vibrate in fixed positions.','The butter undergoes evaporation; particles spread far apart and fill the space available.','The butter undergoes melting; particles gain energy and move past one another more freely.','D','When the solid butter is heated, heat energy is absorbed by its particles. This increases the particles’ kinetic energy, causing them to vibrate more and weaken the forces holding them in fixed positions. Once enough energy is gained, the particles can break free from their fixed structure and slide past each other, which is the liquid state. This change from solid to liquid is called melting. The key idea is that the state changes and the particle movement changes at the same time.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,13,'The periodic table is a systematic arrangement of elements, organized into 7 periods and 18 groups. This organization is based on the atomic structure of the elements and their chemical properties, including reactivity. Understanding this arrangement helps us predict the behavior of elements and their interactions. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the periodic table.','What is the primary reason elements are arranged in groups (columns) in the periodic table?','Elements in the same group have similar atomic masses.','Elements in the same group have the same number of neutrons in their nuclei.','Elements in the same group have identical physical properties regardless of their atomic structure.','Elements in the same group have similar chemical properties and reactivity due to the same number of valence electrons.','D','Elements in the same group have the same number of valence (outer) electrons, which determines how they bond and react chemically. o Example: Group 1 elements (alkali metals) all have 1 valence electron → very reactive. o Group 17 (halogens) all have 7 valence electrons → very reactive non- metals.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,14,'The periodic table is a systematic arrangement of elements, organized into 7 periods and 18 groups. This organization is based on the atomic structure of the elements and their chemical properties, including reactivity. Understanding this arrangement helps us predict the behavior of elements and their interactions. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the periodic table.','How does the arrangement of elements into periods (rows) in the periodic table reflect their atomic structure?','Elements in the same period are all metals.','Elements in the same period have identical electron configurations.','Elements in the same period have the same number of protons in their nuclei.','Elements in the same period have increasing atomic numbers, and their electrons occupy the same main energy level, with the number of valence electrons increasing across the period','D','The arrangement of elements into periods reflects their atomic structure, as elements in the same period have increasing atomic numbers and correspond to the principal energy levels of their electrons. As you move from left to right across a period, the number of protons and electrons increases, influencing the elements'' properties.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,15,NULL,'Maria accidentally spilled salt (NaCl) on the table while cooking. She wonders how the salt is formed. What happens to sodium (Na) and chlorine (Cl) atoms to create NaCl?','Sodium and chlorine share electrons equally to form a covalent bond.','Sodium and chlorine do not exchange electrons but form a hydrogen bond.','Sodium loses one electron to become Na+, and chlorine gains one electron to become Cl-. They form an ionic bond.','Sodium gains one electron to become Na−, and chlorine loses one electron to become Cl+. They form a metallic bond.','C','Sodium (Na) has 1 valence electron. It loses that electron to become Na⁺ (a positively charged ion). Chlorine (Cl) has 7 valence electrons. It gains 1 electron to complete its outer shell, becoming Cl⁻ (a negatively charged ion). These oppositely charged ions attract each other, forming a strong ionic bond—that’s how NaCl (table salt) is created.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,16,NULL,'During a science activity, Mark is asked to explain why the formula for Magnesium Chloride is MgCl2. What is the reason?','Magnesium and Chlorine share electrons equally.','Magnesium and Chlorine do not exchange electrons but form a hydrogen bond.','Magnesium loses two electrons, and two Chlorine atoms each gain one electron.','Magnesium gains two electrons, and two Chlorine atoms each lose one electron.','C','Magnesium Chloride has the chemical formula MgCl₂ because of how the atoms form ionic bonds: o Magnesium (Mg) is a metal with two electrons in its outer shell. To become stable, it loses both electrons, forming a Mg²⁺ ion. o Chlorine (Cl) is a non-metal with seven electrons in its outer shell. Each chlorine atom needs one more electron to become stable, so each gains one electron, forming Cl⁻ ions. To balance the charges: o 1 Magnesium atom loses 2 electrons → Mg²⁺ o 2 Chlorine atoms each gain 1 electron → 2 Cl⁻ This results in MgCl₂, a neutral compound with balanced charges.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,17,'In her chemistry class, Jessa is tasked to identify the chemical formula of an unknown cleaning agent. Laboratory analysis shows that each molecule of the compound contains one nitrogen atom and three hydrogen atoms. To figure out the formula, she must recall: • The symbols for nitrogen and hydrogen from the periodic table. • How to write a chemical formula based on the number of atoms. • The standard order for writing chemical symbols in a formula.','Using the information above, what is the correct chemical formula for the compound?','NH3','N3H','H3N','NH4','A','o Step 1 – Identify symbols: Nitrogen → N, Hydrogen → H. o Step 2 – Determine the ratio: 1 nitrogen atom and 3 hydrogen atoms means the subscript 3 goes after H. o Step 3 – Apply correct formula writing rule: In chemical formulas, the more electropositive element (nitrogen in this case) is written first, followed by hydrogen. o Step 4 – Combine: N + H₃ → NH₃, which is ammonia.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,18,NULL,'While working on a science project about different metals, Carlo observes a piece of stainless steel in his kitchen. He notices that it has a shiny surface and has stayed in good condition for years without showing any signs of rust, even after frequent contact with water. He recalls that some metals have special properties that prevent them from corroding or rusting easily. Which property does it likely to have?','High ductility','High density','Low conductivity','Corrosion resistance','D','If a metal is shiny and does not rust easily, it likely has corrosion resistance — the ability to withstand damage caused by oxidation or chemical reactions with the environment. Rusting is a form of corrosion, especially common in metals like iron when exposed to oxygen and moisture. Metals like aluminum, stainless steel, and gold are known for their corrosion resistance, which helps them stay shiny and durable over time.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,19,'The solute is the substance that is dissolved, while the solvent is the substance that dissolves the solute. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the comparison of solutes and solvents.','Which of the following correctly describes the primary role of a solute in a solution?','The solute is always a liquid in a solution.','The solute is the substance that dissolves a solvent to form a solution.','The solute is the substance that is dissolved in a solvent to form a solution.','The solute is the component of a solution that determines the color and viscosity.','C','Option C is correct because the solute is defined as the substance that is dissolved in a solvent to form a solution. This is a fundamental aspect of solutions, where the solute is present in a lesser amount compared to the solvent.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,20,'The solute is the substance that is dissolved, while the solvent is the substance that dissolves the solute. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the comparison of solutes and solvents.','In a saltwater solution, which statement accurately describes the roles of the solute and solvent?','Both salt and water are solutes in the solution.','Salt acts as the solvent while water acts as the solute.','Water acts as the solute while salt acts as the solvent.','Salt is the solute that is dissolved in water, which acts as the solvent.','D','Option D is correct because in a saltwater solution, salt is the solute that dissolves in water, which serves as the solvent. This distinction highlights the relationship between solutes and solvents in forming a homogeneous mixture.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,21,'Felrod is conducting a study on the physical and chemical properties of acids, bases, and salts. This exploration will help you develop a deeper understanding of these substances and how they behave in various contexts. Felrod''s task is to identify and classify their properties.','Which of the following is a common physical property of acids?','They have a sour taste.','They feel slippery to the touch.','They turn red litmus paper blue.','They produce hydroxide ions in solution.','A','Acids have several physical and chemical properties. Among the choices, the common physical property is: o They have a sour taste. o This is a physical property commonly associated with acids. Examples include Citric acid in lemons and Acetic acid in vinegar. They all have a sour flavor, which is a distinguishing physical trait.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,22,'Felrod is conducting a study on the physical and chemical properties of acids, bases, and salts. This exploration will help you develop a deeper understanding of these substances and how they behave in various contexts. Felrod''s task is to identify and classify their properties.','Which of the following statements accurately describes a chemical property of bases?','A base has a pH lower than 7.','A base turns red litmus paper blue.','A base tastes bitter and feels slippery.','A base reacts with an acid to make salt and water.','D','o This is a chemical property because it describes how a base reacts with another substance (an acid). o The reaction is called neutralization: Acid+Base→Salt+Water Example: HCl (acid)+NaOH (base)→NaCl (salt)+H2O (water)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,23,NULL,'Why do scientists write chemical equations in both word form and formula form when describing chemical reactions?','To make the equations longer and more complicated.','To ensure that the reactions are more interesting to read.','To confuse those who are not familiar with chemical reactions.','To provide clarity and detail for different audiences and applications.','D','Scientists write chemical equations in both word form and formula form to serve different purposes: Word Form: o Descriptive and easy to understand. o Useful for beginners, students, or general audiences. o Example: Hydrogen reacts with oxygen to form water. Formula Form (Chemical Equation): o Precise and compact. o Shows the exact chemical substances involved using their chemical symbols and formulas. o Useful for scientists, engineers, and in laboratory work. o Example: 2H2+O2→2H2O',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,24,NULL,'Which of the following statements best explains how the combustion of fossil fuels impacts both natural and built environments?','Combustion does not affect built environments, only natural ecosystems.','Combustion is a clean process that has no significant environmental impact.','Combustion of fossil fuels primarily benefits plant growth by providing carbon dioxide.','Combustion releases pollutants that can harm air quality and contribute to climate change, affecting both ecosystems and human health.','D','The combustion of fossil fuels is a major source of air pollutants, including carbon dioxide, sulfur dioxide, and nitrogen oxides, which can degrade air quality and contribute to climate change. This process impacts natural environments by affecting ecosystems and wildlife, as well as human health through respiratory issues.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,1,25,NULL,'Which of the following pairs correctly identifies an organelle unique to plant cells and an organelle with a substantially different primary role in plant cells compared to animal cells, along with a brief description of their key functions in each cell type?','Cell Wall (plant: structural support; animal: absent) and Ribosomes (plant: protein synthesis; animal: protein synthesis).','Centrioles (plant: absent in most; animal: cell division) and Nucleus (plant: genetic control; animal: genetic control).','Chloroplasts (plant: photosynthesis; animal: absent) and Mitochondria (plant: energy production; animal: energy production).','Chloroplasts (plant: photosynthesis; animal: absent) and Large Central Vacuole (plant: storage, turgor; animal: small, varied storage/transport).','C','Chloroplasts are organelles unique to plant cells (and some algae) and are responsible for photosynthesis, the conversion of light energy into chemical energy. They are absent in animal cells. The Large Central Vacuole is a prominent organelle in mature plant cells, occupying a significant portion of the cell volume. Its primary roles include storage of water, nutrients, and waste products, as well as maintaining turgor pressure, which provides structural support to the plant cell. Animal cells have vacuoles as well, but they are typically smaller, more numerous, and have more varied roles such as storage and transport, but not the central role in maintaining turgor pressure seen in plants.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,26,NULL,'In an ALS science class, Teacher Noel asks his students to imagine planting a mango seed from a tree in their backyard. A few years later, the new mango tree grows and produces fruit. Some fruits taste like the parent tree’s mangoes, but some are slightly different in sweetness and size. He explains that, just like plants, humans inherit traits from their parents through DNA in chromosomes. During the formation of egg and sperm cells, a process called meiosis shuffles genetic material, making each offspring unique while still sharing similarities with their parents. Which of the following statements best explains how the roles of DNA and chromosomes during sexual reproduction result in the transmission of traits, leading to both similarities and differences between parents and offspring?','DNA, organized into genes on chromosomes, is duplicated during mitosis in the parents’ somatic cells. These duplicated chromosomes are then directly passed to the offspring through fertilization, creating a mix of parental traits.','DNA replication ensures that each parent’s exact genetic information is copied and passed directly to each offspring, resulting in offspring being genetically identical to one parent. Chromosomes then randomly mutate, causing slight differences.','Chromosomes contain proteins that directly determine traits. During fertilization, the number of chromosomes doubles, leading to new combinations of traits in the offspring. DNA’s role is only in maintaining the structural integrity of the chromosomes.','DNA carries the genetic code organized into genes. During meiosis, homologous chromosomes pair up and exchange genetic material (crossing over), creating unique combinations of alleles. These recombined chromosomes are then distributed into gametes, and fertilization combines the genetic information from two parents.','D','This answer correctly integrates multiple key concepts: o DNA as the carrier of genetic code: It accurately states that DNA holds the instructions for traits in the form of genes. o Chromosomes as organizers of DNA: It acknowledges that DNA is organized into chromosomes. o Meiosis and genetic recombination (crossing over): It highlights meiosis as the specialized cell division that produces gametes and correctly identifies crossing over as a crucial process that shuffles genetic material between homologous chromosomes, leading to new combinations of alleles. o Haploid gametes: It implicitly understands that meiosis results in gametes with half the number of chromosomes. o Fertilization: It correctly describes fertilization as the fusion of two gametes, combining the genetic information from both parents. o Resulting in similarities and differences: This process explains why offspring inherit traits from both parents (leading to similarities) but also have unique combinations of alleles due to crossing over and the random assortment of chromosomes during meiosis (leading to differences).',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,27,NULL,'Maria is studying the digestive system and the different processes involved in breaking down food and absorbing nutrients. She is asked to explain how mechanical processing and secretion work together to facilitate the subsequent stages of digestion and absorption in the alimentary canal. Which of the following best explains how mechanical processing and secretion contribute to the overall process of digestion and absorption in the digestive system?','Secretions, including enzymes, are the primary means of physically fragmenting food through chemical reactions. Mechanical processing then mixes these chemically broken-down particles, allowing for efficient absorption in the large intestine.','Secretions mainly lubricate the passage of large food boluses through the esophagus. Mechanical processing then occurs primarily in the large intestine to compact indigestible material for elimination, with minimal impact on nutrient absorption.','Mechanical processing, like chewing and churning, physically breaks down food into smaller pieces, increasing the surface area for enzymatic action. Secretions, such as saliva and stomach acid, primarily function to transport these smaller food particles along the digestive tract.','Mechanical processing increases the surface area of food, allowing secretions containing enzymes to more effectively break down complex molecules into simpler ones through chemical digestion. These simpler molecules are then more readily absorbed across the lining of the digestive tract.','D','This answer correctly integrates the roles of mechanical processing and secretion in facilitating digestion and absorption: o Mechanical Processing (e.g., chewing, churning): Physically breaks down large food particles into smaller ones. o Increased Surface Area: This smaller particle size significantly increases the surface area available for enzymatic action. o Secretion (e.g., saliva, stomach acid, enzymes): Introduces fluids containing enzymes (for chemical digestion), acids (to denature proteins and aid enzyme activity), and other substances that chemically break down complex molecules (carbohydrates, proteins, fats) into simpler ones. o Enhanced Chemical Digestion: The increased surface area due to mechanical processing allows these secreted enzymes to work more efficiently. o Facilitated Absorption: The resulting simpler molecules (e.g., monosaccharides, amino acids, fatty acids) are small enough to be absorbed across the lining of the small intestine into the bloodstream or lymphatic system. o Elimination: While not directly addressed in the interaction between mechanical processing and secretion for digestion/absorption, the remaining indigestible material eventually moves to the large intestine for water absorption and elimination.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,28,'A physiology lab assistant, preparing a report on human homeostasis, is investigating how the digestive and excretory systems collaborate. To understand this interaction, they are considering two key aspects: (1) the origin of materials that the excretory system eliminates and (2) how the processing of materials by the digestive system makes elimination by the excretory system possible.','Which of the following is the primary source of the waste materials that the excretory system ultimately removes from the body?','Intake of oxygen by the respiratory system.','Breakdown of food by the digestive system.','Movement of muscles by the muscular system.','Regulation of hormones by the endocrine system.','B','The digestive system breaks down food, absorbing usable nutrients. The remaining indigestible materials and some metabolic wastes processed by the liver and moved into the digestive tract become part of the waste that the excretory system (specifically the large intestine for solid waste) eliminates.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,29,'A physiology lab assistant, preparing a report on human homeostasis, is investigating how the digestive and excretory systems collaborate. To understand this interaction, they are considering two key aspects: (1) the origin of materials that the excretory system eliminates and (2) how the processing of materials by the digestive system makes elimination by the excretory system possible.','How does the digestive system prepare materials in a way that facilitates their elimination by the excretory system (specifically considering solid waste)?','It filters waste products directly from the blood into the intestines.','It converts toxic substances into harmless gases that are exhaled.','It absorbs water from indigestible material, forming more solid waste.','Digestive: Transports nutrients to cells; Excretory: Balances pH levels in the blood.','C','After nutrients are absorbed in the small intestine, the remaining indigestible material moves to the large intestine. The large intestine absorbs water from this material, concentrating it into a more solid form (feces) that is then eliminated by the body, a key function of the excretory system in removing solid waste. •',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,30,NULL,'Sarah is learning about how different organ systems help keep the body in balance. She notices that both the digestive and excretory systems involve removing substances from the body, but in different ways. She needs to explain how each system works to maintain the body’s internal stability (homeostasis). How do the digestive and excretory systems contribute to maintaining homeostasis in the human body?','Digestive: Breaks down food; Excretory: Filters blood to remove toxins.','Digestive: Produces enzymes; Excretory: Regulates body temperature.','Digestive: Carries oxygen to cells; Excretory: Helps digestion by making enzymes.','Digestive: Absorbs food nutrients; Excretory: Removes liquid waste from the body.','D','The digestive system breaks down food into smaller molecules that can be absorbed and used by the body for energy and growth. The excretory system filters blood to remove waste products, such as urea, and maintains the body''s chemical balance by eliminating toxins through urine. Together, these systems ensure the body processes nutrients efficiently and removes harmful substances, contributing to overall homeostasis.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,31,NULL,'Maria is growing a tomato plant in her backyard. She notices that the leaves are turning yellow and the plant looks weak. She wonders how the leaves, stem, and roots work together to keep the plant healthy. Which of the following correctly explains their interconnected roles in the plant''s transport system?','The stem pumps water from the roots to the leaves, and the leaves release extra water while the stem stores food.','The roots make food for the plant and send it to the leaves, while the leaves absorb water and send it to the roots.','The roots hold the plant in place and take in sunlight, while the stem moves air between the leaves and the outside.','The leaves take in carbon dioxide and make food, which is sent to the roots for storage, while the roots take in water and minerals and send them to the leaves','D','The leaves absorb carbon dioxide and use sunlight to make food (sugars) through photosynthesis. sugars are transported down the stem to the roots for storage and energy. The roots absorb water and minerals from the soil, which are transported up the stem to the leaves to help with photosynthesis.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,32,'Ms. Jane''s learners are studying basic genetics. They understand that individuals inherit genes from their parents, resulting in specific genetic makeup. To demonstrate a more comprehensive understanding of how these genes are expressed and observed as traits, the learners need to connect the specific genetic combinations to the visible characteristics, considering how some genetic factors can mask others.','Which of the following statements correctly describes the relationship between genotype and phenotype?','Phenotype directly dictates the genetic information (genotype) that an organism can pass on to its offspring.','Genotype refers to the observable traits of an organism, while phenotype is the specific set of genes it possesses.','Genotype and phenotype are interchangeable terms that both describe the physical appearance of an organism.','Genotype is the underlying genetic makeup of an organism, which determines its observable characteristics, the phenotype.','D','The genotype is the internal genetic code – the specific alleles an organism has. The phenotype is the external, observable expression of that genetic code – the physical or biochemical characteristics that result from the genotype interacting with the environment.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,33,'Ms. Jane''s learners are studying basic genetics. They understand that individuals inherit genes from their parents, resulting in specific genetic makeup. To demonstrate a more comprehensive understanding of how these genes are expressed and observed as traits, the learners need to connect the specific genetic combinations to the visible characteristics, considering how some genetic factors can mask others.','Which of the following genotypes results in a tall plant when ''T'' is dominant for tallness and ''t'' is recessive for shortness?','Only the genotype with two dominant alleles (TT)','Only the genotype with two recessive alleles (tt)','Both genotypes with at least one dominant allele (TT and Tt)','Only the genotype with one dominant and one recessive allele (Tt)','C','In genetics, dominant alleles mask the effect of recessive alleles when both are present in a genotype. • T = dominant allele for tallness • t = recessive allele for shortness There are three possible genotypes: 1. TT → Homozygous dominant → Tall 2. Tt → Heterozygous → Tall (because the dominant allele "T" masks the "t") 3. tt → Homozygous recessive → Short So, both TT and Tt are tall plants because at least one T (dominant) is present.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,34,'A group of students are learning about bacteria in their science class. Their teacher explains that some bacteria in a polluted river have developed the ability to break down a harmful chemical that was recently introduced into the water. The teacher says this change might be due to a genetic alteration in the bacteria. The students are asked to think about what kind of change could have caused this new ability.','What fundamental change within the bacteria most likely explains their ability to break down the harmful chemical?','An increase in the production of proteins in the bacteria’s cytoplasm.','A change in the overall energy use of all the bacteria in the population.','A temporary adjustment in the bacteria’s behavior to deal with the chemical.','A change in the sequence of nucleotides in the bacteria’s DNA or chromosomes that can be passed on to future generations.','D','When bacteria develop a new ability, like breaking down a harmful chemical, the most likely fundamental cause is a genetic mutation or change in their DNA. This change: Alters the sequence of nucleotides in their genes. Can lead to the production of a new or modified protein, such as an enzyme that breaks down the harmful chemical. Is heritable, meaning it can be passed to future generations if it provides a survival advantage.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,35,'A group of students are learning about bacteria in their science class. Their teacher explains that some bacteria in a polluted river have developed the ability to break down a harmful chemical that was recently introduced into the water. The teacher says this change might be due to a genetic alteration in the bacteria. The students are asked to think about what kind of change could have caused this new ability.','Considering the scenario, which of the following factors present in the bacteria''s environment could have plausibly increased the likelihood of mutations occurring that enabled the breakdown of the synthetic pollutant?','A sudden decrease in the availability of their traditional food source.','Exposure to low levels of a new antibiotic that does not directly kill them.','Maintaining a stable and optimal growth temperature for the bacteria.','The presence of a bacteriophage that occasionally inserts its genetic material into the bacterial chromosome.','D','Mutations in bacteria can be caused or accelerated by environmental factors that affect their DNA. One of the most direct and plausible causes of genetic mutation is the involvement of bacteriophages — viruses that infect bacteria. Why D is correct: o Bacteriophages sometimes insert their own genetic material into the bacterial DNA, a process called lysogeny. o This can disrupt existing genes or introduce new genes, leading to mutations. o These mutations can sometimes result in new traits, such as the ability to break down a synthetic pollutant. o These genetic changes can be inherited by bacterial offspring.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,36,NULL,'During a community gardening project, ALS learners observe that many plants (like vegetables and grasses) have stopped growing in a nearby area due to a lack of sunlight and water. Their teacher asks how this change might affect the food pyramid in that small ecosystem, especially for the insects, chickens, and people who rely on those plants. If the number of producers in an ecosystem decreases, what is the most likely effect on the food pyramid?','The consumers will get more energy','There will be no effect on energy flow','More energy will be available at all levels','The energy flow to higher trophic levels will decrease','D','In a food pyramid, producers (like plants and algae) form the base. They capture energy from the sun through photosynthesis and provide energy to all other organisms in the ecosystem. If the number of producers decreases: o Less energy is captured and stored at the base. o Primary consumers (herbivores) will have less food, leading to reduced energy intake. o This effect cascades upward, so secondary and tertiary consumers (carnivores and top predators) also receive less energy. Since energy decreases as it moves up each trophic level (only about 10% is passed on), any reduction at the base greatly impacts the top.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,37,'Jane and her classmates are exploring the classification of animals during a science lesson. Their teacher explains that humans belong to the Class Mammalia, which includes animals such as dogs, cats, and whales. The class is tasked with identifying the unique features that distinguish mammals from other groups like reptiles, birds, and amphibians. Jane is curious about the specific traits that classify humans as mammals.','Which characteristic is unique to mammals and helps classify humans in the Class Mammalia, distinguishing them from reptiles, birds, and amphibians?','Being cold-blooded and laying eggs in water','Having lungs for breathing and a four-chambered heart','Giving birth to live young and having scales on their skin.','Producing milk to nourish their young and having hair or fur.','D','Humans are classified as mammals, and the features that uniquely distinguish mammals from reptiles, birds, and amphibians include: o Mammary glands: Mammals produce milk to feed their young. o Hair or fur: All mammals have some form of hair or fur at some point in their lives. These characteristics are exclusive to mammals and are not found in reptiles, birds, or amphibians.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,38,'Jane and her classmates are exploring the classification of animals during a science lesson. Their teacher explains that humans belong to the Class Mammalia, which includes animals such as dogs, cats, and whales. The class is tasked with identifying the unique features that distinguish mammals from other groups like reptiles, birds, and amphibians. Jane is curious about the specific traits that classify humans as mammals.','Building upon their classification as mammals, which of the following traits is a defining characteristic of the Order Primates, setting humans apart from other mammals?','Lungs for respiration and a closed circulatory system.','Sharp claws and specialized teeth for a carnivorous diet.','The ability to regulate body temperature and having a four-chambered heart.','Forward-facing eyes, highly developed brains, and hands with opposable thumbs.','D','Humans belong to the Order Primates, a group within the Class Mammalia. What sets primates apart from other mammals are the following defining characteristics: o Forward-facing eyes → Provide binocular vision, which helps with depth perception. o Highly developed brains → Support advanced problem-solving, social behavior, and learning. o Opposable thumbs → Allow grasping and manipulating objects, a key feature in tool use and complex tasks.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,39,NULL,'Which of the following traits, beyond being warm-blooded and having hair, are unique to mammals and help classify humans in this group?','Having scales for protection and being cold-blooded.','Laying eggs with hard shells and having a three-chambered heart.','Producing milk to nourish their young and having a diaphragm for breathing.','Possessing feathers for insulation and breathing through gills during early development.','C','In addition to being warm-blooded and having hair, mammals — including humans — share unique characteristics that set them apart from other animal groups: o Mammary glands: Mammals produce milk to feed their young — a defining trait of the group. o Diaphragm: A muscular structure that aids in efficient breathing by separating the chest and abdominal cavities. This feature is exclusive to mammals.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,40,NULL,'In an ALS community garden project, learners plant vegetables like pechay and tomatoes. The facilitator explains how these plants grow using sunlight, air, and water. One learner asks, “Where does the air go when plants and humans breathe?” The teacher then draws a simple flowchart on the board to show how both plants and animals play key roles in the carbon and oxygen cycle. Which of the following correctly describes a primary role of both plants and animals in either the carbon, oxygen, or water cycle, as would be depicted in a flowchart or labeled diagram?','Both plants and animals absorb significant amounts of water from the soil through their root systems.','Plants primarily consume water during transpiration, while animals primarily release water through excretion.','Both plants and animals primarily release carbon dioxide into the atmosphere through the process of photosynthesis.','Plants primarily release oxygen as a byproduct of photosynthesis, while animals primarily consume oxygen during cellular respiration.','D','Plants (Photosynthesis): Plants take in carbon dioxide from the atmosphere and water, using sunlight to produce glucose (sugar) for energy. Oxygen is released as a byproduct of this process, making it a crucial contribution to the oxygen cycle. Animals (Cellular Respiration): Animals consume organic matter (directly or indirectly from plants) and use oxygen to break down these molecules to release energy. Carbon dioxide is released as a byproduct of cellular respiration, contributing to the carbon cycle. Option A is incorrect because plants take in carbon dioxide for photosynthesis.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,41,NULL,'After a rainy day, ALS learners notice that the soil is moist, and leaves are wet. The teacher asks: “Did you know that plants also release water into the air?” Then, using simple drawings, the teacher explains how water moves through living things in the water cycle. Considering the roles of plants and animals in the water cycle, which of the following accurately describes a key difference in their primary contributions to the movement of water within this cycle, as illustrated in flowcharts and labeled diagrams?','Plants primarily return water to the atmosphere through transpiration, while animals primarily return water to the ground through decomposition.','Animals primarily absorb water from the atmosphere through respiration, while plants primarily release water into bodies of water through root exudation.','Plants primarily absorb water from the soil through their roots, while animals primarily release water back into the environment through respiration, excretion, and perspiration.','Animals primarily store large quantities of water within their tissues, significantly slowing down the overall cycle, while plants facilitate rapid water movement from the soil to the atmosphere.','C','Plants (Absorption and Transpiration): Plants absorb water from the soil through their roots, a crucial step in the water cycle''s movement from the ground to living organisms and eventually back to the atmosphere through transpiration (evaporation from leaves). Animals (Consumption and Release): Animals obtain water by drinking and consuming food. They then release water back into the environment through various processes, including respiration (water vapor in exhaled breath), excretion (urine and feces), and perspiration (sweat). Option C accurately contrasts the primary uptake of water by plants and the primary ways animals release it back into the environment.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,42,NULL,'Photosynthesis and cellular respiration are fundamental biological processes, both involving energy transformation. They are interconnected, with the products of one serving as the reactants for the other. Photosynthesis: Occurs in plants, algae, and some bacteria: • 6 CO2+6 H2O+light energy→C6H12O6+6 O2 Plants use carbon dioxide (CO₂) and water (H₂O), with the help of sunlight, to produce glucose (C₆H₁₂O₆) and oxygen (O₂). This stores energy in chemical bonds. Cellular Respiration: Occurs in most living organisms (plants, animals, fungi): • C6H12O6+6 O2→6 CO2+6 H2O+ATP (energy) Cells break down glucose using oxygen to release carbon dioxide, water, and energy (ATP). Which of the following accurately describes the relationship between the inputs and outputs of photosynthesis and cellular respiration, illustrating how these two processes work together in many ecosystems?','Respiration uses sunlight and water to produce glucose and oxygen, which are then used by photosynthesis to release energy.','Photosynthesis uses oxygen and glucose to produce carbon dioxide and water, which are then used by respiration to generate energy.','Respiration uses carbon dioxide and water to produce glucose and oxygen, while photosynthesis breaks down glucose and oxygen to release carbon dioxide and water.','Photosynthesis uses carbon dioxide, water, and light energy to produce glucose and oxygen, which are then used by respiration to produce ATP (energy), carbon dioxide, and water.','D','o Photosynthesis: This process, primarily occurring in plants and some other organisms, converts light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose (a sugar). The inputs are carbon dioxide (CO2), water (H2O), and light energy. The outputs are glucose (CH12O6) and oxygen (O2). o Cellular Respiration: This process occurs in most living organisms and breaks down glucose to release energy in the form of ATP (adenosine triphosphate). The inputs are glucose (C6H F1512O6) and oxygen (O2). The outputs are ATP (energy), carbon dioxide (CO2), and water (H2O). o The products of photosynthesis (glucose and oxygen) are the primary reactants for cellular respiration, and the products of cellular respiration (carbon dioxide and water) are the reactants for photosynthesis. This 1 cyclical relationship is fundamental to energy flow and the cycling of matter in many ecosystems.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,43,'During a class biodiversity project, students were asked to create an infographic showing the conservation status of native species in the Philippines. They were instructed to refer to secondary sources like the IUCN Red List and local conservation databases to classify species as either Critically Endangered or Vulnerable. One group chose to highlight both animal and plant species, aiming to raise awareness about biodiversity loss. As they sorted through species data, they realized how classification helps prioritize conservation efforts and funding. Their final task was to match one critically endangered and one vulnerable species, based on accurate scientific classification from trusted databases.','Based on classifications often provided by secondary sources such as the IUCN Red List, which of the following combinations correctly identifies one critically endangered and one vulnerable species native to the Philippines?','Critically Endangered: Tamaraw; Vulnerable: Philippine Tarsier','Critically Endangered: Cebu Flowerpecker; Vulnerable: Dugong','Critically Endangered: Rafflesia arnoldii; Vulnerable: Philippine Spotted Deer','Critically Endangered: Philippine Eagle; Vulnerable: Palawan Peacock-pheasant','D','Philippine Eagle (Pithecophaga jefferyi): This magnificent bird is endemic to the Philippines and is globally classified as Critically Endangered by the IUCN Red List due to severe habitat loss and hunting. Palawan Peacock-pheasant (Polyplectron napoleonis): This beautiful pheasant is endemic to Palawan, Philippines, and is classified as Vulnerable by the IUCN Red List, primarily due to habitat degradation and hunting pressure.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,44,'During a class biodiversity project, students were asked to create an infographic showing the conservation status of native species in the Philippines. They were instructed to refer to secondary sources like the IUCN Red List and local conservation databases to classify species as either Critically Endangered or Vulnerable. One group chose to highlight both animal and plant species, aiming to raise awareness about biodiversity loss. As they sorted through species data, they realized how classification helps prioritize conservation efforts and funding. Their final task was to match one critically endangered and one vulnerable species, based on accurate scientific classification from trusted databases.','When using secondary sources to determine the conservation status of Philippine plant species, which of the following pieces of information is most critical for accurate classification as critically endangered or vulnerable?','The plant''s traditional uses in local indigenous communities.','High-resolution photographs of the plant''s flowers and leaves.','Anecdotal accounts from local residents about the plant''s historical abundance.','Quantitative data on the plant''s population size, distribution, and rates of decline, as assessed by conservation organizations.','D','The classification of a species as critically endangered or vulnerable is based on specific scientific criteria that assess the risk of extinction. This assessment relies heavily on quantitative data regarding: o Population size: The number of mature individuals remaining. o Distribution: The geographic range of the species. o Rates of decline: The observed or estimated reduction in population size or habitat area.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,45,'During an environmental science lesson, Anna and her classmates are learning about how conservation organizations like the IUCN work to protect endangered species. Their teacher explains that the IUCN uses data to assign conservation statuses, such as "Endangered" or "Critically Endangered," to species at risk of extinction. The teacher asks the class to think about conservation methods that focus directly on protecting endangered species and their habitats, rather than methods that involve sustainable use or community- based approaches. Anna wonders which method is most effective for directly protecting species and their habitats.','Which conservation strategy focuses most directly on protecting endangered species and their natural habitats, without relying on economic use or community-based management?','Breeding endangered species in captivity to later releases them into the wild.','Allowing limited harvesting of species under community-led sustainable practices','Encouraging ecotourism to support local livelihoods in areas where endangered species live.','Creating strictly regulated protected zones like national parks and wildlife sanctuaries. .','D','This strategy focuses directly on protecting endangered species and their natural habitats by: o Restricting human activities like logging, hunting, or farming o Preserving ecosystems in their natural state o Providing safe spaces for species to live and reproduce without disturbance Examples include: o National parks (e.g., Yellowstone, Mount Apo) o Wildlife sanctuaries (e.g., Palawan Wildlife Rescue and Conservation Center) These areas are managed primarily for conservation, not for economic gain or community use.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,46,'During an environmental science lesson, Anna and her classmates are learning about how conservation organizations like the IUCN work to protect endangered species. Their teacher explains that the IUCN uses data to assign conservation statuses, such as "Endangered" or "Critically Endangered," to species at risk of extinction. The teacher asks the class to think about conservation methods that focus directly on protecting endangered species and their habitats, rather than methods that involve sustainable use or community- based approaches. Anna wonders which method is most effective for directly protecting species and their habitats.','Which of the following conservation methods for economically important species best integrates the principles of sustainable use to ensure long-term viability and benefits for local communities?','Relocating the species to remote, uninhabited areas to prevent human interaction and exploitation.','Implementing a complete and permanent ban on the harvesting of the species to allow its population to recover.','Establishing large-scale commercial plantations of the species managed by private corporations for maximum profit.','Develop community-based management plans that regulate harvesting levels, protect breeding grounds, and provide economic incentives for conservation.','D','Community-based management plans that incorporate regulated harvesting, habitat protection, and economic benefits for local communities are the most aligned with sustainable use principles. This approach recognizes the interdependence of human livelihoods and species conservation, aiming for long- term viability by ensuring that resource use does not exceed the species'' capacity to regenerate and that local people have a vested interest in its protection.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,47,'A local government unit in Northern Mindanao is facing the challenge of balancing the conservation of the critically endangered Philippine Eagle and supporting the livelihoods of communities that live in or near its remaining habitat. They are considering various conservation strategies but need to choose the most effective and sustainable approaches.','The local government is considering establishing a protected area to safeguard the Philippine Eagle''s nesting sites. Which of the following potential negative consequences should they most critically consider and plan to mitigate to ensure long-term success and local support for this conservation method?','An increase in the local birdwatching tourism industry.','Increased monitoring and research activities conducted by external scientists.','A decrease in the population of the eagle''s prey species due to habitat preservation.','Potential restrictions on traditional land use practices by local communities within the protected area.','D','Establishing protected areas can often lead to restrictions on traditional activities like farming, hunting, and gathering, which can negatively impact the livelihoods and cultural practices of local communities. Without proper engagement, compensation, and alternative livelihood options, this can lead to resentment, non- compliance, and ultimately undermine the conservation efforts.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,48,'A local government unit in Northern Mindanao is facing the challenge of balancing the conservation of the critically endangered Philippine Eagle and supporting the livelihoods of communities that live in or near its remaining habitat. They are considering various conservation strategies but need to choose the most effective and sustainable approaches.','To address the economic needs of communities living near the eagle''s habitat while promoting conservation, the local government is exploring sustainable livelihood alternatives. Which of the following options would best align with both conservation goals and potential long-term economic benefits for the local population?','Encouraging the conversion of forest areas into large-scale monoculture plantations for export crops.','Supporting the development of community-based ecotourism initiatives focused on responsible wildlife viewing and local culture.','Providing financial incentives for local communities to hunt and remove potential threats to the eagles, such as introduced predators.','Facilitating the extraction of timber and other forest resources under strict government control to generate revenue for the community.','B','Community-based ecotourism can provide direct economic benefits to local communities through guiding, accommodation, and sale of local crafts, while simultaneously creating a vested interest in protecting the natural environment and the flagship species like the Philippine Eagle. It promotes sustainable use of resources and can raise awareness about conservation.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,49,NULL,'The local government is also considering a captive breeding and reintroduction program for the Philippine Eagle to boost its population. Which of the following factors would be the most significant challenge to the long-term success of such a program in contributing to the overall conservation of the species in the wild?','The potential for a decrease in genetic diversity within the captive population.','The high cost and logistical complexity of maintaining a captive breeding facility.','The potential for reintroduced eagles to become habituated to human presence and dependent on supplementary feeding','Ensuring the availability of suitable and protected habitat for the reintroduced eagles and addressing the threats that caused their initial decline.','D','Captive breeding and reintroduction are only effective if the underlying threats in the wild (habitat loss, hunting, etc.) are addressed and there is suitable, protected habitat for the released individuals to survive and reproduce. Without addressing these issues, reintroduced eagles will likely face the same challenges that led to their endangered status in the first place, rendering the expensive and complex captive breeding efforts futile in the long run.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,2,50,NULL,'A young scientist, Allen, is fascinated by how living things can solve human problems. Allen knows biotechnology uses organisms for many things, but wants to understand the core idea behind it all. Which of the following statements best describes the fundamental concept underlying the field of biotechnology?','The study of the ethical implications of using living organisms in research.','The application of technological advancements to understand the complex functions of living cells.','The development of new pharmaceutical drugs through chemical synthesis and testing on animal models.','The utilization of biological systems, living organisms, or their derivatives to create or modify products or processes for specific uses.','D','Biotechnology, at its core, involves harnessing the power of biology to solve problems and create useful products or processes. This includes manipulating living organisms, their components (like enzymes or genes), or biological processes for applications in various fields. Options A, B, and D describe related but distinct concepts. While watching a television program about farming and health, Jenny hears the host mention how scientists are helping farmers grow healthier crops and doctors create better medicines. The host says these benefits come from something called "biotechnology." Jenny becomes curious and wants to understand why biotechnology is considered so important in farming, healthcare, and industries.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,51,NULL,'Which statement best highlights a key reason why biotechnology is important in different fields like agriculture, health, and industry?','It helps protect endangered species and preserve biodiversity','It replaces traditional industries with artificial, non-living technologies','It mainly helps scientists study how different organisms are related through evolution','It supports sustainable farming, better medical treatments, and new industrial innovations','D','Biotechnology is the use of living organisms or biological systems to develop products and solve problems in various fields. The key reason it’s important is its wide-ranging impact: o Agriculture: Produces drought-resistant crops, improves yields, and reduces pesticide use o Health: Enables vaccines, gene therapy, and personalized medicine o Industry: Creates biodegradable plastics, biofuels, and efficient waste treatment methods This makes biotechnology a powerful tool for sustainability, innovation, and human well-being.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,52,NULL,'A student walks from their home to a grocery store located 2 kilometers east. After shopping, they return home via a different route that is 3 kilometers west. Considering the student''s journey, which of the following statements accurately describes the distance traveled and displacement relative to their home as the reference point?','Distance: 5 kilometers; Displacement: 1 kilometer west','Distance: 3 kilometers; Displacement: 5 kilometers east','Distance: 5 kilometers; Displacement: 5 kilometers east','Distance: 2 kilometers; Displacement: 3 kilometers west','A','The distance is calculated as the total path traveled. The student walks 2 kilometers to the east and then 3 kilometers to the west, resulting in a total distance of 2 +3 = 5 kilometers The displacement is the straight-line distance from the starting point (home) to the ending point (grocery store). After returning, the student ends up 3 – 2 = 1;3−2=1 kilometer west of their original position (home). Therefore, the displacement is 1 kilometer west.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,53,NULL,'A child rides their bicycle 4 kilometers north to a park, then rides 1 kilometer south to a friend''s house. If the child''s home is the reference point, what is the total distance traveled and the displacement from their home?','Distance: 5 kilometers; Displacement: 3 kilometers north','Distance: 3 kilometers; Displacement: 5 kilometers north','Distance: 4 kilometers; Displacement: 1 kilometer south','Distance: 5 kilometers; Displacement: 1 kilometer north','A','The distance traveled includes all movement. The child rides 4 kilometers north and then 1 kilometer south, giving a total distance of 4 +1=5 4 + 1 = 5 kilometers. The displacement is the straight-line distance from the starting point (home) to the ending point (friend''s house). After riding north and then south, the child ends up 4 −1= 3 4−1=3 kilometers north of their starting position (home). Therefore, the displacement is 3 kilometers north.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,54,NULL,'A physics teacher is explaining Newton''s second law of motion in class, which describes the relationship among force, acceleration, and mass. Which of the following statements accurately captures this relationship?','Acceleration increases as mass increases, provided the force remains constant.','Mass has no effect on acceleration when a constant force is applied.','Acceleration is independent of force and mass; it only depends on the speed of the object.','Force is directly proportional to mass and acceleration, meaning that if either mass or acceleration increases, the force must increase as well.','D','The correct answer accurately reflects Newton''s second law of motion, which is often stated as F = ma F=ma, where F F is the force applied, m is the mass of the object, and a is the acceleration produced. This law indicates that: The greater the mass of an object, the more force is required to achieve the same acceleration. Conversely, for a constant mass, an increase in force will result in an increase in acceleration. Option A is incorrect because, according to Newton''s second law, if mass increases while the force remains constant, the acceleration will actually decrease. Option C is misleading; mass does affect acceleration, as a larger mass requires more force to achieve the same acceleration as a smaller mass. Option D is incorrect because acceleration is indeed dependent on both force and mass, not independent of them. Thus, the correct answer effectively illustrates the fundamental relationship among force, acceleration, and mass, enhancing students'' comprehension of this key concept in physics.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,55,NULL,'Consider the following three scenarios: I. A car accelerating from rest at a traffic light. II. A satellite orbiting Earth at a constant speed on a circular path. III. A car slows down as it approaches a stop sign. Which of these scenarios (I, II, and III) demonstrate acceleration as a change in speed, direction, or both?','I, II and III','II and III only','I and II only','I and III only','A','Acceleration is defined as any change in velocity, which includes: o A change in speed o A change in direction o Or both Let’s examine each scenario: I. A car accelerating from rest at a traffic light o The car is increasing speed from zero. o This is acceleration due to a change in speed. II. A satellite orbiting Earth at a constant speed in a circular path o The speed remains constant, but the direction is continuously changing as it follows a curved (circular) path. o This is acceleration due to a change in direction. III. A braking car slowing down as it approaches a stop sign o The car is decreasing speed (negative acceleration or deceleration). o This is acceleration due to a change in speed.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,56,NULL,'Which of the following options accurately lists “two or more distinct innovative devices” that convert a non-electrical form of energy into electrical energy, along with their primary input energy source?','Solar Panels (Light Energy) and Wind Turbines (Kinetic Energy of Air)','Fuel Cells (Chemical Energy) and Thermoelectric Generators (Mechanical Stress)','Batteries (Stored Chemical Energy) and Electric Motors (Electrical Energy to Mechanical Energy)','Geothermal Power Plants (Heat Energy from Earth) and Nuclear Fission Reactors (Nuclear Energy)','A','Both solar panels and wind turbines are recognized as innovative technologies that directly convert light and kinetic energy, respectively, into electrical energy.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,57,NULL,'A roller coaster car is at the top of a hill, where it has a height of 30 meters. As it descends, it picks up speed. Which of the following statements accurately describes the changes in kinetic energy and potential energy as the car moves from the top of the hill to the bottom?','Both potential energy and kinetic energy increase as the car descends.','The kinetic energy remains constant while the potential energy decreases','Potential energy increases while the kinetic energy decreases as the car moves down.','The potential energy decreases while the kinetic energy increases, keeping the total energy constant.','D','o Potential energy is the energy stored in an object due to its position or height. At the top of the hill, the roller coaster car has maximum potential energy because it is at a height of 30 meters. As the car descends, its height decreases, leading to a decrease in potential energy. o Kinetic energy, on the other hand, is the energy of motion. As the roller coaster car moves down the hill, it accelerates, which increases its speed and therefore its kinetic energy. o According to the law of conservation of energy, the total mechanical energy (the sum of potential energy and kinetic energy) in a closed system remains constant, assuming negligible friction and air resistance. Therefore, as potential energy decreases, kinetic energy increases, keeping the total energy constant. o The correct answer clearly illustrates the relationship between potential energy and kinetic energy in the context of the roller coaster''s motion, reinforcing the understanding of these fundamental concepts in physics.58. A family is moving furniture in their home. Which of the following scenarios represents work being done according to the physical definition of work (force applied over a distance)?',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,58,NULL,'A family is moving furniture in their home. Which of the following scenarios represents work being done according to the physical definition of work (force applied over a distance)?','The family stretches a rubber band while sitting on the couch.','The family lifts a heavy couch and carries it to a different room.','The family pushes against a wall while trying to rearrange the living room.','The family takes a break while standing next to the couch in the living room.','B','In this scenario, work is defined as the force applied to an object multiplied by the distance over which that force is applied in the direction of the force. Lifting the heavy couch involves applying a force to overcome gravity and moving it to a different room, which constitutes work being done.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,59,NULL,'At a local school, students are participating in a community clean-up day. Which of the following activities demonstrates work being done in the context of this event?','Students take pictures of the clean-up for social media.','Students gather supplies and discuss their cleaning strategy.','Students sit in a circle to talk about the importance of a clean environment.','Students pick up trash and place it in garbage bags while walking around the schoolyard.','D','In this example, the students are performing work by applying force to pick up trash and moving it (the force applied over a distance), which involves physical displacement of the trash into garbage bags. This action aligns with the physical definition of work. Thus, both correct answers effectively illustrate the concept of work done in practical scenarios at home and in the community, reinforcing the understanding of this important principle in physics.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,60,NULL,'During a science lab, students are instructed to use electrical equipment to conduct experiments. Which of the following practices represents a safe measure for handling electricity in this environment?','Students should work quickly to complete their experiments without checking connections','Students can use any type of wire, even if it is frayed or damaged, as long as they are careful.','Students can use metal tools to adjust equipment while it is powered on, as long as they are cautious.','Students should ensure that their hands are dry and that they do not touch electrical equipment with wet hands.','D','The correct answer emphasizes a critical safety measure: keeping hands dry when handling electrical equipment. Wet hands increase the risk of electrical shock as water is a good conductor of electricity. Ensuring that hands are dry is a fundamental practice in preventing accidents.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,61,NULL,'In a workshop, a technician is preparing to work on electrical circuits. Which of the following statements describes a safe practice for handling electricity in this situation?','The technician should ensure that all tools are metal to enhance conductivity.','The technician can leave the power on while making adjustments to save time.','The technician should disconnect the power supply before making any adjustments to the wiring.','The technician can work alone without informing anyone about the electrical work being done.','C','The correct answer highlights an essential safety measure: always disconnecting the power supply before working on electrical circuits. This practice significantly reduces the risk of electric shock and ensures a safer working environment Thus, both correct answers effectively illustrate safe measures in handling electricity, reinforcing the importance of safety protocols in any situation involving electrical work.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,62,'Imagine a community where electricity is generated at a power plant and sent to homes, schools, and businesses. Drake notices the tall towers carrying wires across the countryside and wonders how electricity travels such long distances without losing power. At home, he sees an electric meter outside his house and asks his father what it does. These observations make Drake curious about how electricity is transmitted and measured.','Which electrical component is used to increase voltage for efficient transmission over long distances?','Substation','Electric Meter','Distribution Line','Step-Up Transformer','D','The step-up transformer is responsible for increasing the voltage of electricity generated at power plants to ensure efficient transmission over long distances. Electric meters measure usage, distribution lines carry electricity, and substations step down voltage, but they do not increase it.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,63,'Imagine a community where electricity is generated at a power plant and sent to homes, schools, and businesses. Drake notices the tall towers carrying wires across the countryside and wonders how electricity travels such long distances without losing power. At home, he sees an electric meter outside his house and asks his father what it does. These observations make Drake curious about how electricity is transmitted and measured.','What is the primary purpose of substations in the electricity distribution network?','To store excess electricity for future use','To measure energy consumption for billing','To generate electricity from renewable sources','To convert high-voltage electricity to a lower voltage','D','Substations are designed to step down high-voltage electricity to lower voltages that are safe and usable for consumers. They do not generate electricity, measure consumption, or store energy.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,64,'Imagine a community where electricity is generated at a power plant and sent to homes, schools, and businesses. Drake notices the tall towers carrying wires across the countryside and wonders how electricity travels such long distances without losing power. At home, he sees an electric meter outside his house and asks his father what it does. These observations make Drake curious about how electricity is transmitted and measured.','Which device helps ensure accurate billing by tracking the electricity consumption in households?','Electric Meter','Circuit Breaker','Voltage Regulator','Power Generator','A','An electric meter tracks the amount of electricity consumed in a household. This data is used by utility companies to ensure accurate billing based on the electricity usage.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,65,NULL,'Consider the process by which potential energy stored in lakes and dams is used to generate electricity in the Philippines. Which of the following statements correctly describes this energy transformation process?','Water is evaporated from lakes to create steam that generates electricity','Water stored in dams is used directly as electricity without any transformation.','The electricity generated from dams is produced by solar panels installed around the lakes.','Potential energy of water is converted into kinetic energy, which then spins turbines to generate electricity.','D','The correct answer is B because it accurately describes the process of transforming potential energy (from stored water) into kinetic energy (as water flows down) to spin turbines, which ultimately generates electricity. Option A is incorrect as water must be transformed into kinetic energy before it can generate electricity. Option C is incorrect because the energy generated is from water movement, not solar panels. Option D is also incorrect as evaporation does not directly contribute to the electricity generation process in dams.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,66,'home. Electricity travels from power plants to homes, schools, and businesses through a network of wires and equipment. Along the way, it needs to be adjusted to ensure it is safe and usable for consumers. Substations play a key role in this process, but what exactly do they do?','Which path correctly illustrates electricity''s journey from power plant to a home, including essential voltage adjustments and infrastructure?','High-voltage towers → directly to consumer appliances → power plants for recycling.','Power plant → direct low-voltage cables → home''s electrical panel for conversion.','Generation → high-voltage transmission → step-down at substations → local distribution → home.','Generator → step-down for immediate local use → community transformers → individual residences.','C','This sequence accurately outlines the main stages: initial generation, voltage step-up for efficient long-distance transmission, subsequent voltage reductions at substations, and final distribution to end-users.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,67,'home. Electricity travels from power plants to homes, schools, and businesses through a network of wires and equipment. Along the way, it needs to be adjusted to ensure it is safe and usable for consumers. Substations play a key role in this process, but what exactly do they do?','What are the functions of substations in the distribution of electricity?','They store electricity and distribute it directly to households.','They generate electricity from fossil fuels and store it for future use.','They convert high-voltage electricity to lower voltage for safe use and regulate power flow.','They measure energy consumption for billing and distribute electricity to appliances.','C','Substations perform two key functions in the distribution of electricity: o They reduce the high-voltage electricity from transmission lines to a lower voltage that is safe for use in homes, schools, and businesses. o They regulate the flow of electricity to ensure stable and efficient delivery to consumers.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,68,'Electrical devices are commonly used in homes, schools, and workplaces. While they make life more convenient, they can also pose risks if not handled properly. Implementing safety precautions is essential to avoid potential hazards.','What are the reasons for implementing safety precautions when using electrical devices?','To make the devices work faster and improve their efficiency','To prevent electric shocks, injuries, and damage to the devices','To increase the cost of electricity and reduce energy consumption','To improve the appearance of devices and make them more attractive','B','Safety precautions are implemented to protect users from electric shocks and injuries, which can occur due to improper handling or faulty devices. Additionally, these precautions help prevent damage to the devices, ensuring their safe and efficient operation.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,69,'Electrical devices are commonly used in homes, schools, and workplaces. While they make life more convenient, they can also pose risks if not handled properly. Implementing safety precautions is essential to avoid potential hazards.','Why are safety precautions essential when using household electrical devices?','Only to ensure that wiring meets local building codes and standards.','Mainly to keep appliances working longer by avoiding any electrical surges.','To prevent only minor device malfunctions and occasional power outages.','To guard against electrocution, fires, and burns by managing electrical current and maintaining device integrity.','D','The correct answer is D. This option accurately covers the critical dangers (electrocution, fire, burns) and links them to the underlying electrical principles and device conditions that precautions aim to control.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,70,'Electrical devices are commonly used in homes, schools, and workplaces. While they make life more convenient, they can also pose risks if not handled properly. Implementing safety precautions is essential to avoid potential hazards.','What is the benefit of following safety guidelines when using electrical devices?','They help prolong the lifespan of the devices','They make devices more difficult to operate','They prevent the use of modern technology','They allow users to ignore manufacturer instructions','A','The correct answer is A because adhering to safety guidelines ensures that devices are used correctly and maintained properly, which can extend their lifespan. Options B, C, and D are incorrect as they do not emphasize the benefits of following safety guidelines in a positive manner.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,71,'Electromagnetic radiation is used in various fields, including medicine, technology, and energy production. In the medical field, specific types of electromagnetic radiation play a crucial role in diagnosing and treating illnesses.','How is electromagnetic radiation used in communication?','By storing energy in batteries','By blocking harmful UV rays','By reflecting sound waves from satellites','By transmitting signals through radio waves','D','The correct answer is D because electromagnetic radiation, specifically radio waves, is used to transmit signals for various forms of communication, including radio and television. Options A, B, and C do not accurately describe how EMR is involved in communication.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,72,'Electromagnetic radiation is used in various fields, including medicine, technology, and energy production. In the medical field, specific types of electromagnetic radiation play a crucial role in diagnosing and treating illnesses.','Which of the following describes a medical application of electromagnetic radiation?','Using infrared light to cook food and sterilize medical equipment','Developing solar panels for energy and powering medical devices','Generating electricity from wind turbines and supplying power to hospitals','Employing X-rays to create images of the inside of the body and detect fractures','D','X-rays are a type of electromagnetic radiation widely used in medicine to: o Create detailed images of the inside of the body, such as bones and organs o Detect fractures, infections, or abnormalities o Assist in diagnosing conditions like pneumonia or tumors This application is a cornerstone of medical imaging and has revolutionized healthcare diagnostics.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,73,NULL,'Understanding how the magnitude of earthquakes affects communities is crucial for disaster preparedness, response planning, and reducing the risks associated with seismic events. How do earthquake effects on communities change with increasing magnitude?','Effects remain constant; only the duration of shaking increases.','Impacts are unpredictable, unrelated to magnitude, and solely depend on local building quality.','Lower magnitudes create major building collapses, while higher magnitudes only cause minor ground cracks.','Higher magnitudes cause more severe, widespread structural damage, secondary hazards (e.g., landslides, tsunamis), and greater socio-economic disruption.','D','The correct answer is D. This option accurately captures the escalating and diversifying impacts of higher magnitude earthquakes across multiple dimensions: physical, environmental, and societal. Earthquakes are natural phenomena that vary in magnitude and impact. Moderate magnitude earthquakes, ranging from \\4.0 \\ to \\5.9 \\, are common and can affect communities in different ways depending on factors such as infrastructure and preparedness.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,74,NULL,'What are the typical impacts of moderate magnitude earthquakes (Magnitude \\4.0 - 5.9 \\) on communities?','They go unnoticed by the population and have no measurable effects.','They only affect rural areas with no infrastructure and leave urban areas unaffected.','They may cause minor damage to buildings, are generally felt by people, and can disrupt daily activities.','They cause catastrophic damage and loss of life. They cause catastrophic damage, widespread destruction, and loss of life.','C','Moderate magnitude earthquakes typically result in minor damage to structures, such as cracks in walls or ceilings, and are often felt by people in the affected area. While they rarely cause catastrophic destruction, they can disrupt daily activities and highlight the importance of earthquake preparation.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',2,3,75,NULL,'On a quiet morning, residents of a coastal city suddenly experienced intense ground shaking. Emergency sirens begin to wail as buildings sway and infrastructure cracks. Local authorities later report that the earthquake had a magnitude of ≥ 8.0, triggering widespread panic and overwhelming emergency services. What are the typical impacts of major earthquakes (Magnitude ≥ 8.0) on communities?','They cause only minor injuries and no structural damage.','They have no impact on buildings, infrastructure, or the population.','They cause minimal damage, allowing communities to recover quickly.','They result in catastrophic damage to buildings and infrastructure, leading to long-term recovery challenges.','D','Major earthquakes release immense seismic energy. In densely populated or poorly prepared areas, this can cause buildings to collapse, roads to buckle, and essential services to fail. Recovery takes time due to the scale of destruction and humanitarian needs. The scenario highlights how even one major quake can overwhelm systems and change lives.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('JHS','LS2',3,1,1,NULL,'Which of the following statements differentiates the subatomic particles in terms of their symbol, mass, charge, and location within an atom?','Protons (p+) are negatively charged particles with very little mass, found outside the nucleus.','Neutrons (n⁰) are positively charged particles with a mass equal to electrons, located in the electron cloud.','Electrons (e⁻) are neutral particles with a mass equal to protons, found in the nucleus.','Protons (p⁺) are positively charged particles with a mass of approximately 1 amu, located in the nucleus.','C','When a substance transitions from a solid to a liquid (melting), the particles become less organized and begin to move past one another due to an increase in energy, which overcomes the strong intermolecular forces that held them in place as a solid.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,2,NULL,'Which of the following statements correctly compares the charge and mass of protons, neutrons, and electrons?','Protons have no charge and a mass of approximately 1 amu, neutrons are negatively charged with a negligible mass, and electrons are positively charged with a mass of about 1 amu.','Protons are positively charged with a mass of approximately 1 amu, neutrons are neutrally charged with a mass of about 1 amu, and electrons are negatively charged with a negligible mass.','Protons have a negative charge and a mass of about 0.5 amu, neutrons are positively charged with a mass of approximately 1 amu, and electrons are neutral with a mass of about 1 amu.','Protons and neutrons are negatively charged, while electrons are positively charged; all have a mass of 1 amu.','B','Option B correctly compares the subatomic particles: Protons are positively charged with a mass of approximately 1 atomic mass unit (amu), neutrons are neutrally charged and also have a mass of about 1 amu, and electrons are negatively charged with a negligible mass. This understanding is vital for studying atomic structure and chemical behavior.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,3,NULL,'How do the locations of protons, neutrons, and electrons within an atom differ?','Protons and neutrons are found in the nucleus, while electrons are located in the nucleus as well.','Protons and electrons are found in the nucleus, while neutrons are located in orbitals around the nucleus.','Protons and neutrons are located in the nucleus, while electrons occupy orbitals around the nucleus.','Neutrons are in the nucleus, while protons and electrons are found in orbitals around the nucleus.','C','Option C accurately describes the locations of the subatomic particles: Protons and neutrons are found in the nucleus at the center of the atom, while electrons occupy orbitals around the nucleus. This distinction is crucial for understanding atomic structure and the interactions between subatomic particles.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,4,'Understanding the chemical formulas and names of common ionic compounds is crucial for studying chemistry. Ionic compounds are formed from the combination of cations (positively charged ions) and anions (negatively charged ions). Recognizing these compounds helps students understand their properties and applications. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding common ionic compounds.','Which of the following pairs correctly matches the chemical name with its corresponding chemical formula?','Sodium Chloride – KCl','Magnesium Oxide – MgO','Potassium Chloride – NaCl','Magnesium Chloride – KCl','B','Option B correctly matches the chemical name "Magnesium Oxide" with its corresponding chemical formula "MgO." Sodium Chloride corresponds to NaCl, Potassium Chloride corresponds to KCl, and Magnesium Chloride corresponds to MgCl₂. This question encourages students to demonstrate their understanding of the relationship between the names and formulas of ionic compounds.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,5,'Understanding the chemical formulas and names of common ionic compounds is crucial for studying chemistry. Ionic compounds are formed from the combination of cations (positively charged ions) and anions (negatively charged ions). Recognizing these compounds helps students understand their properties and applications. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding common ionic compounds.','Which of the following chemical formulas correctly matches an ionic compound with its name?','NaCl - Potassium Chloride','MgCl2 - Magnesium Chloride','KCl - Sodium Chloride','Na2O - Potassium Oxide','B','Option B correctly identifies the chemical formula "MgCl2". MgCl2 is an ionic compound made of magnesium (Mg2+) and chloride ions (Cl⁻), correctly named Magnesium Chloride. The other options are mismatched: NaCl is Sodium Chloride, not Potassium Chloride, and KCl is Potassium Chloride, not Sodium Chloride. Na2O is also incorrectly named—it should be Sodium Oxide, not Potassium Oxide.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,6,'Covalent compounds are formed when nonmetal atoms share electrons. Being able to correctly identify and name these compounds helps students communicate effectively in chemistry. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the rules for writing and naming covalent compounds.','Which of the following is the correct name for the covalent compound represented by the formula N₂O₃?','Nitrogen Oxide','Dinitrogen Trioxide','Nitrogen Trioxide','Dinitrogen Oxide','B','Option B is correct because N2O3 is named "Dinitrogen Trioxide." The prefix "di-" indicates there are two nitrogen atoms, and "tri-" indicates there are three oxygen atoms. The naming convention for covalent compounds includes using prefixes to denote the number of atoms.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,7,'Covalent compounds are formed when nonmetal atoms share electrons. Being able to correctly identify and name these compounds helps students communicate effectively in chemistry. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the rules for writing and naming covalent compounds.','What is the correct formula for the covalent compound named "Carbon Disulfide"?','CS2','C2S','C2S2','CS','A','Option A is correct; "Carbon Disulfide" has the formula CS2. The prefix "di-" indicates there are two sulfur atoms bonded to one carbon atom. Understanding how to translate names into chemical formulas is important in chemical nomenclature.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,8,'Covalent compounds are formed when nonmetal atoms share electrons. Being able to correctly identify and name these compounds helps students communicate effectively in chemistry. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the rules for writing and naming covalent compounds.','Which of the following correctly identifies the naming convention for the covalent compound P4O10?','Tetr phosphorus Decaoxide','Tetraphosphorus Dioxide','Tetraphosphorus Decaoxide','Phosphorus Tetraoxide','C','Option C is correct because P4O10 is named "Tetraphosphorus Decaoxide." The prefix "tetra-" indicates four phosphorus atoms, and "deca-" indicates ten oxygen atoms. This question emphasizes the importance of using the appropriate prefixes in naming covalent compounds.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,9,'Covalent bonds are formed when nonmetal atoms share electrons to achieve a full outer electron shell, leading to the creation of molecules. Understanding the formation of covalent bonds is crucial for comprehending the behavior of compounds such as water and carbon dioxide. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the formation of covalent bonds in these molecules.','How are covalent bonds formed in a water molecule (H2O)?','The oxygen atom shares one electron with each hydrogen atom, forming two single covalent bonds.','The hydrogen atoms each share two electrons with the oxygen atom, resulting in one double bond.','Each hydrogen atom loses one electron to the oxygen atom, forming two ionic bonds.','The oxygen atom shares all four of its electrons with the hydrogen atoms, forming a single covalent bond.','A','Option A is correct because in a water molecule (H2O), the oxygen atom shares one electron with each hydrogen atom, forming two single covalent bonds. This sharing allows all atoms to achieve a stable electron configuration, fulfilling the octet rule for oxygen and the duet rule for hydrogen.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,10,'Covalent bonds are formed when nonmetal atoms share electrons to achieve a full outer electron shell, leading to the creation of molecules. Understanding the formation of covalent bonds is crucial for comprehending the behavior of compounds such as water and carbon dioxide. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the formation of covalent bonds in these molecules.','In a carbon dioxide molecule (CO2), how are covalent bonds formed between the carbon and oxygen atoms?','Carbon forms two ionic bonds with the oxygen atoms.','Carbon forms two single covalent bonds with each oxygen atom.','Carbon forms two double covalent bonds, one with each oxygen atom.','Carbon forms one double covalent bond with one oxygen atom and a single bond with the other oxygen atom.','C','Option C is correct because in a carbon dioxide molecule (CO2), the carbon atom forms two double covalent bonds, one with each oxygen atom. Each double bond consists of two pairs of shared electrons, allowing carbon to achieve a full octet while each oxygen also achieves stability through sharing electrons.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,11,'Covalent compounds are formed when nonmetal atoms share electrons, and their names reflect the number of atoms present in the compound. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the rules for writing and naming covalent compounds.','What is the correct name for the covalent compound with the formula of N2O5?','Dinitrogen Pentoxide','Nitrogen Dioxide','Nitrogen Pentoxide','Dinitrogen Oxide','A','Option A is correct because N2O5 is named "Dinitrogen Pentoxide." The prefix "di-" indicates two nitrogen atoms, and "pent-" indicates five oxygen atoms. This follows the rule of using prefixes to denote the number of each type of atom in covalent compounds.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,12,'Covalent compounds are formed when nonmetal atoms share electrons, and their names reflect the number of atoms present in the compound. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the rules for writing and naming covalent compounds.','When naming a covalent compound, which of the following statements is true regarding the use of prefixes?','The prefix "mono-" is always used for the first element in the formula.','The prefix "hexa-" can only be used for the second element in a compound.','The prefix "di-" is used for the first element only when there are two of them.','The prefix "tri-" indicates three atoms of an element and is used for both elements in a compound.','D','Option B is correct. The prefix "tri-" indicates three atoms of an element and can be used for both elements in a compound. While "mono-" is often omitted for the first element, prefixes such as "di-", "tri-", and "hexa-" are consistently used to indicate the number of atoms for both the first and second elements.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,13,'Covalent compounds are formed when nonmetal atoms share electrons, and their names reflect the number of atoms present in the compound. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the rules for writing and naming covalent compounds.','Which of the following formulas correctly represents the covalent compound named "Carbon Tetrafluoride"?','CF4','C4F','C2F4','C4F2','A','Option A is correct; "Carbon Tetrafluoride" corresponds to the formula CF4. The prefix "tetra-" indicates that there are four fluorine atoms bonded to one carbon atom. This question reinforces the understanding of how to translate names into correct chemical formulas for covalent compounds.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,14,'Investigating the properties of ionic, covalent, and metallic substances is essential for understanding their behaviors and applications in various contexts. These properties include melting point, hardness, and electrical and thermal conductivity. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the properties of these types of substances.','Which of the following statements correctly describes the melting point and conductivity of ionic compounds?','Ionic compounds generally have low melting points and are poor conductors of electricity in both solid and liquid states.','Ionic compounds typically have high melting points and conduct electricity only when dissolved in water or melted.','Ionic compounds have variable melting points and are excellent conductors of electricity in solid form.','Ionic compounds usually have low melting points and conduct electricity well when solid.','B','Option B is correct because ionic compounds typically have high melting points due to the strong electrostatic forces between the charged ions. They conduct electricity only when dissolved in water (aqueous state) or melted (liquid state) because the ions are free to move. In solid form, ionic compounds do not conduct electricity since the ions are fixed in place',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,15,'Investigating the properties of ionic, covalent, and metallic substances is essential for understanding their behaviors and applications in various contexts. These properties include melting point, hardness, and electrical and thermal conductivity. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the properties of these types of substances.','Which of the following statements describes the properties of metallic substances compared to covalent substances?','Metallic substances have low melting points and are brittle, while covalent substances are malleable and conduct electricity well.','Metallic substances are generally good conductors of electricity and heat, have high melting points, and are malleable, while covalent substances tend to have lower melting points and do not conduct electricity.','Metallic substances are poor conductors of heat and electricity, while covalent substances are excellent conductors.','Metallic substances have high melting points and are hard, while covalent substances are always soft and have high melting points.','B','Option B is correct because metallic substances are generally good conductors of electricity and heat due to the presence of free-moving electrons. They typically have high melting points and are malleable. In contrast, covalent substances usually have lower melting points and do not conduct electricity, as they consist of neutral molecules without free ions or electrons.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,16,'Investigating the properties of ionic, covalent, and metallic substances is essential for understanding their behaviors and applications in various contexts. These properties include melting point, hardness, and electrical and thermal conductivity. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the properties of these types of substances.','Which of the following statements describes the properties of metallic substances compared to covalent substances?','Metallic substances have low melting points and are brittle, while covalent substances are malleable and conduct electricity well.','Metallic substances are generally good conductors of electricity and heat, have high melting points, and are malleable, while covalent substances tend to have lower melting points and do not conduct electricity.','Metallic substances are poor conductors of heat and electricity, while covalent substances are excellent conductors.','Metallic substances have high melting points and are hard, while covalent substances are always soft and have high melting points.','B','Option B is correct because metallic substances are generally good conductors of electricity and heat due to the presence of free-moving electrons. They typically have high melting points and are malleable. In contrast, covalent substances usually have lower melting points and do not conduct electricity, as they consist of neutral molecules without free ions or electrons.',NULL,0,0),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,17,'Investigating the properties of ionic, covalent, and metallic substances is essential for understanding their behaviors and applications in various contexts. These properties include melting point, hardness, and electrical and thermal conductivity. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the properties of these types of substances.','Which of the following best explains why metals are malleable and conduct electricity, while covalent substances typically do not?','Metals consist of ions held together by ionic bonds, while covalent substances have free electrons that allow conductivity.','Metals have a sea of delocalized electrons that move freely, enabling conductivity and malleability, while covalent substances have localized electrons in shared bonds.','Metals are composed of molecules with strong directional bonds, while covalent substances have metallic lattices.','Metals have low melting points due to weak bonds, while covalent substances have high melting points due to strong metallic bonding.','B','The correct answer is B because metals have a structure where atoms are arranged in a lattice and their outer electrons are free to move throughout the material—this "sea of delocalized electrons" allows metals to conduct electricity and be reshaped without breaking. In contrast, covalent substances have electrons tightly shared between specific atoms, forming rigid bonds that do not allow free movement of charge. This difference in electron behavior explains why metals are malleable and conductive, while covalent substances are typically not.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,18,'The solubility of a substance changes based on external conditions, which can be critical in both academic and practical applications. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the factors affecting solubility.','How does increasing the temperature typically affect the solubility of most solid solutes in water?','Solubility decreases as temperature increases.','Solubility remains constant regardless of temperature changes.','Solubility increases as temperature increases.','Solubility fluctuates randomly with temperature changes.','C','Option C is correct because, for most solid solutes, increasing the temperature leads to an increase in solubility. The added heat provides energy that helps break the intermolecular forces between solute particles, allowing them to dissolve more readily in the solvent.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,19,'The solubility of a substance changes based on external conditions, which can be critical in both academic and practical applications. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the factors affecting solubility.','When gases dissolve in liquids, temperature can affect how well they stay mixed. Understanding this helps explain everyday things like why soda goes flat faster when it''s warm. What happens to the solubility of gases in liquids when the temperature increases?','Gas solubility increases with temperature.','Gas solubility decreases with temperature.','Temperature has no effect on gas solubility.','Gas solubility fluctuates randomly with temperature changes.','B','Option B is correct because, as temperature rises, gas molecules gain more energy and are more likely to escape from the liquid into the air. This means fewer gas molecules stay dissolved, so solubility goes down.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,20,'The solubility of a substance changes based on external conditions, which can be critical in both academic and practical applications. Based on this understanding, answer the following questions regarding the factors affecting solubility.','Which of the following factors can also affect the solubility of a solute in a solvent, aside from temperature?','The color of the solute.','The size of the solute particles.','The shape of the solvent container.','The pressure applied to the solvent, particularly for gases.','B','Option B is correct because pressure significantly affects the solubility of gases in liquids. Increasing pressure increases the solubility of a gas in a liquid, as it forces more gas particles into the solution. The other options (color, size of solute particles, and shape of the container) do not have a direct effect on solubility in the same way.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,21,'Coleen is investigating at home and school using a litmus indicator to determine whether various common substances are acids, bases, or salts. Her goal is to understand the properties of these substances and how they interact with the litmus indicator.','When you dip a blue litmus paper into a solution and it turns red, what does this indicate about the solution?','The solution is neutral.','The solution is acidic.','The solution is basic.','The solution is saline.','B','A blue litmus paper turning red indicates that the solution is acidic. Acids have a pH less than 7 and turn blue litmus paper red.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,22,'Coleen is investigating at home and school using a litmus indicator to determine whether various common substances are acids, bases, or salts. Her goal is to understand the properties of these substances and how they interact with the litmus indicator.','If a red litmus paper turns blue when dipped into a solution, what can you conclude about that solution?','The solution is neutral.','The solution is acidic.','The solution is basic.','The solution is a salt','C','A red litmus paper turning blue indicates that the solution is basic (alkaline), which has a pH greater than 7.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,23,'Coleen is investigating at home and school using a litmus indicator to determine whether various common substances are acids, bases, or salts. Her goal is to understand the properties of these substances and how they interact with the litmus indicator.','Which of the following substances would you expect to turn blue litmus paper red?','Vinegar','Baking soda','Water','Soap','A','Vinegar is an acidic solution (pH around 2-3) and would turn blue litmus paper red, indicating its acidic nature. Baking soda is basic, water is neutral, and soap is also typically basic.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,24,'Coleen is investigating at home and school using a litmus indicator to determine whether various common substances are acids, bases, or salts. Her goal is to understand the properties of these substances and how they interact with the litmus indicator.','Coleen tested three solutions: Solution A turned blue litmus paper red, Solution B turned red litmus paper blue, and Solution C did not change the color of either paper. What can you conclude about these solutions?','All solutions are acidic.','All solutions are neutral.','Solution A is basic, Solution B is acidic, and Solution C is neutral.','Solution A is acidic, Solution B is basic, and Solution C is neutral.','D','Solution A turned blue litmus paper red, indicating it is acidic. Solution B turned red litmus paper blue, indicating it is basic. Solution C did not change the color of either litmus paper, signifying it is neutral.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,1,25,'Seth is tasked with examining various solutions he can find in his home to determine whether they are acids, bases, or salts. This investigation will him gather and interpret data about common household substances.','Seth found a bottle of lemon juice in your kitchen. After conducting a litmus test, the blue litmus paper turns red. What can he conclude about lemon juice?','Lemon juice is a base.','Lemon juice is neutral.','Lemon juice is an acid.','Lemon juice is a salt.','C','Lemon juice has a low pH, typically around 2, which categorizes it as an acid. The reaction with blue litmus paper, turning it red, supports this conclusion.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,26,'Seth is tasked with examining various solutions he can find in his home to determine whether they are acids, bases, or salts. This investigation will him gather and interpret data about common household substances.','Seth tested a solution of baking soda mixed in water with red litmus paper, and it did not change color. What does this indicate about the baking soda solution?','The solution is acidic.','The solution is basic.','The solution is neutral.','The solution is a salt.','C','If the red litmus paper does not change color when dipped into the baking soda solution, it suggests that the solution is neutral (pH around 7). Baking soda itself is a basic substance, but when dissolved in water, it may not significantly affect the acidity of the solution, depending on the concentration.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,27,'A student is using physical models and diagrams from a textbook to compare the structures of typical plant and animal cells. To demonstrate an understanding of the relationships between these structures and their presence or absence in each cell type, the student needs to accurately identify organelles and determine whether they are found in plant cells only, animal cells only, both, or neither, based on the provided models.','Based on the typical models of plant and animal cells, which of the following organelles is present in both plant and animal cells and performs a similar fundamental function in both?','Cell wall, providing structural support and protection.','Large central vacuole, storing water and maintaining turgor pressure.','Chloroplast, carrying out photosynthesis to produce energy.','Mitochondria, generating ATP (energy) through cellular respiration.','D','Typical models of both plant and animal cells depict mitochondria. In both cell types, mitochondria are the primary sites of cellular respiration, the process that breaks down glucose to produce ATP, the main energy currency of the cell. While plant cells also produce energy through photosynthesis in chloroplasts, both kingdoms rely on mitochondria for ATP production from organic molecules.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,28,'A student is using physical models and diagrams from a textbook to compare the structures of typical plant and animal cells. To demonstrate an understanding of the relationships between these structures and their presence or absence in each cell type, the student needs to accurately identify organelles and determine whether they are found in plant cells only, animal cells only, both, or neither, based on the provided models.','When comparing models of plant and animal cells, the presence or absence of which of the following pairs of structures provides a key distinction between these two cell types?','Nucleus (present in both) and cell membrane (present in both).','Ribosomes (present in both) and cytoplasm (present in both).','Endoplasmic reticulum (present in both) and Golgi apparatus (present in both).','Cell wall (typically present in plant cells, absent in animal cells) and centrioles (typically absent in plant cells, present in animal cells).','D','The cell wall is a rigid outer layer found in typical plant cells that provides structural support and protection but is absent in typical animal cells. Centrioles are small, cylindrical organelles involved in cell division in animal cells and are typically absent in plant cells (though there are exceptions in lower plant forms). The presence or absence of this pair of structures is a significant distinguishing feature when comparing typical models of plant and animal cells. The other options list organelles that are generally present in both cell types (A, B, and D).',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,29,'A scientist is studying cell samples under a microscope to classify them as either plant or animal cells. While observing the structures, she notices that some cells contain large, membrane-bound compartments filled with fluid, while others do not. Additionally, she sees a distinct green coloration in certain cells. She wonders what these features indicate about the nature and function of these cells.','Which organelle is present in plant cells but absent in animal cells, helping plants to produce their own food?','Mitochondria','Chloroplasts','Lysosomes','Ribosomes','B','Chloroplasts are unique to plant cells and contain chlorophyll, which allows plants to perform photosynthesis, converting sunlight into energy. Animal cells lack this organelle because they obtain energy from consuming other organisms.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,30,'A scientist is studying cell samples under a microscope to classify them as either plant or animal cells. While observing the structures, she notices that some cells contain large, membrane-bound compartments filled with fluid, while others do not. Additionally, she sees a distinct green coloration in certain cells. She wonders what these features indicate about the nature and function of these cells.','A student compares vacuoles in plant and animal cells. What is a key difference between them?','Animal cells do not have vacuoles at all.','Animal cells have vacuoles that store chlorophyll.','Plant cells have a small vacuole, while animal cells have a large central vacuole','Plant cells have a large central vacuole, while animal cells have multiple small vacuoles','D','The large central vacuole in plant cells stores water, nutrients, and waste, helping maintain cell structure and rigidity. Animal cells, on the other hand, may have small vacuoles that play minor roles in storage and digestion.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,31,'A scientist is studying cell samples under a microscope to classify them as either plant or animal cells. While observing the structures, she notices that some cells contain large, membrane-bound compartments filled with fluid, while others do not. Additionally, she sees a distinct green coloration in certain cells. She wonders what these features indicate about the nature and function of these cells.','If a scientist finds a cell with a rigid structure surrounding the membrane, what type of cell is she observing?','Animal Cell','Plant Cell','Bacterial Cell','Fungal Cell','B','Plant cells have a cell wall; a rigid outer layer made of cellulose that provides structural support and protection. Animal cells lack a cell wall, relying instead on their cell membrane for flexibility.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,32,'A group of students is studying a labeled diagram that shows the journey of food through the digestive system. They observe arrows indicating the path food takes as it moves from ingestion to digestion, absorption, and finally elimination. One student asks, “How do different organs contribute to breaking down and absorbing nutrients?” Using the diagram, they trace how food changes in each stage and discuss the roles of key digestive organs.','Based on the diagram, which organ is responsible for pushing food down into the stomach using muscular contractions?','Liver','Esophagus','Small Intestine','Large Intestine','B','The esophagus moves food from the mouth to the stomach using a process called peristalsis, where muscles contract in waves to push food downward.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,33,'A group of students is studying a labeled diagram that shows the journey of food through the digestive system. They observe arrows indicating the path food takes as it moves from ingestion to digestion, absorption, and finally elimination. One student asks, “How do different organs contribute to breaking down and absorbing nutrients?” Using the diagram, they trace how food changes in each stage and discuss the roles of key digestive organs.','In the labeled diagram, where does most nutrient absorption take place?','Stomach','Small Intestine','Large Intestine','Esophagus','B','The small intestine contains tiny structures called villi, which increase surface area and help absorb nutrients into the bloodstream.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,34,'A group of students is studying a labeled diagram that shows the journey of food through the digestive system. They observe arrows indicating the path food takes as it moves from ingestion to digestion, absorption, and finally elimination. One student asks, “How do different organs contribute to breaking down and absorbing nutrients?” Using the diagram, they trace how food changes in each stage and discuss the roles of key digestive organs.','According to the diagram, which part of the digestive tract is responsible for compacting undigested food and absorbing excess water before elimination?','Pancreas','Liver','Large Intestine','Stomach','C','The large intestine absorbs any remaining water and electrolytes, helping form solid waste before elimination through the rectum and anus.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,35,'A group of students is analyzing a labeled diagram showing the interaction between the digestive and excretory systems. They notice that nutrients are absorbed in the small intestine, while waste products are eventually removed by the kidneys. Their teacher asks them to explain how these systems work together to process food and eliminate waste.','In the labeled diagram, which organ is responsible for filtering waste from the blood before excretion?','Liver','Kidneys','Small Intestine','Stomach','B','The kidneys filter waste, excess water, and toxins from the blood, producing urine, which is then excreted through the urinary system.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,36,'A group of students is analyzing a labeled diagram showing the interaction between the digestive and excretory systems. They notice that nutrients are absorbed in the small intestine, while waste products are eventually removed by the kidneys. Their teacher asks them to explain how these systems work together to process food and eliminate waste.','According to the diagram, how do the digestive and excretory systems work together?','Both systems store energy for future use','Both systems produce enzymes to break down food','The excretory system digests food, and the digestive system removes waste','The digestive system absorbs nutrients, and the excretory system removes waste','D','The digestive system breaks down food and absorbs nutrients, while the excretory system eliminates waste products (such as undigested food and toxins) from the body.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,37,'A farmer wants to understand the inheritance of flower color in her garden. She knows that purple flowers (P) are dominant over white flowers (p). She performs a genetic cross between two heterozygous (Pp) purple-flowered plants. Using a Punnett square, she wants to calculate the ratio of offspring with different genotypes and phenotypes.\n\nPunnett Square: Pp x Pp Cross\n\nP ( Parent 1) P (Parent 1) P (Parent 2) PP (Purple) Pp (Purple) p (Parent 2) Pp (Purple) Pp (wHite)','When crossing two heterozygous (Pp) flowers, what percentage of the offspring will have purple flowers?','25%','50%','75%','100%','C','The Punnett square for Pp × Pp shows a 3:1 phenotype ratio, where three offspring will have at least one dominant allele (PP or Pp), making them purple, while one offspring will be recessive (pp) and white. This results in 75% purple and 25% white.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,38,'A farmer wants to understand the inheritance of flower color in her garden. She knows that purple flowers (P) are dominant over white flowers (p). She performs a genetic cross between two heterozygous (Pp) purple-flowered plants. Using a Punnett square, she wants to calculate the ratio of offspring with different genotypes and phenotypes.\n\nPunnett Square: Pp x Pp Cross\n\nP ( Parent 1) P (Parent 1) P (Parent 2) PP (Purple) Pp (Purple) p (Parent 2) Pp (Purple) Pp (wHite)','What is the expected genotype ratio for the offspring in this Pp × Pp cross?','1 PP : 2 Pp : 1 pp','S3 PP : 1 Pp','2 PP : 2 pp','4 Pp : 0 pp','A','The Punnett square breakdown reveals that 25% of the offspring will be homozygous dominant (PP), 50% heterozygous (Pp), and 25% homozygous recessive (pp), leading to a 1:2:1 genotype ratio.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,39,'A farmer wants to understand the inheritance of flower color in her garden. She knows that purple flowers (P) are dominant over white flowers (p). She performs a genetic cross between two heterozygous (Pp) purple-flowered plants. Using a Punnett square, she wants to calculate the ratio of offspring with different genotypes and phenotypes.\n\nPunnett Square: Pp x Pp Cross\n\nP ( Parent 1) P (Parent 1) P (Parent 2) PP (Purple) Pp (Purple) p (Parent 2) Pp (Purple) Pp (wHite)','If the farmer crosses a homozygous dominant (PP) flower with a homozygous recessive (pp) flower, what will be the expected phenotype of all the offspring?','All white flowers','50% purple, 50% white','All purple flowers','75% purple, 25% white','C','PP × pp produces only heterozygous (Pp) offspring, each inheriting one dominant allele (P) and one recessive allele (p). Since purple (P) is dominant, all offspring will express the purple phenotype.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,40,'A group of students is working on genetics experiment to determine the inheritance of fur color in guinea pigs. In this species, black fur (B) is dominant over brown fur (b). They create a Punnett square diagram to visualize the results of a cross between two heterozygous black guinea pigs (Bb × Bb). Their goal is to predict the ratios of offspring genotypes and phenotypes and analyze how dominant and recessive traits are inherited.','Based on Punnett square, what is the expected phenotype ratio of the offspring from a Bb × Bb cross?','100% black, 0% brown','50% black, 50% brown','75% black, 25% brown','25% black, 75% brown','C','A Bb × Bb cross produces one BB (homozygous dominant), two Bb (heterozygous), and one bb (homozygous recessive). Since black (B) is dominant, three out of four offspring will have black fur, while one out of four will have brown fur, creating a 3:1 phenotype ratio.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,41,'A group of students is working on genetics experiment to determine the inheritance of fur color in guinea pigs. In this species, black fur (B) is dominant over brown fur (b). They create a Punnett square diagram to visualize the results of a cross between two heterozygous black guinea pigs (Bb × Bb). Their goal is to predict the ratios of offspring genotypes and phenotypes and analyze how dominant and recessive traits are inherited.','What is the expected genotype ratio for the offspring from a Bb × Bb cross?','1 BB : 2 Bb : 1 bb','3 BB: 1Bb','2BB: 2bb','4 Bb: 0bb','A','The Punnett square for these cross reveals that 25% of the offspring will be homozygous dominant (BB), 50% will be heterozygous (Bb), and 25% will be homozygous recessive (bb). This results in a 1:2:1 genotype ratio, meaning that most offspring will carry the dominant trait, but recessive traits can still appear.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,42,'A group of students is working on genetics experiment to determine the inheritance of fur color in guinea pigs. In this species, black fur (B) is dominant over brown fur (b). They create a Punnett square diagram to visualize the results of a cross between two heterozygous black guinea pigs (Bb × Bb). Their goal is to predict the ratios of offspring genotypes and phenotypes and analyze how dominant and recessive traits are inherited.','If a homozygous dominant black guinea pig (BB) is crossed with a homozygous recessive brown guinea pig (bb), what would be the expected phenotype of all offspring?','All black','All brown','75% black, 25% brown','50% black, 50% brown','A','BB × bb produces only heterozygous (Bb) offspring, meaning every guinea pig inherits one dominant allele (B) and one recessive allele (b). Because black (B) is dominant, all offspring will have black fur, even though they carry the recessive brown allele.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,43,'A group of students is conducting an experiment on pea plants. They cross a heterozygous tall plant (Tt) with a homozygous recessive short plant (tt) to predict the possible height outcomes of the offspring. They use a Punnett square to calculate the expected genotypic and phenotypic ratios for this trait, where tall (T) is dominant and short (t) is recessive.','What is the expected phenotype ratio of the offspring when crossing a Tt (heterozygous tall) plant with a tt (homozygous short) plant?','100% tall, 0% short','50% tall, 50% short','75% tall, 25% short','25% tall, 75% short','B','A Tt × tt cross results in two Tt (tall) and two tt (short) offspring, meaning half the offspring inherit at least one dominant allele (T) and will be tall, while the other half inherit two recessive alleles (tt) and will be short, producing a 1:1 phenotype ratio.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,44,'A group of students is conducting an experiment on pea plants. They cross a heterozygous tall plant (Tt) with a homozygous recessive short plant (tt) to predict the possible height outcomes of the offspring. They use a Punnett square to calculate the expected genotypic and phenotypic ratios for this trait, where tall (T) is dominant and short (t) is recessive.','What is the expected genotype ratio from this Tt × tt cross?','1 Tt : 1 tt','3 Tt : 1 tt','2 TT : 2 tt','4 Tt : 0 tt','A','The Punnett square reveals that 50% of the offspring will be heterozygous (Tt), and 50% will be homozygous recessive (tt), leading to a 1:1 genotype ratio.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,45,'A group of students is conducting an experiment on pea plants. They cross a heterozygous tall plant (Tt) with a homozygous recessive short plant (tt) to predict the possible height outcomes of the offspring. They use a Punnett square to calculate the expected genotypic and phenotypic ratios for this trait, where tall (T) is dominant and short (t) is recessive.','If two heterozygous tall plants (Tt × Tt) were crossed instead, what would be the expected phenotype ratio?','100% tall, 0% short','50% tall, 50% short','75% tall, 25% short','25% tall, 75% short','C','A Tt × Tt cross produces one TT (homozygous dominant), two Tt (heterozygous), and one tt (homozygous recessive). Since tall (T) is dominant, three out of four offspring will be tall, while one out of four will be short, leading to a 3:1 phenotype ratio.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,46,'A team of researchers is reviewing scientific articles to study how mutations affect living organisms. They find sources explaining that mutations can be beneficial, harmful, or neutral, depending on how they alter genetic material. Some mutations help species adapt to their environment, while others can lead to genetic disorders. The researchers analyze these sources to classify different types of mutations.','Based on what the researchers learned, which of the following is an example of a helpful (beneficial) mutation?','A mutation that causes cancer in the lungs','A mutation that helps bacteria survive medicine (antibiotics)','A mutation that causes a disease like cystic fibrosis','A mutation that does not change anything in the body','B','This is an example of a beneficial mutation because it helps the bacteria live longer, even when medicine is used to kill them. The mutation gives the bacteria resistance, which means they can fight off the effects of the antibiotics. This helps them survive and grow, making the mutation helpful for the bacteria. Although this can be a problem for humans trying to treat infections, it shows how some mutations can help living things adapt to their environment. The other choices are not beneficial: option A causes cancer, option C leads to a disease, and option D does not change anything in the body.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,47,'A team of researchers is reviewing scientific articles to study how mutations affect living organisms. They find sources explaining that mutations can be beneficial, harmful, or neutral, depending on how they alter genetic material. Some mutations help species adapt to their environment, while others can lead to genetic disorders. The researchers analyze these sources to classify different types of mutations.','According to secondary sources, what determines whether a mutation is harmful, beneficial, or neutral?','The amount of genetic material affected','The way the mutation influences the function of a protein or trait','Whether the mutation occurs in animals or plants','The number of mutations an organism has','B','A mutation’s effect depends on how it changes protein function or gene expression. Some mutations improve an organism''s survival (beneficial), some cause diseases (harmful), while others have no noticeable effect (neutral).',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,48,'A team of environmental scientists is studying a tropical rainforest and a desert ecosystem. They observe that the rainforest has a vast variety of plant and animal species, while the desert has fewer. Over time, they notice that ecosystems with higher biodiversity recover more quickly from natural disasters, such as droughts or wildfires. The scientists analyze how biodiversity influences ecosystem resilience, food chains, and adaptation to changing conditions.','Why does high biodiversity contribute to the stability of an ecosystem?','It reduces competition for resources','It allows more species to depend on a single food source','It increases resilience to environmental changes','It prevents organisms from adapting to new conditions','C','High biodiversity ensures that ecosystems have a variety of species with different roles. If one species declines due to disease or climate change, other species can fill its ecological function, helping the ecosystem recover.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,49,'A team of environmental scientists is studying a tropical rainforest and a desert ecosystem. They observe that the rainforest has a vast variety of plant and animal species, while the desert has fewer. Over time, they notice that ecosystems with higher biodiversity recover more quickly from natural disasters, such as droughts or wildfires. The scientists analyze how biodiversity influences ecosystem resilience, food chains, and adaptation to changing conditions.','According to scientists, which ecosystem would be more vulnerable to collapse if a single species went extinct?','A rainforest with rich biodiversity','A grassland with many plants and herbivore species','A coral reef with thousands of interconnected species','A monoculture farm with only one plant species','D','Monoculture farms lack biodiversity, meaning they depend on a single species for survival. If disease or pests wipe out the species, the entire ecosystem collapses, unlike diverse natural ecosystems where multiple species support one another.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,2,50,'A team of environmental scientists is studying a tropical rainforest and a desert ecosystem. They observe that the rainforest has a vast variety of plant and animal species, while the desert has fewer. Over time, they notice that ecosystems with higher biodiversity recover more quickly from natural disasters, such as droughts or wildfires. The scientists analyze how biodiversity influences ecosystem resilience, food chains, and adaptation to changing conditions.','How does biodiversity help ecosystems maintain food web balance?','By preventing all predators from hunting','By ensuring multiple species contribute to nutrient cycling','By allowing one species to dominate all resources','By eliminating competition among organisms','B','In high-biodiversity ecosystems, different species play unique roles in the food web, ensuring balanced energy flow and nutrient cycling. Predators, herbivores, decomposers, and producers all interact, helping maintain ecosystem stability.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,51,'Students are examining different food pyramids to understand the flow of energy in ecosystems. Their teacher explains that energy is transferred from producers (plants) to primary consumers (herbivores), then to higher-level consumers (carnivores). The students use diagrams to compare energy loss at each trophic level and discuss why top predators have fewer numbers than primary consumers. Food Pyramid','In a food pyramid, why is the energy available to top predators (tertiary consumers) much lower than the energy available to primary consumers?','Energy is used up and lost as heat at each level','Producers store more energy for predators than herbivores','predators do not need energy to survive','Energy increases as it moves up the pyramid','A','Energy transfer in a food pyramid follows the 10% rule, meaning only 10% of energy is passed to the next trophic level, while the rest is lost as heat, movement, and metabolic processes.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,52,'Students are examining different food pyramids to understand the flow of energy in ecosystems. Their teacher explains that energy is transferred from producers (plants) to primary consumers (herbivores), then to higher-level consumers (carnivores). The students use diagrams to compare energy loss at each trophic level and discuss why top predators have fewer numbers than primary consumers. Food Pyramid','According to food pyramids, why do ecosystems typically support fewer top predators compared to primary consumers?','Carnivores create their own food','Producers absorb too much energy','Less energy is available at higher trophic levels','Top predators reproduce faster than herbivores','C','Fewer top predators exist because each trophic level receives less energy than the previous one, making it difficult to sustain large populations. Primary consumers have more food sources, leading to larger populations compared to top predators.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,53,'A town near a coastal region has noticed a decline in the population of an economically important fish species due to overfishing and habitat destruction. Local scientists and community leaders hold meetings to explore sustainable solutions, such as fishing regulations, marine protected areas, and habitat restoration projects. They also encourage businesses and residents to take active roles in conservation efforts to ensure both ecological balance and economic sustainability.','Which of the following strategies would be the most effective in ensuring the long-term survival of an endangered species in the local community?','Allowing unlimited fishing and hunting to increase profits','Implementing laws that regulate hunting, fishing, and habitat destruction','Removing all predators to help the species grow faster','Introducing non-native species to increase genetic diversity','B','Conservation laws such as hunting restrictions, seasonal fishing bans, and habitat restoration projects ensure that species populations recover sustainably while balancing ecological and economic needs.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,54,'A town near a coastal region has noticed a decline in the population of an economically important fish species due to overfishing and habitat destruction. Local scientists and community leaders hold meetings to explore sustainable solutions, such as fishing regulations, marine protected areas, and habitat restoration projects. They also encourage businesses and residents to take active roles in conservation efforts to ensure both ecological balance and economic sustainability.','A local conservation group wants to protect a species that is both endangered and economically important. What approach would be the most effective?','Educating the community about sustainable practices and alternative livelihoods','Encouraging businesses to use more of the species for higher profits','Allowing habitat destruction to make space for tourism and agriculture','Ignoring the issue, hoping the species will naturally adapt','A','Community education and engagement help people understand sustainable conservation methods while promoting alternative ways to support the economy, ensuring long-term protection of the species.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,55,'A community agricultural program is testing different methods to improve food sustainability. They study food preservation techniques to extend shelf life, experiment with modern farming practices to boost crop yield, and explore hydroponics as a soil-free alternative for growing vegetables in urban areas. Scientists and farmers work together to analyze which methods are the most efficient and environmentally friendly.','Which food preservation method slows bacterial growth by removing moisture from food?','Freezing','Drying','Fermentation','Pickling','B','Drying removes moisture, preventing the growth of bacteria and fungi that cause food spoilage. Methods like sun-drying, dehydration, or freezing help preserve food for longer periods without refrigeration.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,56,'A community agricultural program is testing different methods to improve food sustainability. They study food preservation techniques to extend shelf life, experiment with modern farming practices to boost crop yield, and explore hydroponics as a soil-free alternative for growing vegetables in urban areas. Scientists and farmers work together to analyze which methods are the most efficient and environmentally friendly.','In hydroponic farming, why is nutrient-rich water used instead of soil?','To increase plant exposure to sunlight','To reduce the risk of overwatering','To provide essential nutrients directly to plant roots','To prevent plants from absorbing nutrients','C','Hydroponics eliminates soil, instead using water infused with nutrients to deliver essential elements (like nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium) directly to plant roots, optimizing growth and minimizing space requirements.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,57,'Consider the concepts of energy transformation and the applications of electromagnetic radiation. Which of the following statements correctly describes these concepts?','Which of the following scenarios demonstrate the transformation of kinetic energy into potential energy?','A ball rolling down a hill','A stretched rubber band ready to be released','A car accelerating on a flat road','A roller coaster climbing to the top of a hill','D','The correct answer is D because this scenario shows kinetic energy (from the moving coaster) being transformed into potential energy as it gains height. Options A and C involve kinetic energy being maintained or increasing, while B describes a stored potential energy situation.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,58,'Consider the concepts of energy transformation and the applications of electromagnetic radiation. Which of the following statements correctly describes these concepts?','Which situation exemplifies the transformation of potential energy to kinetic energy?','A water dam storing water at a height','A bouncing ball reaching its highest point','A ball dropping from a table to the ground','A person holding a book above their head','C','The correct answer is C because this scenario illustrates potential energy (stored in the height of the ball) being transformed into kinetic energy as it falls. Options A and B describe potential energy situations, while D describes potential energy held by the book but not a transformation.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,59,'Consider the concepts of energy transformation and the applications of electromagnetic radiation. Which of the following statements correctly describes these concepts?','In which application is electromagnetic radiation used for communication?','Using X-rays to examine bones','Using radio waves to transmit music','Using microwaves to heat food','Using infrared radiation for night vision','B','The correct answer is B because radio waves, a type of electromagnetic radiation, are used to transmit music and other signals for communication. Options A and C involve medical or cooking applications of EMR, while D refers to a different use of EMR not related to communication.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,60,'In a class discussion about reducing electrical energy use in Filipino houses and communities, which of the following strategies would be the most effective in achieving energy conservation?','Which of the following actions can help reduce electricity consumption in homes?','Keeping lights on when not in use','Using energy-efficient appliances','Frequently using air conditioning regardless of weather','Using incandescent light bulbs','B','The correct answer is B because energy-efficient appliances are designed to use less electricity, thereby reducing overall energy consumption in homes. Options A, C, and D contribute to higher energy usage rather than conservation.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,61,'In a class discussion about reducing electrical energy use in Filipino houses and communities, which of the following strategies would be the most effective in achieving energy conservation?','What is the benefit of utilizing natural light in homes?','It increases the need for artificial lighting','It helps reduce electricity use for lighting','It requires more electricity for heating','It makes homes warmer in the summer','B','The correct answer is B as utilizing natural light decreases the need for artificial lighting, leading to lower electricity consumption. Options A and C incorrectly imply increased energy use, while D does not reflect the benefits of natural light.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,62,'In a class discussion about reducing electrical energy use in Filipino houses and communities, which of the following strategies would be the most effective in achieving energy conservation?','How can promoting renewable energy sources, like solar panels, impact electricity usage?','It increases reliance on traditional energy sources','It decreases the overall cost of electricity bills','It has no effect on energy consumption','It increases the use of non-renewable resources','B','The correct answer is B because promoting renewable energy sources like solar panels allows households to generate their own electricity, which can significantly lower electricity bills and reduce reliance on traditional energy sources. Options A, C, and D inaccurately reflect the impact of renewable energy on electricity consumption.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,63,'When handling household electrical devices, which of the following safety precautions is essential to prevent accidents and injuries?','What is the most important safety precaution when using electrical devices near water?','Using devices with wet hands','Keeping devices away from water','Plugging devices into ungrounded outlets','Ignoring damaged cords','B','The correct answer is B because keeping electrical devices away from water is crucial for preventing electric shocks. Options A and C increase the risk of accidents, while D ignores the importance of checking for damage.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,64,'When handling household electrical devices, which of the following safety precautions is essential to prevent accidents and injuries?','Why is it important to unplug electrical devices when they are not in use?','To increase their lifespan','To prevent them from being stolen','To reduce the risk of overheating and fires','To make them easier to clean','C','The correct answer is C because unplugging devices when not in use helps prevent overheating, which can lead to fires. Options A, B, and D do not address the primary safety concern associated with leaving devices plugged in.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,65,'Understanding the mechanisms that drive the movement of tectonic plates is essential for comprehending geological processes, predicting earthquakes, and understanding the formation of various landforms.','What is the primary mechanism that drives the movement of tectonic plates through the heat from the Earth''s core?','Slab pull','Ridge push','Mantle convection','Atmospheric pressure','C','The correct answer is C because mantle convection is the primary mechanism that drives the movement of tectonic plates through the heat generated by the Earth''s core, creating convection currents. Options A and B describe other mechanisms, and D is incorrect because atmospheric pressure does not drive plate movement.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,66,'Understanding the mechanisms that drive the movement of tectonic plates is essential for comprehending geological processes, predicting earthquakes, and understanding the formation of various landforms.','What is the name of the force that helps a sinking tectonic plate move down into the Earth at a subduction zone?','Mantle convection','Ridge push','Slab pull','Erosion','C','Slab pull is the force that happens when part of a tectonic plate sinks into the mantle, the deeper layer of the Earth. As it goes down, it pulls the rest of the plate with it. This helps move the plate. Mantle convection and ridge push are also forces that move plates, but they work in different ways. Erosion is not related to plate movement—it’s about wearing away rocks and soil. So, slab pull is the correct answer.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,67,'Understanding the mechanisms that drive the movement of tectonic plates is essential for comprehending geological processes, predicting earthquakes, and understanding the formation of various landforms.','How does the atmosphere indirectly influence tectonic plate movement?','By causing tectonic plates to collide','By affecting weather patterns that lead to earthquakes','By influencing surface processes like erosion that can affect landforms','By directly pushing plates through atmospheric pressure','C','The correct answer is C because the atmosphere influences weather and climate, which can lead to erosion and sedimentation that affect landforms and the stability of tectonic plate boundaries. Option A is incorrect as it misrepresents the relationship between the atmosphere and plate movement. Option B is incorrect as weather patterns do not directly cause earthquakes. Option D is incorrect because atmospheric pressure does not directly push tectonic plates.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,68,NULL,'Which of the following is the best way to help many families in a barangay use less electricity?','Change old light bulbs to LED bulbs in one house','Remind your own family to turn off lights when not needed','Teach neighbors and friends how to save electricity','Use electric fans instead of air conditioners in your house','C','Teaching neighbors and friends how to save electricity is the best way to help many families because it spreads helpful knowledge to more people. When more households learn simple ways to reduce energy use—like turning off lights, unplugging appliances, or switching to LED bulbs—the whole barangay benefits. Unlike actions that only help one house, sharing what you know creates a bigger and lasting impact on the community.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,69,'The suitability of a metal for a specific use often depends on how well its properties match the requirements of that application.','A company is designing a new cooking pot that must heat food quickly and spread heat evenly across the bottom. They choose between different metals. Which metal would best meet these needs?','Aluminum','Iron','Gold','Silver','D','Silver is the best choice because it has the highest thermal conductivity among the options, meaning it transfers heat very quickly and evenly. This makes it excellent for cooking. However, silver is expensive, so aluminum is often used instead because it also conducts heat well and is more affordable. Iron heats slowly and unevenly, and gold, while a good conductor, is not practical due to its cost. So, silver is the most appropriate metal based on the heating needs described.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,70,'The suitability of a metal for a specific use often depends on how well its properties match the requirements of that application.','Considering the need for a material that can efficiently carry electrical current over long distances with minimal loss of energy, which of these metals is best suited for making electrical wires?','Iron','Aluminum','Copper','Gold','C','Copper is an excellent conductor of electricity, meaning it allows electrical current to flow through it with very little resistance, minimizing energy loss over long distances. Aluminum is also a good conductor and is used in some high- voltage transmission lines due to its lighter weight, but copper is generally preferred for household wiring due to its better conductivity and ductility (ability to be drawn into wires).',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,71,'The suitability of a metal for a specific use often depends on how well its properties match the requirements of that application.','If a metal is needed for an outdoor gate that will be exposed to rain and air for many years without weakening due to rust, which of the following would be the most practical choice?','Iron','Copper','Aluminum','Silver','C','Aluminum is known for its excellent corrosion resistance. It forms a thin layer of aluminum oxide on its surface when exposed to air, which is very hard and prevents further oxidation (rusting). Iron readily reacts with oxygen and moisture to form rust (iron oxide), which weakens the metal over time. Therefore, an iron gate would need protective coatings to last outdoors. Copper forms a greenish layer called patina over time, which protects it from further corrosion but might not be the desired appearance. Silver tarnishes when exposed to air and sulfur compounds, so it''s not the most practical choice for a long-lasting outdoor structure.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,72,NULL,'How is the standard International System of Units (SI) for length, mass, and time related to ensuring consistent and universally understood measurements in science and everyday life?','They are arbitrary units chosen randomly for convenience within specific regions.','They are based on historical customs that vary significantly between countries.','They provide a common language of measurement, enabling accurate communication and comparisons globally.','They are primarily used in academic research but have little relevance to practical applications.','C','This is the correct answer because the standard SI units (meter for length, kilogram for mass, and second for time) serve as a universal language of measurement. This standardization is crucial for accurate communication, consistent comparisons and precision in various fields.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,73,'The interconnectedness of the steps in a scientific investigation ensures a logical and evidence-based approach to understanding the natural world.','How does the "Method or Procedures" step directly influence the "Results including Data" step in a scientific investigation?','The "Method" determines the initial question being asked in the investigation.','The "Method" outlines how the data will be collected and what types of observations will be made, directly shaping the "Results."','The "Method" involves analyzing the collected data to form a conclusion.','The "Method" lists the equipment needed to interpret the "Results."','B','The Method or Procedures step provides the detailed plan for how the investigation will be conducted. This includes specifying what measurements will be taken, what observations will be recorded, and how they will be collected. Therefore, the method directly dictates the nature and type of Results including Data that will be obtained. A poorly designed method will likely lead to unreliable or irrelevant data.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,74,'The interconnectedness of the steps in a scientific investigation ensures a logical and evidence-based approach to understanding the natural world.','What is the crucial relationship between the "Aim or Problem" and the "Conclusion" of a scientific investigation?','The "Aim" provides the list of materials, while the "Conclusion" describes the steps taken.','The "Aim" is a prediction about the outcome, while the "Conclusion" records the measurements.','The "Aim" states the question or purpose, and the "Conclusion" provides an answer or summary based on the evidence gathered.','The "Aim" is formulated after analyzing the results and drawing a conclusion.','C','The Aim or Problem step sets the stage for the entire investigation by clearly stating what the scientist wants to find out or the question they are trying to answer. The Conclusion is the final step where the scientist analyzes the collected data and summarizes their findings in relation to the initial aim or problem. The conclusion essentially provides an answer to the question posed in the aim, based on the evidence gathered through the investigation.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS2',3,3,75,NULL,'Why is it important to measure the force between two objects that are touching or pushing each other?','It helps us know the color and texture of the objects','It helps us understand how the objects move or change shape','It tells us what chemicals the objects are made of','It shows us how hot or cold the objects are form','B','Measuring force is important because it helps us understand how objects move, stop, or change shape when they push or pull each other. For example, when you kick a ball, the force from your foot makes the ball move. Knowing how strong that force is helps us explain why the ball moves fast or slow, and in which direction. This is how scientists and engineers predict motion and design safe and useful tools, machines, and buildings.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,1,NULL,'What is the value of (-3)²?','8','12','9','20','C','(-3)² = 9, because squaring a negative number yields a positive result.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,2,NULL,'Which of the following is a perfect square?','15','25','18','24','B','25 is a perfect square because it equals 5 × 5.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,3,NULL,'What do you call a well – defined distinct objects?','numbers','objects','set','operation of sets','C','A set is a well-defined collection of distinct objects.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,4,NULL,'Which of the following is a subset of the set (2, 4, 6, 8, 10)?','(1, 2)','(2, 6)','(3, 4)','(4, 5)','B','A subset contains only elements from the original set (2, 4, 6, 8, 10).',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,5,NULL,'Find the subset of Z= (5,6,7)','(5,6,7,8)','(6,7)','(4,5)','(7,8)','B','A subset contains only elements from the original set (5, 6,',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,6,NULL,'Let A=(1,2,3) and B=(1,2,3,4,5). Which of the following is true?','A = B','A ⊆ B','B ⊆ A','A ∩ B = ∅','B','Set A is a subset of Set B because all elements in A (1, 2, 3) are also found in Set B. • A is not equal to B because B has more elements (4 and 5). • B is not a subset of A because B has elements not in A. • A ∩ B is not empty (∅) because they share common elements',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,7,NULL,'Given: X=(a,b,c) and Y = (b, c, d). What is X∪Y?','(a,b,c,d)','(b,c)','(a,d)','(a,b,c)','A','The union (∪) of two sets is a set containing all elements from both sets, without duplication. • X ∪ Y = {a, b, c} ∪ {b, c, d} = {a, b, c, d}',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,8,NULL,'Among the numbers given below, which is irrational?','√25','7/3','√2','0.75','C','√2 cannot be written as a fraction and its decimal never ends or repeats. √25 = 5, 7/3 and 0.75 are rational.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,9,NULL,'Which of the following is a real number?','√−1','5/2','√−3','∞','B','5/2 is a real number. Square roots of negative numbers are not real, and ∞ is not a number.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,10,NULL,'Claire says: “All whole numbers are also integers. Rovina says: “All integers are also whole numbers.” Whose statement is correct?','Claire','Rovina','Neither','Both Claire and Rovina','A','Whole numbers = {0, 1, 2, 3, …} Integers = {..., –3, –2, –1, 0, 1, 2, 3, …}. All whole numbers are integers, but not all integers are whole numbers (because integers include negatives).So, Claire is correct, Rovina is not.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,11,NULL,'Which number is not a real number?','−3/5','π','√−2','0','C','The square root of a negative number is not a real number.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,12,NULL,'Which set contains all real numbers?','Integers','Irrational numbers','Real numbers','Rational numbers','C','The real number set includes rational (e.g., $, 5) and irrational (e.g., √2, π) numbers. Integers and rational/irrational numbers are subsets of real numbers.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,13,NULL,'Miss Lucy asked: “Which numbers are both rational and real?” Who gave the best answer?','Mirasol: All fractions','Rosalina: Imaginary number','Pinky: Only decimal number','Nelson: Only square roots of a number','A','Fractions (like 1/2, 3/4) are rational and are part of the real number system. Imaginary numbers (B) are not real. Not all decimals are rational—non- repeating, non-terminating decimals are irrational. Some square roots are irrational (like √2), so Nelson’s answer is incomplete.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,14,NULL,'On a number line, the numbers are marked, –5, –3, –1, 1, and 3. What set do these numbers belong to?','Natural Numbers','Integers','Whole Numbers','Rational Numbers','B','Integers include negative numbers, zero, and positive whole numbers: {..., –3, –2, –1, 0, 1, 2, ...}.Natural numbers don’t include negatives. Rational numbers I nclude fractions and decimals too, which aren''t listed here.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,15,NULL,'Which number line correctly shows the set of integers from –3 to 3?','–3, –2, –1, 0, 1, 2, 3','–3, –2, –1, 1, 2, 3','0, 1, 2, 3','–3, –2, 0, 1, 2','A','This is the complete list of integers from –3 to 3.Option B skips 0, Option C only includes positives, and Option D misses –1 and 3.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,16,NULL,'Which number is accurately between –3 and 1 on the number line?','–1','–2','–0.5','0','C','–0.5 is a decimal between –1 and 0, and clearly between –3 and 1. The other choices are valid but not as precise (they are endpoints or farther away).',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,17,NULL,'Which of the following describes the |−4|?','The distance between -4& 4','The distance between 0 & 4','The distance between 0&-4','The distance between 4&-4','C','Absolute value is the distance from 0 on the number line.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,18,NULL,'Which of the following is a set of integers?','{−2, −1, 0, 1, 2}','{√2, π, 3}','{1/2, 2/3, 2/5}','{−1.1, 0, 2.5}','A','Integers are whole numbers and their negatives, with no fractions or decimals.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,19,NULL,'Glenda says: “All integers are positive.”Apida says: “Integers include negative numbers, zero, and positive numbers.”Who is correct?','Glenda','Both A and B','Apida','Neither','C','Integers include – , 0, and +',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,20,NULL,'What set describes the numbers: (...,−3,−2,−1,0,1,2, 3,...)?','Natural Numbers','Rational Numbers','Whole Numbers','Integers','D','Describes all whole + negative numbers',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,21,NULL,'What is the absolute value of /–8/?','–8','0','8','-1','C','Absolute value does not follow whether it is positive or negative, distance is always positive',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,22,NULL,'On a number line, how far is –5 from 0?','–5 units','0 units','5 units','10 units','C','Absolute distance from 0 to –5 is',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,23,NULL,'Amie Rose says: “The absolute value of a number is always positive.” Charlene says: “The absolute value of 0 is 1.” Who is correct?','Amie Rose','Both are correct','Charlene','Neither','A','Absolute value is always ≥',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,24,NULL,'Which statement best describes absolute value?','The number''s opposite','The number’s direction on the number line','The distance from 0 on the number line','The value of only positive numbers','C','That’s the definition of absolute value',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,1,25,NULL,'Which expression is equivalent to (2a²)³?','2a','8a⁶','4a','3','B','(2a²)³ = 2³ × (a²)³ = 8a⁶.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('JHS','LS3',1,2,26,NULL,'What is a⁰, given a ≠ 0?','0','a','1','Undefined','C','Any nonzero number raised to the power 0 is 1.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,27,NULL,'Simplify x⁴ · x⁵','x⁹','x','x²','10x','A','When multiplying powers with the same base, add the exponents: x⁴ · x⁵ = x⁹.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,28,NULL,'Marvilyn reads a problem that says: “Ben had 5 more apples than Dave. Together, they had 23 apples.”Which of the following best represents the mathematical operation for “Ben had 5 more apples than Dave”?','Subtraction','Addition','Division','Multiplication','B','"5 more" implies addition',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,29,NULL,'Which of the following is a mathematical keyword for addition?','Difference','More than','Multiply','Less than','B','Common phrase for addition',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,30,NULL,'A word problem says:“A group of ALS learners gathered three times as many bottle caps as last year. They now have 320 caps.”What is the keyword showing the correct operation to compare this year and last year?','Times','Increased by','More than','Left','A','"Three times" implies multiplication',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,31,NULL,'Which pair of terms is similar?','2x and 3','5a and –2a','3x and 3x²','x and y','B','Same variables and powers',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,32,NULL,'Which of the following best describes why 3xy and 3yx are similar terms?','The variables and powers are the same, just in a different order','They have different variable orders, so they are not similar.','The coefficients are the same, so they must be different.','They are both constants.','A','Same terms in different order',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,33,NULL,'Which group below comprises only similar terms?','3x,5x,−2x','x,𝑥 ,3x','2y,2z,2','4a,𝑎 ,a','A','All similar terms (same variable)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,34,NULL,'What is the next number in the pattern: 3, 6, 9, 12, ___?','13','14','15','16','C','Pattern increases by',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,35,NULL,'Which of the following is a rational algebraic expression?','(x² + 1)/(x – 2)','x + π','√(x + 3)','1/√x','A','Rational expression (polynomial/polynomial)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,36,NULL,'What is the next number in the pattern: 15, 30, 45, 60, ___?','70','72','74','75','D','Pattern increases by',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,37,NULL,'A drone delivery app tracks package drop-off location using coordinates on a Cartesian Plane. If a package was delivered to the point (–4, 2), in which direction did the drone most likely move from the origin (0, 0)?','4 units right and 2 units up','4 units left and 2 units down','4 units left and 2 units up','2 units right and 4 units up','C','From (0,0) to (–4,2)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,38,NULL,'A student recorded coordinates of different weather stations on a grid map. Based on the given coordinate points of the different stations, which station is located at (2, –3)?','Station A','Station B','Station C','Station D','C','Assuming (2,–3) corresponds to Station C',NULL,0,0),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,39,NULL,'A robot follows these instructions from the origin (0, 0): Move 5 steps to the right , Move 3 steps down .Which of the following is the final position of the robot on the Cartesian Coordinate Plane?','(–5, –3)','(5, –3)','(5, 3)','(–5, 3)','B','5 right, 3 down from (0,0)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,40,NULL,'Jimbo needs to find the equation of a line that passes through the point (2,3) and has a slope of 1/2. Which method would be most appropriate?','Slope-intercept form','Two-point form','Point-slope form','Parallel line method','C','Best when given a point and slope',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,41,NULL,'Given are methods used to find the equation of a line as indicated above. If you are given the slope and y-intercept of a line, which method from the list is the most appropriate to use?','Point-slope form','Slope-intercept form','Two-point form','Standard form','B','y = mx + b form fits known slope and intercept',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,42,NULL,'Given that you know the slope and y-intercept of a line, which method would be the most suitable for finding the equation, and why?','Point-slope form, because it works best with two points','Two-point form, because it uses the x- and y-intercepts','Slope-intercept form, because it directly uses slope and y-intercept','Standard form, because it doesn''t require slope','C','Direct substitution of m and b',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,43,NULL,'Based on the general form of a linear inequality in one or two variables, which of the following represents a linear inequality in one variable?','3x+2>7','2x−4y>6','x+y≤5','x2+3y<4','A','Only one variable (x)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,44,NULL,'A school is designing a policy for students where the number of hours spent on study (x) and extracurricular activities (y) must satisfy the condition: 2x + 3y ≤ 18 Which of the following best represents a correct interpretation of this inequality in real life?','Study and activity hours must both be exactly divisible by 3','The total of 2 study hours and 3 activity hours must equal 18.','Students should only spend more time on study than on activities','The combined weighted time for study and activities should not exceed 18 hours.','D','Interpretation of inequality',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,45,NULL,'A student is analyzing a set of data representing the number of hours studied and the scores received by different students. The relation is as follows:{(2,85),(3,90),(2,88),(4,92)} Using your understanding of the definition of a function, which of the following explains whether the relation is a function or not?','Yes, because all values are different.','Yes, because the outputs are unique.','No, because the outputs are greater than the inputs.','No, because the input 2 is matched with more than one output.','D','Function must have unique output for each input',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,46,NULL,'Which of the following equations correctly represents an inverse variation based on the definitions given?','y=3x','y=4/x','y=2x+5','y=x2','B','Inverse variation follows y = k/x form',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,47,NULL,'Based on the information above, which of the following is considered an undefined term in geometry?','Line','Angle','Circle','Triangle','A','Undefined terms: point, line, and plane',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,48,NULL,'Which of the following terms in the passage refers to the corners of a polygon where two sides meet?','Sides','Angles','Vertices','Diagonals','C','Where sides of a polygon meet',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,49,NULL,'Based on the given description and examples of parallelogram, which of the following statements is TRUE about a rhombus? A rhombus has …','one pair of parallel sides','four right angles and equal diagonal','unequal sides and angles are all 90 degrees','all sides equal and its diagonals are not necessarily equal in length.','D','Rhombus has equal sides, not always equal diagonals',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,2,50,NULL,'Which of the following statements can be concluded correct from the description and examples about parallelograms?','Only squares have diagonals that bisect each other.','All parallelograms must have right angles to be valid shapes.','Squares share the properties of both rectangles and rhombuses.','A rhombus cannot be a parallelogram because its angles are not 90 degrees.','C','True by definition',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,51,NULL,'A cone-shaped cup has a radius of 3 cm and a height of 6 cm. Based on the prescribed formula above, what is the approximate volume of the cup? (Use π ≈ 3.14)','56.52 cm³','113.04 cm³','169.56 cm³','226.08 cm³','A','V = 1/3 × π × r² × h = 1/3 × 3.14 × 9 × 6 = 56.52 cm³.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,52,NULL,'Based on the description of a cone above, which of the following statements correctly describes the volume of a cone? The volume of a cone …','The volume of a cone cannot be calculated because it is not a regular solid.','The volume of a cone is equal to the area of its base multiplied by its height.','The volume of a cone is one-third the volume of a cylinder with the same base and height.','The volume of a cone is the same as the volume of a cylinder with the same base and height .','C','That’s the formula: V = (1/3)πr²h',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,53,NULL,'Which of the following statements best explains the similarity in how the volume of a pyramid and a cone are calculated?','Both shapes have equal volumes because they are three- dimensional.','Both shapes have bases and heights, so they are always cylindering in disguise.','Both have flat surfaces only, so their volumes are calculated the same way.','Both formulas use the factor 1/3, showing that each shape takes up one-third the volume of a prism or cylinder with the same base and height.','D','Cone & pyramid volume = (1/3)(base area)(height)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,54,NULL,'A ladder is leaning against a wall. The base of the ladder is 6 meters from the wall, and the ladder reaches a height of 8 meters on the wall. Using the Pythagorean Theorem above, what is the length of the ladder?','10 meters','12 meters','14 meters','15 meters','A','Apply Pythagorean Theorem: c = √(6² + 8²) = √100 = 10.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,55,NULL,'Wilfredo is creating a rectangular frame for a solar panel and needs to check if the corners form a right angle. He measures two sides of the triangle: 10 meters and 24 meters. He estimates the diagonal should be 26 meters. Is the student correct?','Yes, because 10 + 24 = 26','Yes, because 10² + 24² = 26','No, because 10² + 24² = 576','No, because the diagonal should be 25 meters','B','10² + 24² = 100 + 576 = 676 = 26²',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,56,NULL,'Edgar find a diagram online that claims a triangle with side lengths of 8 meters, 15 meters, and 17 meters is a right triangle. How would Edgar verify if this information is accurate using the Pythagorean Theorem described above?','Check if 8² + 15² is equal to 17²','Subtract 8 from 17, then square the result','Add 8 and 15, then compare the sum to 17','Multiply 8 by 15 and compare the result to 17','A','8² + 15² = 64 + 225 = 289 = 17²',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,57,NULL,'A student places a ladder against a tree to pick fruits. The base of the ladder is 5 meters away from the tree, and the point where the ladder touches the tree is 12 meters above the ground. Using the Pythagorean Theorem, what is the length of the ladder?','11 meters','13 meters','12.5 meters','14 meters','B','√(5² + 12²) = √169 =',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,58,NULL,'A construction worker is using a ladder that leans against a wall. The ladder makes an angle θ with the ground. If the height up the wall (opposite side) is 6 meters and the length of the ladder (hypotenuse) is 10 meters, which trigonometric ratio should the worker use to determine the value of sin(θ)? + &'' + +','6/10','10/6','6 / √(10² + 6²)','6 / (10√(10² + 6²))','A','sin θ = opposite ÷ hypotenuse = 6/10.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,59,NULL,'Zaldy needs to calculate the angle of elevation from the ground to a drone flying directly above a point that is 8 meters away horizontally and 6 meters high. Which trigonometric ratio should Zaldy use to find the angle of elevation? + +','sin θ = 6/10','tan θ = 8/6','tan θ = 6/8','cos θ = 6/8','C','With the height (opposite = 6) and the horizontal distance (adjacent = 8), use tan θ = opposite ÷ adjacent = 6/8.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,60,NULL,'A worker is installing a pole for a streetlight. The pole stands 12 meters tall (opposite) and is leaning against a building. The distance from the base of the pole to the building is 9 meters (adjacent). Which trigonometric ratio should the worker use to find the angle between the pole and the ground? &$ &$ ) )','sin 𝜃 = &#','tan 𝜃 = )','cos 𝜃 = &$','cot 𝜃 = &$','B','',NULL,0,0),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,61,NULL,'Which of the following represents the ratio of the adjacent side to the hypotenuse in a right triangle? /01/2345 /01/2345','tan 𝜃 = 67768953','sin 𝜃 = :;76534<83','cot 𝜃 = 67768953 /01/2345 /01/2345','cos 𝜃 = :;76534<83','D','That’s the correct definition',NULL,0,0),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,62,NULL,'Which of the following statements is correct based on the given properties of a circle?','The secant line XY is tangent to the circle at two points.','The tangent line PT is perpendicular to the radius OT at point T.','The central angle ∠ABC is always half the measure of the inscribed angle ∠ADB.','The inscribed angle ∠ADB is always equal in measure to the central angle ∠ABC.','B','Tangent is perpendicular to the radius at point of contact',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,63,NULL,'Alvin is an engineer, designing a roundabout. He places a straight road (PT) so that it just touches the roundabout at one point T and connects it to the center using a radius OT. Based on the information above, what geometric relationship should he use to ensure the road functions correctly?','PT is parallel to OT','PT bisects the central angle ∠ABC','PT is a secant of the circle','PT forms a right angle with radius OT','D','Tangent is perpendicular to the radius at point of contact',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,64,NULL,'Mark is a city planner wants to install a bench that aligns perfectly with a tangent to a circular park. To ensure safety and precision, the bench must be perpendicular to the radius drawn from the center of the park to the point of contact. Based on the information above, which line best represents the correct position of the bench?','Along line PT','Along radius OT','Along chord DB','Along secant XY','A','Line PT is tangent',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,65,NULL,'Amulek is planning the layout of a circular fountain. To add a decorative tile path that just touches the edge of the fountain without cutting through it, which geometric element should they follow?','The secant line XY','The central angle ∠ABC','The tangent line PT','The inscribed angle ∠ADB','C','Tangent touches only once',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,66,NULL,'Ruel is analyzing the layout of different lines and angles in a circular park design. If the goal is to identify a line that only touches the park''s edge once and forms a right angle with a radius at the point of contact, which element should the student choose?','Secant line XY','Central angle ∠ABC','Tangent line PT','Inscribed angle ∠ADB','C','Defined as line touching only one point on a circle',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,67,NULL,'Karina jogs at the Iligan Medical College rotunda. She stops at the two points that represent opposite ends of a diameter of the rotunda. Suppose the coordinates of these points are 𝐴(2, 3) and 𝐵(8, 7). To find the center, you need to use the midpoint formula. Which of the following is the formula in getting the midpoint? = -= ; -;','M = ((x₁ + x₂)/2, (y₁ + y₂)/2)','M = (y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁)','M = ((y₁ + y₂)/2, (x₁ + x₂)/2)','M = √((x₂ − x₁)² + (y₂ − y₁)²)','A','The midpoint is the average of the x-values and the average of the y-values.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,68,NULL,'Karina jogs at the Iligan Medical College rotonda. She stops at the two points that represent opposite ends of a diameter of the rotunda. Suppose the coordinates of these points are 𝐴(2, 3) and 𝐵(8, 7). What is the center of the rotunda?','( 10, 10)','( 3, 2)','( 6, 4)','( 5, 5)','D','Midpoint of (2+8)/2 = 5, (3+7)/2 =',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,69,NULL,'Karina jogs at the Iligan Medical College rotonda. She stops at the two points that represent opposite ends of a diameter of the rotonda. Suppose the coordinates of these points are 𝐴(2, 3) and 𝐵(8, 7). How to determine the radius of the rotonda?','First, use the distance formula √((x₂ − x₁)² + (y₂ − y₁)²) to get the diameter. Then, half the diameter gives a radius of 13 units.','First, use the distance formula √((x₂ − x₁)² + (y₂ − y₁)²) to get the diameter. Then, half the diameter gives a radius of √13 units.','First, use ((x₁ + x₂)/2, (y₁ + y₂)/2) to get the diameter. Then, half the diameter gives a radius of 10 units.','First, use √((x₂ + x₁)² + (y₂ + y₁)²) to get the diameter. Then, half the diameter gives a radius of 10√2 units.','B','Diameter = √((8−2)² + (7−3)²) = √52 = 2√13. Radius = √13 units.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,70,NULL,'Maliwanag National High School conducts a yearly entrance examination for incoming grade 7 students. Teacher Mara has been asked to report the distribution of test scores of 20 takers, as shown below: 48 49 50 44 55 56 42 65 59 42 74 46 81 55 76 68 32 44 68 58 Teacher Mara is advised to present the scores using a frequency distribution table; however, she is unfamiliar with it. Which of the following best describes the purpose of a frequency distribution table?','To display the raw data in a list format','To summarize the data by showing how often each value or group of values occurs.','To calculate the mean, median, and mode of the data','To represent the data graphically in a histogram','B','That’s what frequency tables do',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,71,'Leah sells banana cue for 7 days. Number sold: Monday 4, Tuesday 5, Wednesday 5, Thursday 6, Friday 7, Saturday 8, Sunday 50.','To find the mean sales, which of the following formulas should be used?','(highest number of banana cues + lowest number of banana cues) ÷ 2','(frequency)(class mark)','sum of all banana cues sold ÷ number of days','middle value of the data set','C','The mean is the sum of all values divided by the number of values.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,72,NULL,'Teacher Geraldine recorded the scores of 9 students on a quiz: NAME SCORE Lanie 56 Julius 62 May 68 Sweet 70 Marie 72 Nicole 75 Marky 78 Leony 80 Jenny 85 Teacher Geraldine wants to find the measures of position of the scores. Which of the following teacher Geraldine will not find?','Quartile','Percentile','Decile','Mean','D','Mean is not a position measure (quartile, percentile, decile are)',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,73,NULL,'A manager of pater store recorded the number of sales made by 5 employees in a week: 12, 15, 13, 10, 20. The manager wants to compute measures of variability of the sales. Which of the following would the manager compute?','Mean, Median, Mode','Range, Variance, Standard Deviation','Quartiles, Percentiles, Deciles','Z-score, Percentile Rank, Interquartile Range','B','These are variability measures',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,74,NULL,'Every morning around 3:00 – 5:00 PM, Mrs. Mabuti sells affordable homemade snacks. Each serving contains food and drink. Food consists of suman and kutsinta while drinks consist of kalamansi juice, sikwati, and coffee. To determine the number of possible snack combinations, the Fundamental Counting principle should be used. What is fundamental counting principle?','The average of a set of numbers','The probability of a single event occurring','The greatest common factor of two numbers','The number of ways two or more events can occur together','D','That’s the fundamental counting principle',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',1,3,75,NULL,'Mario throws a die while Maria flips a coin. And, Marianne, their friend, wants to do both: throwing a die and flipping a coin simultaneously. Who does/do compound event?','Mario','Marianne','Maria','Mario and Maria','C','She’s doing both events (compound event) ______________________END OF LEVEL 1______________________________ .',NULL,0,1),
