('JHS','LS3',2,2,32,NULL,'The endpoints of a line segment are E (–3, 5) and F (1, –1). What is the length and midpoint of the segment EF?','Length: √52 units, Midpoint: (–1, 2)','Length: √40 units, Midpoint: (–1, 2)','Length: √20 units, Midpoint: (–2, 1)','Length: √52, Midpoint: (–2, 1)','A','',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,33,NULL,'Find the equation of the line that passes through points A (–2, 3) and B (4, –1). $ # $','y = −(2/3)x + 5/3','y = −(3/2)x + 5/2','y = −(2/3)x + 7/3','y = −(2/3)x + 1','A','Slope = (−1 − 3) ÷ (4 − (−2)) = −4/6 = −2/3. Using A: y − 3 = −(2/3)(x + 2), so y = −(2/3)x + 5/3.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,34,NULL,'Find the equation of a line with slope of 2 that passes through the point (3, –4).','y=2x−10','y=2x−4','y=2x+10','y=2x+2','A','',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,35,NULL,'Find the equation of the line with x-intercept at 6 and y-intercept at –3.','y = (1/2)x − 3','y = −(1/2)x + 6','y = −(1/2)x + 3','y = (1/2)x − 6','A','Slope = (0 − (−3)) ÷ (6 − 0) = 3/6 = 1/2, and the y-intercept is −3, so y = (1/2)x − 3.',NULL,0,1),
