('JHS','LS3',2,2,40,NULL,'In a parallelogram ABCD, diagonal AC intersects diagonal BD at point E. Which of the following statements is true?','AE = EC and BE = ED','AE ≠ EC and BE = ED','AE = EC but BE ≠ ED','AE > EC and BE < ED','A','Diagonals of a parallelogram bisect each other.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,41,NULL,'In parallelogram PQRS, angle P = 65°. What is the measure of angle R?','65°','115°','90°','120°','B','Opposite angles in a parallelogram are equal, adjacent angles are supplementary (180° - 65°).',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,42,NULL,'The diagonals of a rhombus measure 10 cm and 24 cm. What is the area of the rhombus?','120 cm²','240 cm²','60 cm²','100 cm²','A','Area of a rhombus = (1/2) × d₁ × d₂ = (1/2) × 10 × 24 = 120 cm²',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,43,NULL,'Which of the following statements is true for a square but not necessarily for a rhombus?','All sides are equal','All angles are right angles','Diagonals are perpendicular','Diagonals bisect each other at 90°','B','Only a square guarantees all angles are 90°, unlike a rhombus.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,44,NULL,'In a parallelogram, one side is 18 cm, and its opposite side is unknown. What is the measure of the opposite side?','36 cm','18 cm','9 cm','Cannot be determined','B','Opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,45,NULL,'A square pyramid has a base side of 6 cm and a height of 10 cm. What is its volume?','120 cm³','240 cm³','360 cm³','180 cm³','A','Volume of a square pyramid = (1/3) × base area × height = (1/3) × 36 × 10 = 120 cm³',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,46,NULL,'A cone has a radius of 4 cm and a height of 9 cm. What is its volume? (Use π=3.14)','150.72 cm³','301.44 cm³','452.16 cm³','113.04 cm³','A','Volume of a cone = (1/3)πr²h = (1/3) × 3.14 × 16 × 9 = 150.72 cm³',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,47,NULL,'What is the volume of a sphere with radius 5 cm? (Use π=3.14)','523.33 cm³','392.5 cm³','314 cm³','261.67 cm³','A','V = (4/3)πr³ = (4/3)(3.14)(5³) = (4/3)(3.14)(125) ≈ 523.33 cm³.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,48,NULL,'In an isosceles triangle, the two equal sides measure 10 cm each, and the angle between them is 90°. What is the length of the base?','10 cm','10√2 𝑐𝑚','5√2 𝑐𝑚','14 cm','B','Use the law of cosines or recognize it''s an isosceles right triangle.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,49,NULL,'In a triangle, a perpendicular bisector is drawn to the base, forming a right angle with it. If the bisector splits the base into two 6 cm segments and the height is 8 cm, what is the length of the equal sides of the triangle?','10 cm','6√2 𝑐𝑚','8 cm','12 cm','A','Use Pythagorean Theorem: 62 + 82 = 10√6$ + 8$ = 1062 + 82 =',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,2,50,NULL,'In triangle ABC, DE is the midline connecting the midpoints of sides AB and AC. If BC = 10 cm, what is the length of DE? Can Pythagorean Theorem be used in triangle ADE?','5 cm, Yes','10 cm, No','5 cm, No','10 cm, Yes','A','Midline is half of the base; triangle ADE is right by construction',NULL,0,1);
