('JHS','LS3',2,3,51,NULL,'Finding a Height Using Tangent A ladder leans against a wall and makes a 60° angle with the ground. If the ladder is 10 meters long, how high up the wall does it reach?','5 m','8.7 m','10 m','6 m','B','ℎ = 10𝑠𝑖 𝑛 6 0° ≈ 8.66ℎ = 10 sin 6 0° ≈ 8.66ℎ = 10𝑠𝑖𝑛60° ≈ 8.66',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,52,NULL,'A guy wire is attached from the ground to the top of a 12-meter pole. The wire makes a 30° angle with the ground. How long is the wire?','6 m','13.9 m','24 m','10.4 m','C','The pole is opposite the 30° angle and the wire is the hypotenuse: sin 30° = 12 ÷ wire, so wire = 12 ÷ 0.5 = 24 m.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,53,NULL,'A 1.5-meter-tall student sees the top of a flagpole at an angle of elevation of 40°. The student is standing 20 meters from the base of the pole. How tall is the flagpole?','16.8 m','17.3 m','21.8 m','23.3 m','C','𝑡𝑎 𝑛(40°) = ℎ − 1.520 → ℎ ≈ 21.8 tan(40°) = $'' → ℎ ≈ 21.8𝑡𝑎𝑛(40°) = 20ℎ − 1.5 → ℎ ≈ 21.8m',NULL,0,0),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,54,NULL,'A ramp is 5 meters long and rises vertically 2 meters. What is the angle of elevation of the ramp from the ground?','30.0°','23.6°','45.0°','60.0°','B','sin θ = 2/5 = 0.4, so θ ≈ 23.6°.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,55,NULL,'A circular garden has a path that goes exactly halfway around its edge, starting and ending at opposite points on the circle. A student says, “This path is a radius because it connects to the edge.” Why is the student’s statement incorrect?','A radius must go through the center of the circle, and the path doesn''t.','A radius connects any two points on the edge of the circle.','The path described is actually the entire circumference.','The path is a chord, and all chords are longer than a radius.','A','',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,56,NULL,'In a circle, a central angle measures 72°. What fraction of the circle''s area is occupied by the corresponding sector?','1/3','1/4','1/5','1/6','C','72°/360° = 1/572°/360° = 1/572°/360° = 1/5',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,57,NULL,'Karina jogs at the Iligan Medical College rotunda. She stops at the two points that represent opposite ends of a diameter of the rotunda. Suppose the coordinates of these points are 𝐴(2, 3) and 𝐵(8, 7). Find the equation of the circle that represents the rotunda.','(x − 6)² + (y − 4)² = 13','(x − 3)² + (y − 2)² = 13','(x − 5)² + (y − 5)² = 13','(x − 10)² + (y − 10)² = 13','C','The center is the midpoint of AB: ((2+8)/2, (3+7)/2) = (5, 5). The radius² is (8−5)² + (7−5)² = 9 + 4 = 13.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,58,NULL,'Which of the following sets of points correctly represent the vertices of a square on the Cartesian plane?','(1, 1), (1, 4), (4, 4), (4, 1)','(2, 2), (4, 4), (6, 2), (4, 0)','(0, 0), (2, 0), (2, 3), (0, 3)','(0, 0), (1, 2), (3, 3), (4, 1)','A','Forms a square: all sides equal, right angles',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,59,NULL,'What is the area of the triangle formed by the points A(2,3), B(6,3), and C(6,7) on the Cartesian plane?','8 square units','16 square units','12 square units','20 square units','A','Base = 4, Height = 2 → (1/2) × 4 × 4 =',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,60,NULL,'A school wants to survey students about A public health researcher gathers information about smoking trends by analyzing previously published data from national health databases. What type of data collection method is this?','Experiment','Survey','Secondary data collection','Observation','C','Researcher uses existing data.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,61,NULL,'A researcher wants to study the reading habits of high school students in a city. She randomly selects four schools from the city and surveys all students in those selected schools. What type of sampling technique is this?','Simple random sampling','Stratified sampling','Systematic sampling','Cluster sampling','D','Choosing whole groups (schools) at random and surveying everyone in them is cluster sampling.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,62,NULL,'In an experiment on the effect of exercise on heart rate, participants are asked to engage in a 10-minute exercise, during which their heart rate is measured at one-minute interval. What is the best method for organizing the data collected?','Organize the data into a frequency table','Create a scatter plot to show heart rate vs. time','Use a bar graph to display each participant''s heart rate','Use a line graph to compare the heart rate of all participants','D','Heart rate measured every minute over time is best shown with a line graph.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,63,NULL,'Maliwanag National High School conducts a yearly entrance examination for incoming grade 7 students. Teacher Mara is asked to report the distribution of test scores of 20 takers which are shown below: 48 49 50 44 55 56 42 65 59 42 74 46 81 55 76 68 32 44 68 58 Which of the following statements is INCORRECT about the data set of test scores from 20 takers?','The range is 49.','There are 20 test scores in the data.','The lowest score is 32 while the highest score is 81.','There are more takers getting score of 60 above than getting score below 60.','D','Only 6 scores are 60 or above (65, 74, 81, 76, 68, 68); 14 are below 60, so D is incorrect.',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,64,NULL,'Maliwanag National High School conducts a yearly entrance examination for incoming grade 7 students. Teacher Mara is asked to report the distribution of test scores of 20 takers which are shown below: 48 49 50 44 55 56 42 65 59 42 74 46 81 55 76 68 32 44 68 58 Teacher Mara presented the following frequency distribution table below. Is the table correct? Explain. Class Frequency Interval 32 – 41 2 42 – 51 8 52 – 61 5 62 – 71 3 72 – 81 3','Yes, it does follow the correct class interval.','No, the total number of frequencies is wrong.','Yes, the frequency is correct and indicated in the right class interval.','No, the frequencies of 62 – 71 and 72 – 81 class intervals are wrong.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,65,NULL,'Which of the following is an example of primary data?','Using census data from the government','Looking at historical records of rainfall data','Reviewing past research papers on climate change','Analyzing survey results that you collected from participants','D','Primary data = directly collected. Analyzing survey results that you collected from participants',NULL,0,1),
