('JHS','LS3',2,3,72,NULL,'Every morning around 3:00 – 5:00 PM, Mrs. Rubeneth sells affordable homemade snacks. Each serving contains food and drink. Food consists of suman and kutsinta while drinks consist of kalamansi juice, sikwati, and coffee. Which of the following is the sample space of choosing a set of snacks from Mrs. Rubeneth? A . {suman and kalamansi juice, suman and sikwati, suman and coffee, kutsinta and kalamansi juice, kutsinta and sikwati, kutsinta and coffee} B. {suman, kutsinta, kalamansi juice, sikwati, coffee} C. {kalamansi juice, sikwati, coffee} D. {suman, kutsinta}','{suman and kalamansi juice, suman and sikwati, suman and coffee, kutsinta and kalamansi juice, kutsinta and sikwati, kutsinta and coffee}','{suman, kutsinta, kalamansi juice, sikwati, coffee}','{kalamansi juice, sikwati, coffee}','{suman, kutsinta}','A','',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,73,NULL,'Every morning around 3:00 – 5:00 PM, Mrs. Mabuti sells affordable homemade snacks. Each serving contains food and drink. Food consists of suman and kutsinta while drinks consist of kalamansi juice, sikwati, and coffee. How many combinations of snacks can you choose when buying from Mrs. Mabuti?','5','2','3','6','D','2 foods × 3 drinks = 6 combinations',NULL,0,1),
('JHS','LS3',2,3,74,NULL,'Mario throws a die while Maria flips a coin. And, Marianne, their friend, wants to do both: throwing a die and flipping a coin simultaneously.','The number of times an event occurs divided by the number of possible outcomes','The difference between the most likely and least likely events','A measure of how certain we are that an event will occur','The total number of favorable outcome','C','Definition of probability',NULL,0,0),
